WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:00.800
E

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:13.713 line:78%
CASE OF U.S. VERSUS NIXON.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:24.724 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE'LL HEAR ARGUMENTS IN

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:25.759 line:78%
73-1766, UNITED STATES OF

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.893 line:78%
AMERICA AGAINST NIXON AND THE

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.527 line:78%
CROSS-PETITION, RICHARD M. NIXON

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.228 line:78%
AGAINST THE UNITED STATES.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.895 line:78%
MR. JAWORSKI, THERE HAS BEEN A

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:42.742 line:78%
REQUEST FOR ADDITIONAL TIME.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:43.877 line:78%
THE COURT THEN SET ADDITIONAL

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.277 line:78%
TIME OF ONE-AND-A HALF HOURS, I

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:44.944 line:78%
UNDERSTAND.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.779 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.946 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'LL BE ALLOWED TO EACH SIDE

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.580 line:78%
AND WE WILL NOT INTERRUPT THE

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.348 line:78%
ARGUMENT WITH ANY RECESS.

00:00:47.681 --> 00:00:48.882 line:78%
WE'LL GO RIGHT THROUGH UNTIL

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.816 line:78%
YOU'RE FINISHED.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.483 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU, SIR.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.217 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU MAY PROCEED WHENEVER

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.951 line:78%
YOU'RE READY, MR. JAWORSKI.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.952 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. CHIEF JUSTICE AND MAY IT

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.653 line:78%
PLEASE THE COURT.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.354 line:78%
ON MARCH 1 LAST, UNITED STATES

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.755 line:78%
DISTRICT COURT GRAND JURY, SET

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.756 line:78%
IT HERE, RETURNED AN INDICTMENT

00:00:55.855 --> 00:01:01.961 line:78%
AGAINST SEVEN DEFENDANTS

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:08.868 line:78%
CHARGING VARIOUS OFFENSES

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:09.869 line:78%
INCLUDING AMONG THEM A

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.804 line:78%
CONSPIRACY TO DEFRAUD THE UNITED

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:20.847 line:78%
STATES AND ALSO TO OBSTRUCT

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:21.915 line:78%
JUSTICE.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.949 line:78%
JOHN MITCHELL, ONE OF THE

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:36.996 line:78%
DEFENDANTS, WAS A FORMER

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:37.964 line:78%
ATTORNEY GENERAL OF THE UNITED

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:39.099 line:78%
STATES AND ALSO CHAIRMAN OF THE

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.466 line:78%
COMMITTEE TO REELECT THE

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.200 line:78%
PRESIDENT.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.001 line:78%
ANOTHER, H.R. HALDEMAN, WAS THE

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.002 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S CHIEF OF STAFF.

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.969 line:78%
ANOTHER, JOHN EHRLICHMAN, WAS

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.938 line:78%
ASSISTANT TO THE PRESIDENT FOR

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:50.176 line:78%
ECONOMIC -- FOR DOMESTIC

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:51.011 line:78%
AFFAIRS.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.045 line:78%
THE OTHERS WERE EITHER ON THE

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.046 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S STAFF OR HELD

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.048 line:78%
RESPONSIBLE POSITIONS ON THE

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:56.082 line:78%
REELECTION COMMITTEE.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.050 line:78%
IN THE COURSE OF ITS

00:01:56.182 --> 00:02:01.054 line:78%
DELIBERATIONS, THE GRAND JURY

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:03.056 line:78%
VOTED UNANIMOUSLY WITH 19

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:04.124 line:78%
MEMBERS CONCURRING THAT THE

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.125 line:78%
COURSE OF EVENTS IN THE

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:08.194 line:78%
FORMATION AND CONTINUATION OF

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:12.198 line:78%
THE CONSPIRACY WAS SUCH THAT

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:13.199 line:78%
PRESIDENT NIXON, AMONG A NUMBER

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:17.237 line:78%
OF OTHERS, SHOULD BE IDENTIFIED

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:18.238 line:78%
AS AN UNINDICTED CO-CONSPIRATOR

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:20.206 line:78%
IN THE BILL, PARTICULAR AS TO BE

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:25.245 line:78%
FILED IN CONNECTION WITH THE

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:27.247 line:78%
PRETRIAL PROCEEDINGS.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:29.249 line:78%
NOW, ALTHOUGH THIS PARTICULAR

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:30.250 line:78%
DECISION AND DETERMINATION ON

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:32.252 line:78%
THE PART OF THE GRAND JURY

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:34.187 line:78%
OCCURRED IN FEBRUARY, IT WAS A

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:36.256 line:78%
WELL-KEPT SECRET FOR TWO-AND-A

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:41.161 line:78%
HALF MONTHS.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:42.228 line:78%
THE GRAND JURY, OF COURSE, KNEW

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:44.197 line:78%
IT.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:47.233 line:78%
THE MEMBERS OF THE PROSECUTION

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:50.337 line:78%
STAFF KNEW IT.

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:57.310 line:78%
IT WAS DONE SO TO AVOID

00:02:50.437 --> 00:02:59.312 line:78%
AFFECTING THE PROCEEDINGS IN A

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.314 line:78%
HOUSE JUDICIARY COMMITTEE.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:05.352 line:78%
IT WAS SO KEPT DURING THESE

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:09.356 line:78%
TWO-AND-A HALF MONTHS UNTIL IT

00:03:05.452 --> 00:03:12.359 line:78%
BECAME NECESSARY TO REVEAL IT AS

00:03:09.456 --> 00:03:15.395 line:78%
A RESULT OF THE PRESIDENT'S

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:17.297 line:78%
MOTION TO QUASH A SUBPOENA, AS I

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:19.366 line:78%
WILL INDICATE SUBSEQUENTLY IN MY

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:20.367 line:78%
ARGUMENT.

00:03:19.466 --> 00:03:21.368 line:78%
NOW, TO OBTAIN ADDITION EVIDENCE

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.402 line:78%
WHICH THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR HAS

00:03:21.468 --> 00:03:23.370 line:78%
GOOD REASON TO BELIEVE IS IN THE

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.404 line:78%
POSSESSION OF AND UNDER THE

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.605 line:78%
CONTROL OF THE PRESIDENT AND

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.272 line:78%
WHICH IT IS BELIEVED BY THE

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:28.475 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR AS QUITE

00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:29.542 line:78%
IMPORTANT TO THE DEVELOPMENT OF

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.478 line:78%
THE GOVERNMENT'S PROOF AT THE

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:33.546 line:78%
TRIAL IN UNITED STATES VERSUS

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:35.515 line:78%
MITCHELL.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:37.517 line:78%
A SPECIAL PROSECUTOR, ON BEHALF

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:39.519 line:78%
OF THE UNITED STATES, MOVED FOR

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:41.454 line:78%
A SUBPOENA DUCES TECUM.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.522 line:78%
AND, IT IS THE SUBPOENA HERE IN

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:46.526 line:78%
QUESTION.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:48.561 line:78%
THE DISTRICT COURT ORDERED THE

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:49.629 line:78%
SUBPOENA TO ISSUE RETURNABLE ON

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:52.732 line:78%
MAY 2 AND THE SUBPOENA, OF

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:53.733 line:78%
COURSE, CALLED FOR THE

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.669 line:78%
PRODUCTION OF TAPE RECORDINGS IN

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:59.706 line:78%
ADVANCE OF SEPTEMBER 9, 1972

00:03:55.769 --> 00:04:02.709 line:78%
WHICH IS A TRIAL DATE.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:04.744 line:78%
AND, THIS WAS DONE TO ALLOW TIME

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.745 line:78%
FOR LITIGATION IN THE EVENT

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:11.718 line:78%
LITIGATION WAS TO ENSUE OVER THE

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:12.952 line:78%
PRODUCTION OF THE TAPES AND ALSO

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:13.586 line:78%
FOR TRANSCRIPTION AND

00:04:13.053 --> 00:04:14.320 line:78%
AUTHENTICATION OF ANY TAPE

00:04:13.687 --> 00:04:23.997 line:78%
RECORDINGS THAT WERE PRODUCED IN

00:04:14.421 --> 00:04:24.831 line:78%
RESPONSE TO THE SUBPOENA.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:32.872 line:78%
ON APRIL 30, THE PRESIDENT

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:33.873 line:78%
RELEASED TO THE PUBLIC AND

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.908 line:78%
SUBMITTED TO THE HOUSE JUDICIARY

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.909 line:78%
COMMITTEE 1,216 PAGES OF EDITED

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.943 line:78%
TRANSCRIPTS OF 43 CONVERSATIONS

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:42.215 line:78%
DEALING WITH WATERGATE.

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:42.882 line:78%
PORTIONS OF 20 OF THE SUBPOENAED

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:57.130 line:78%
CONVERSATIONS WERE INCLUDED

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:57.998 line:78%
AMONG THE 43.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.999 line:78%
THEN, ON MAY 1, THE PRESIDENT

00:04:58.098 --> 00:05:00.000 line:78%
ADVISED COUNSEL TO FILE A

00:04:59.099 --> 00:05:05.972 line:78%
SPECIAL APPEARANCE, A FORMAL

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:06.973 line:78%
CLAIM OF PRIVILEGE, AND A MOTION

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:08.008 line:78%
TO QUASH A SUBPOENA.

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:10.010 line:78%
NOW FOR THE UNITED STATES TO

00:05:08.108 --> 00:05:11.044 line:78%
CONDUCT A FULL AND APPROPRIATE

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:20.120 line:78%
HEARING ON A MOTION TO QUASH THE

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:21.121 line:78%
SUBPOENA, IT BECAME NECESSARY TO

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.122 line:78%
REVEAL THE GRAND JURY'S FINDING

00:05:21.221 --> 00:05:25.191 line:78%
REGARDING THE PRESIDENT.

00:05:22.222 --> 00:05:26.192 line:78%
AND, THIS WAS FIRST DONE BY THE

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:32.232 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR CALLING ON

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:33.266 line:78%
THE CHIEF OF STAFF, GENERAL

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:34.234 line:78%
ALEXANDER HAIG, AND THE

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:36.336 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S COUNSEL, MR. ST.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:44.444 line:78%
CLAIRE, AND ADVISING THEM OF

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:47.480 line:78%
WHAT HAD OCCURRED TWO-AND-A HALF

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:48.515 line:78%
MONTHS PRIOR.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.482 line:78%
AND THEN, ON THE FOLLOWING

00:05:48.615 --> 00:05:50.517 line:78%
MORNING, ADVISING JUDGE RICO OF

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.551 line:78%
WHAT HAD OCCURRED IN CAMERA AND

00:05:50.617 --> 00:05:53.453 line:78%
POINTING OUT AT THE NECESSITY OF

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:54.521 line:78%
THIS BEING USED IN CONNECTION

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.588 line:78%
WITH THE ARGUMENTS ON A MOTION

00:05:54.621 --> 00:05:59.592 line:78%
TO QUASH BECAUSE OF THEIR

00:05:55.689 --> 00:06:04.564 line:78%
RELEVANCE AND THE NECESSITY OF

00:05:59.693 --> 00:06:05.598 line:78%
THESE MATTERS BEING MADE A PART

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:06.800 line:78%
OF THE PROCEEDING.

00:06:05.699 --> 00:06:07.534 line:78%
NOW, THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.234 line:78%
JOINED COUNSEL FOR THE PRESIDENT

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:08.902 line:78%
IN URGING THAT MATTER BE HEARD

00:06:08.335 --> 00:06:09.636 line:78%
IN CAMERA, WHICH, WAS DONE.

00:06:09.002 --> 00:06:10.637 line:78%
THREE OF THE DEFENDANTS HAD

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:16.710 line:78%
JOINED THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR IN

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:17.744 line:78%
MOVING FOR THE SUBPOENA.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:22.749 line:78%
ALL OF THE DEFENDANTS, AT THE

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:23.683 line:78%
TIME OF ARGUMENT IN CAMERA TO

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:28.755 line:78%
JUDGE SIRICA, OPPOSED THE MOTION

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:29.756 line:78%
TO QUASH.

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:30.724 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I DON'T SEE THE RELEVANCY OF

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:37.797 line:78%
THE FACT THAT THE GRAND JURY

00:06:30.824 --> 00:06:38.898 line:78%
INDICTED THE PRESIDENT AS

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:39.899 line:78%
CO-CONSPIRATOR.

00:06:38.999 --> 00:06:40.967 line:78%
THE LEGAL ISSUE, AS TO THE DUTY

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.838 line:78%
TO DELIVER PURSUANT TO THE

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:46.906 line:78%
SUBPOENA THAT YOU ARE ASKING FOR

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:47.907 line:78%
--

00:06:47.007 --> 00:06:49.976 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE ONLY RELEVANCE, MR.

00:06:48.008 --> 00:06:51.978 line:78%
JUSTICE, LIES IN IT BEING

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:52.979 line:78%
NECESSARY TO SHOW UNDER RULE 17C

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:56.049 line:78%
THAT THERE IS SOME RELEVANCE TO

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:58.051 line:78%
THE MATERIAL THAT WE WERE

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:59.085 line:78%
SEEKING TO SUBPOENA, AND --

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:01.087 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, BUT 17C PRESUPPOSES A

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:02.989 line:78%
SUBPOENA RUNNING AGAINST THE

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:19.105 line:78%
PARTY, AND THE PRESIDENT IS NO

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:20.073 line:78%
PARTY.

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:21.174 line:78%
HE'S NOT A DEFENDANT IN ONE OF

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:22.175 line:78%
THESE CASES.

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:28.181 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR, BUT IT

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:29.249 line:78%
WAS FELT IT WOULD BE NECESSARY

00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:30.250 line:78%
TO SHOW WHY.

00:07:29.349 --> 00:07:31.251 line:78%
AND, IN ORDER TO PROVE THIS

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.419 line:78%
CONSPIRACY AND IN ORDER TO

00:07:31.351 --> 00:07:33.053 line:78%
PROVIDE ALL OF THE LINKS IN THE

00:07:32.519 --> 00:07:33.687 line:78%
CONSPIRACY, IT WAS DEEMED

00:07:33.153 --> 00:07:34.320 line:78%
NECESSARY TO SHOW THAT THE

00:07:33.787 --> 00:07:35.455 line:78%
PRESIDENT OR HIS NAME WAS

00:07:34.421 --> 00:07:36.122 line:78%
INDICTED CO-CONSPIRATOR AND ALSO

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:36.856 line:78%
THAT THERE'S PRUDENCE.

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:37.590 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THOUGHT THAT WAS PRIMARILY

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:38.358 line:78%
JUST FOR THE COLLAGE INFORMATION

00:07:37.691 --> 00:07:38.725 line:78%
OF THE HOUSE JUDICIARY

00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:39.325 line:78%
COMMITTEE.

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:40.527 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR.

00:07:39.426 --> 00:07:41.227 line:78%
THAT IS NOT CORRECT, SIR.

00:07:40.627 --> 00:07:41.961 line:78%
IT BECAME VERY IMPORTANT, MR.

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:42.696 line:78%
JUSTICE, FOR US TO HAVE THAT AS

00:07:42.062 --> 00:07:43.430 line:78%
A PART OF PROCEEDINGS SO THAT WE

00:07:42.796 --> 00:07:44.597 line:78%
COULD USE THE VARIOUS LINKS IN

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:45.332 line:78%
THE TESTIMONY, SO AS TO SHOW

00:07:44.698 --> 00:07:53.473 line:78%
THAT THE CONVERSATIONS WERE SUCH

00:07:45.432 --> 00:07:55.475 line:78%
AS TO MAKE ONE ADMISSIBLE AS

00:07:53.573 --> 00:08:00.680 line:78%
AGAINST A CO-CONSPIRATOR.

00:07:55.575 --> 00:08:02.549 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE GRAND JURY SENT IT TO THE

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.550 line:78%
HOUSE COMMITTEE, DIDN'T IT?

00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:04.517 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE GRAND JURY SENT NOTHING

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:05.685 line:78%
OF AN ACCUSATORY NATURE TO THE

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:06.353 line:78%
HOUSE COMMITTEE.

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:07.587 line:78%
NO, SIR, WHAT THE GRAND JURY

00:08:06.453 --> 00:08:19.599 line:78%
SENT TO THE HOUSE COMMITTEE WAS

00:08:07.687 --> 00:08:20.633 line:78%
THE EVIDENCE THAT HAD BEEN

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:21.634 line:78%
ACCUMULATED AND IT, VERY

00:08:20.734 --> 00:08:23.670 line:78%
CAREFULLY, EXCISED FROM IT

00:08:21.735 --> 00:08:24.671 line:78%
ANYTHING BY WAY OF THE GRAND

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.605 line:78%
JURY'S INTERPRETATION OR

00:08:24.771 --> 00:08:26.673 line:78%
ANYTHING ALONG THAT LINE, MR.

00:08:25.705 --> 00:08:27.674 line:78%
JUSTICE.

00:08:26.773 --> 00:08:28.575 line:78%
NOW, IN ITS OPINION AND ORDER OF

00:08:27.774 --> 00:08:29.676 line:78%
MAY 20, THE DISTRICT COURT FIRST

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:33.680 line:78%
--

00:08:29.776 --> 00:08:34.681 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU'D STILL BE HERE, MR.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.682 line:78%
JAWORSKI, WHETHER OR NOT THE

00:08:34.781 --> 00:08:36.683 line:78%
PRESIDENT HAD BEEN NAMED AS AN

00:08:35.782 --> 00:08:37.650 line:78%
UNINDICTED CO-CONSPIRATOR BUT

00:08:36.783 --> 00:08:38.718 line:78%
THAT SIMPLY GIVES YOU ANOTHER

00:08:37.751 --> 00:08:39.753 line:78%
STRING TO YOUR BOW.

00:08:38.818 --> 00:08:40.754 line:78%
ISN'T THAT ABOUT IT?

00:08:39.853 --> 00:08:41.721 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S TRUE THAT IT ADMITS SOME

00:08:40.854 --> 00:08:42.922 line:78%
EVIDENCE THAT WOULD OTHERWISE

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:43.556 line:78%
NOT BE ADMISSIBLE.

00:08:43.023 --> 00:08:44.257 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT, BUT EVEN HAD THE

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:44.924 line:78%
PRESIDENT NOT BEEN NAMED, YOU

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:45.925 line:78%
WOULD STILL HAVE SUBPOENA AT

00:08:45.025 --> 00:08:46.693 line:78%
LEAST PART OF THIS MATERIAL.

00:08:46.026 --> 00:08:47.160 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THERE'S NO QUESTION ABOUT

00:08:46.793 --> 00:08:47.894 line:78%
THAT, YES, SIR.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:48.528 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND YOU'D STILL BE HERE.

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:49.029 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT, SIR.

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:49.796 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WOULD YOU NOT?

00:08:49.129 --> 00:08:50.964 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT, SIR.

00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:51.631 line:78%
BUT, IN ORDER TO PRESENT THE

00:08:51.064 --> 00:08:52.365 line:78%
FULL PICTURE AND IN ORDER TO

00:08:51.731 --> 00:08:52.832 line:78%
PRESENT, THAT ALSO WAS A PART OF

00:08:52.465 --> 00:08:53.767 line:78%
IT.

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:54.801 line:78%
DISTRICT COURT DENIED THE MOTION

00:08:53.867 --> 00:08:55.802 line:78%
TO QUASH AND THE MOTION TO

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.803 line:78%
EXPUNGE HAD ALSO BEEN FILED.

00:08:55.902 --> 00:08:57.837 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO ONE YET HAS EVER SUGGESTED

00:08:56.903 --> 00:08:59.839 line:78%
THAT IF YOU'RE IN A CRIMINAL

00:08:57.937 --> 00:09:00.874 line:78%
TRIAL, CONSPIRACY TRIAL, AND

00:08:59.939 --> 00:09:06.913 line:78%
SOME EVIDENCE IS AUTHORED OF AN

00:09:00.974 --> 00:09:07.947 line:78%
OUT-OF-COURT STATEMENT OF

00:09:07.013 --> 00:09:08.915 line:78%
SOMEONE WHO'S ALLEGED TO BE A

00:09:08.048 --> 00:09:14.154 line:78%
CO-CONSPIRATOR, THAT IT'S ENOUGH

00:09:09.015 --> 00:09:16.956 line:78%
FOR THE PROSECUTION TO THEN SHOW

00:09:14.254 --> 00:09:18.958 line:78%
THAT THE GRAND JURY HAD NAMED

00:09:17.057 --> 00:09:21.061 line:78%
HIM THE CO-CONSPIRATOR.

00:09:19.059 --> 00:09:23.029 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO.

00:09:21.161 --> 00:09:24.064 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT NEVER GETS YOU OR WILL

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:25.165 line:78%
NEVER GET YOU OVER THE --

00:09:24.164 --> 00:09:25.799 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, AND WE DON'T SO CONTEND.

00:09:25.265 --> 00:09:26.099 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THEN THAT WAS THE

00:09:25.899 --> 00:09:27.033 line:78%
POINT.

00:09:26.199 --> 00:09:28.168 line:78%
THAT WAS THE DIRECTION OF YOUR

00:09:28.034 --> 00:09:30.203 line:78%
--

00:09:28.268 --> 00:09:31.204 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, THIS WAS IN CONNECTION

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:32.238 line:78%
WITH THE SUBPOENAING OF THIS

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:34.207 line:78%
EVIDENCE, MR. JUSTICE.

00:09:32.339 --> 00:09:35.241 line:78%
IN OTHER WORDS, THIS WAS IN

00:09:34.307 --> 00:09:38.211 line:78%
CONNECTION WITH SHOWING THAT WE

00:09:35.342 --> 00:09:39.179 line:78%
HAD THE RIGHT TO THIS EVIDENCE.

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:41.314 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I UNDERSTAND THAT.

00:09:39.279 --> 00:09:41.681 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

00:09:41.414 --> 00:09:42.315 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT --

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:44.217 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THAT WAS THE POINT.

00:09:42.415 --> 00:09:46.152 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT YOU DO NOT SUGGEST THAT

00:09:44.317 --> 00:09:47.220 line:78%
THAT'S ALL YOU NEED TO SHOW.

00:09:46.252 --> 00:09:48.254 line:78%
IS THAT IT?

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.255 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR, OF COURSE NOT.

00:09:48.355 --> 00:09:50.156 line:78%
&gt;&gt; OR YOU DON'T SUGGEST THAT THE

00:09:49.356 --> 00:09:52.258 line:78%
GRAND JURY FINDING IS BINDING ON

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:54.227 line:78%
THE COURT OR NOT?

00:09:52.359 --> 00:09:56.229 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I DO SUGGEST THAT IT MAKES A

00:09:54.327 --> 00:09:58.264 line:78%
PRIMA FACIE CASE.

00:09:56.329 --> 00:10:00.300 line:78%
AND I THINK, UNDER THE

00:09:58.365 --> 00:10:03.236 line:78%
AUTHORITIES, IT SO DOES.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:05.305 line:78%
&gt;&gt; LET ME UNDERSTAND THIS, MR.

00:10:03.336 --> 00:10:08.308 line:78%
JAWORSKI.

00:10:05.405 --> 00:10:11.311 line:78%
YOU DON'T SUGGEST THAT YOUR

00:10:08.408 --> 00:10:12.278 line:78%
RIGHT TO THIS EVIDENCE DEPENDS

00:10:11.411 --> 00:10:13.246 line:78%
UPON THE PRESIDENT HAVING THE

00:10:12.379 --> 00:10:15.215 line:78%
NAME AS AN UNINDICTED

00:10:13.346 --> 00:10:26.326 line:78%
CO-CONSPIRATOR.

00:10:15.315 --> 00:10:27.327 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR.

00:10:26.426 --> 00:10:28.328 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND SO, FOR THE PURPOSES OF

00:10:27.427 --> 00:10:29.529 line:78%
OUR DECISION, WE COULD LAY THAT

00:10:28.428 --> 00:10:30.230 line:78%
FACT ASIDE, COULDN'T WE?

00:10:29.629 --> 00:10:30.764 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHAT I WAS REALLY DOING IN

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:31.331 line:78%
POINTING TO THAT --

00:10:30.864 --> 00:10:32.432 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, COULD WE?

00:10:31.431 --> 00:10:33.433 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES.

00:10:32.532 --> 00:10:34.534 line:78%
PRIMARILY WAS AN ORDER TO SHOW A

00:10:33.533 --> 00:10:34.868 line:78%
REASON FOR THE GRAND JURY'S

00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:36.636 line:78%
ACTION.

00:10:34.968 --> 00:10:37.337 line:78%
THERE IS ALSO BEFORE THIS COURT

00:10:36.736 --> 00:10:38.004 line:78%
A MOTION TO EXPUNGE THE ACT OF

00:10:37.437 --> 00:10:38.638 line:78%
THE GRAND JURY IN NAMING THE

00:10:38.104 --> 00:10:39.472 line:78%
PRESIDENT AS AN UNINDICTED

00:10:38.738 --> 00:10:40.507 line:78%
CO-CONSPIRATOR.

00:10:39.572 --> 00:10:41.508 line:78%
AND, I WAS TRYING TO LAY BEFORE

00:10:40.607 --> 00:10:42.475 line:78%
THE COURT THE ENTIRE SITUATION

00:10:41.608 --> 00:10:43.443 line:78%
THAT WARRANTED THAT ACTION.

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:45.545 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. JAWORSKI.

00:10:43.543 --> 00:10:46.546 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:48.515 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AS I UNDERSTAND YOUR BRIEF,

00:10:46.646 --> 00:10:50.550 line:78%
YOU GO BEYOND WHAT YOU HAVE

00:10:48.615 --> 00:10:51.551 line:78%
ADDRESSED SO FAR.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:52.585 line:78%
I THINK YOU SAY THAT THE MERE

00:10:51.651 --> 00:10:53.586 line:78%
FACT THAT THE PRESIDENT WAS

00:10:52.686 --> 00:10:54.587 line:78%
NAMED AS AN UNINDICTED

00:10:53.687 --> 00:11:00.694 line:78%
CO-CONSPIRATOR FORECLOSES HIS

00:10:54.688 --> 00:11:01.695 line:78%
CLAIM OF PRIVILEGE.

00:11:00.794 --> 00:11:03.596 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, WE CERTAINLY POINT --

00:11:01.795 --> 00:11:05.732 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S IN PAGE 91 OF YOUR

00:11:03.697 --> 00:11:06.633 line:78%
BRIEF.

00:11:05.832 --> 00:11:07.701 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE CERTAINLY MAKE THAT AS ONE

00:11:06.733 --> 00:11:10.737 line:78%
OF THE POINTS, WHICH, I INTEND

00:11:07.801 --> 00:11:11.738 line:78%
TO DISCUSS THAT LATER.

00:11:10.837 --> 00:11:12.739 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THAT REDUCES HIM, IN IT

00:11:11.838 --> 00:11:13.773 line:78%
OF ITSELF, TO THE STATUS OF ANY

00:11:12.839 --> 00:11:14.674 line:78%
OTHER PERSON ACCUSED OF CRIME.

00:11:13.873 --> 00:11:21.748 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I DON'T SAY THAT IT FORECLOSE

00:11:14.774 --> 00:11:22.749 line:78%
THIS.

00:11:21.848 --> 00:11:24.684 line:78%
WHAT I THINK WE SUGGEST IS THAT

00:11:22.849 --> 00:11:26.786 line:78%
IT DOES PRESENT A SITUATION

00:11:24.784 --> 00:11:27.787 line:78%
HERE.

00:11:26.886 --> 00:11:29.789 line:78%
THAT SHOULD NOT MAKE THE

00:11:27.887 --> 00:11:31.758 line:78%
APPLICATION OF EXECUTIVE

00:11:29.889 --> 00:11:32.826 line:78%
PRIVILEGE APPROPRIATE.

00:11:31.858 --> 00:11:36.896 line:78%
WE DO SAY THAT.

00:11:32.926 --> 00:11:37.897 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT ONLY PRIMA FACIE.

00:11:36.996 --> 00:11:38.932 line:78%
&gt;&gt; PRIMA FACIE, THAT'S CORRECT.

00:11:37.998 --> 00:11:40.900 line:78%
BUT WHEN YOU GET TO THE MATTER,

00:11:39.032 --> 00:11:41.901 line:78%
MR. JUSTICE POWELL, OF BALANCING

00:11:41.001 --> 00:11:43.903 line:78%
INTERESTS WE DO FEEL THAT THAT

00:11:42.002 --> 00:11:46.039 line:78%
PARTICULAR SITUATION IS A FACTOR

00:11:44.004 --> 00:11:46.840 line:78%
THAT IS IMPORTANT.

00:11:46.139 --> 00:11:47.974 line:78%
AND, THIS IS WHY WE LAID STRESS

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:49.976 line:78%
ON IT.

00:11:48.074 --> 00:11:51.011 line:78%
THE COURT'S ORDER, OF COURSE,

00:11:50.076 --> 00:11:52.012 line:78%
WAS TO DELIVER TO THE COURT THE

00:11:51.111 --> 00:11:54.014 line:78%
ORIGINALS OF ALL SUBPOENAED

00:11:52.112 --> 00:11:55.015 line:78%
ITEMS AS WELL AS AN INDEX

00:11:54.114 --> 00:11:59.019 line:78%
ANALYSIS OF THOSE ITEMS,

00:11:55.115 --> 00:12:01.021 line:78%
TOGETHER WITH TAPED COPIES OF

00:11:59.119 --> 00:12:06.192 line:78%
THOSE PORTIONS OF THE SUBPOENA

00:12:01.121 --> 00:12:07.060 line:78%
RECORDINGS FOR WHICH TRANSCRIPTS

00:12:06.292 --> 00:12:08.028 line:78%
HAD BEEN RELEASED TO THE PUBLIC

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.062 line:78%
BY THE PRESIDENT ON APRIL 30.

00:12:08.128 --> 00:12:09.963 line:78%
NOW, THIS CASE PRESENTS FOR

00:12:09.162 --> 00:12:11.064 line:78%
REVIEW THE ACTION OF THE LOWER

00:12:10.063 --> 00:12:12.065 line:78%
COURT.

00:12:11.164 --> 00:12:13.066 line:78%
NOW MAY I, BEFORE I GET TO THE

00:12:12.165 --> 00:12:17.103 line:78%
JURISDICTIONAL POINTS, BRIEFLY

00:12:13.166 --> 00:12:24.077 line:78%
STATE WHAT WE CONSIDER TO BE A

00:12:17.203 --> 00:12:25.078 line:78%
BIRD'S EYE VIEW OF THIS CASE.

00:12:24.177 --> 00:12:26.112 line:78%
NOW INVEST IN ALMOST 500 PAGES

00:12:25.178 --> 00:12:27.047 line:78%
OF BRIEFS, WHEN BOILED DOWN,

00:12:26.212 --> 00:12:32.285 line:78%
THIS CASE REALLY PRESENTS ONE

00:12:27.147 --> 00:12:34.154 line:78%
FUNDAMENTAL ISSUE.

00:12:32.385 --> 00:12:35.188 line:78%
WHO IS TO BE THE ARBITER OF WHAT

00:12:34.254 --> 00:12:37.190 line:78%
THE CONSTITUTION SAYS?

00:12:35.288 --> 00:12:49.436 line:78%
BASICALLY, THIS IS NOT A NOVEL

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:50.470 line:78%
QUESTION, ALTHOUGH THE FACTUAL

00:12:49.536 --> 00:12:51.504 line:78%
SITUATION INVOLVED IS, OF

00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:52.605 line:78%
COURSE, UNPRECEDENTED.

00:12:51.604 --> 00:12:52.939 line:78%
THERE ARE PRIMARY QUESTIONS TO

00:12:52.706 --> 00:12:53.673 line:78%
BE SURE.

00:12:53.039 --> 00:12:54.574 line:78%
BUT IN THE END, AFTER THE ROUNDS

00:12:53.773 --> 00:12:55.709 line:78%
HAVE BEEN MADE, WE RETURN TO

00:12:54.674 --> 00:12:56.409 line:78%
FACE THESE FLARING FACTS THAT I

00:12:55.809 --> 00:13:03.616 line:78%
WANT TO BRIEFLY REVIEW FOR THE

00:12:56.509 --> 00:13:04.651 line:78%
FINAL ANSWER.

00:13:03.717 --> 00:13:06.686 line:78%
IN REFUSING TO PRODUCE THE

00:13:04.751 --> 00:13:07.687 line:78%
EVIDENCE SOUGHT BY A SUBPOENA

00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:08.688 line:78%
DUCES TECUM IN THE CRIMINAL

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:09.689 line:78%
TRIAL OF SEVEN DEFENDANTS, AMONG

00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:10.657 line:78%
THEM, FORMER CHIEF OF AIDS AND

00:13:09.789 --> 00:13:11.624 line:78%
DUBIETIES, THE PRESIDENT INVOKES

00:13:10.757 --> 00:13:12.692 line:78%
THE PROVISIONS OF THE

00:13:11.725 --> 00:13:13.693 line:78%
CONSTITUTION.

00:13:12.792 --> 00:13:14.728 line:78%
HIS COUNSEL'S BRIEF IS REPLETE

00:13:13.793 --> 00:13:17.664 line:78%
WITH REFERENCES FOR THE

00:13:14.828 --> 00:13:18.765 line:78%
CONSTITUTION AS JUSTIFYING HIS

00:13:17.764 --> 00:13:19.799 line:78%
POSITION.

00:13:18.865 --> 00:13:20.500 line:78%
AND IN HIS PUBLIC STATEMENT, AS

00:13:19.899 --> 00:13:21.334 line:78%
WE ALL KNOW, THE PRESIDENT HAS

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:22.002 line:78%
EMBRACED THE CONSTITUTION THAT'S

00:13:21.434 --> 00:13:22.736 line:78%
OFFERING HIM SUPPORT FOR HIS

00:13:22.102 --> 00:13:25.772 line:78%
REFUSAL TO SUPPLY THE SUBPOENAED

00:13:22.836 --> 00:13:26.740 line:78%
TAPES.

00:13:25.872 --> 00:13:27.707 line:78%
NOW, THE PRESIDENT MAY BE RIGHT

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.742 line:78%
IN HOW HE READS THE

00:13:27.807 --> 00:13:29.776 line:78%
CONSTITUTION.

00:13:28.842 --> 00:13:31.945 line:78%
BUT, HE MAY ALSO BE WRONG.

00:13:29.876 --> 00:13:32.412 line:78%
AND IF HE IS WRONG, WHO IS THERE

00:13:32.045 --> 00:13:33.213 line:78%
TO TELL HIM SO?

00:13:32.512 --> 00:13:33.947 line:78%
AND IF THERE'S NO ONE, THEN THE

00:13:33.313 --> 00:13:34.814 line:78%
PRESIDENT, OF COURSE, IS FREE TO

00:13:34.047 --> 00:13:36.816 line:78%
PURSUE HIS COURSE OF ERRONEOUS

00:13:34.914 --> 00:13:37.851 line:78%
INTERPRETATIONS.

00:13:36.916 --> 00:13:38.918 line:78%
WHAT THEN BECOMES OF OUR

00:13:37.951 --> 00:13:39.319 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL FORM OF

00:13:39.019 --> 00:13:39.919 line:78%
GOVERNMENT?

00:13:39.419 --> 00:13:40.887 line:78%
SO WHEN COUNSEL FOR THE

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:41.855 line:78%
PRESIDENT, IN HIS BRIEF, STATES

00:13:40.987 --> 00:13:43.023 line:78%
THAT THIS CASE GOES TO THE HEART

00:13:41.955 --> 00:13:43.757 line:78%
OF OUR BASIC CONSTITUTIONAL

00:13:43.123 --> 00:13:44.357 line:78%
SYSTEM, WE AGREE BECAUSE, IN OUR

00:13:43.857 --> 00:13:44.924 line:78%
VIEW, THIS NATION'S

00:13:44.457 --> 00:13:46.026 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL FORM OF

00:13:45.025 --> 00:13:46.393 line:78%
GOVERNMENT IS IN SERIOUS

00:13:46.126 --> 00:13:47.127 line:78%
JEOPARDY.

00:13:46.493 --> 00:13:48.995 line:78%
IF THE PRESIDENT, ANY PRESIDENT,

00:13:47.227 --> 00:13:49.996 line:78%
IS TO SAY THAT THE CONSTITUTION

00:13:49.095 --> 00:13:50.997 line:78%
MEANS WHAT HE SAYS IT DOES AND

00:13:50.096 --> 00:13:51.931 line:78%
THAT THERE IS NO ONE, NOT EVEN

00:13:51.097 --> 00:14:26.633 line:78%
THE SUPREME COURT, TO TELL HIM

00:13:52.032 --> 00:14:58.999 line:78%
OTHERWISE --

00:14:26.733 --> 00:15:00.066 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. JAWORSKI.

00:14:59.099 --> 00:15:00.967 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES?

00:15:00.166 --> 00:15:02.068 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE PRESIDENT WENT TO A

00:15:01.067 --> 00:15:03.036 line:78%
COURT.

00:15:02.168 --> 00:15:04.037 line:78%
HE WENT TO THE DISTRICT COURT

00:15:03.136 --> 00:15:05.138 line:78%
WITH HIS MOTION TO QUASH AND

00:15:04.137 --> 00:15:05.438 line:78%
THEN HE FILED A CROSS-PETITION

00:15:05.238 --> 00:15:06.239 line:78%
HERE.

00:15:05.538 --> 00:15:07.107 line:78%
HE'S NOT -- HE'S ASKING THE

00:15:06.339 --> 00:15:08.208 line:78%
COURT TO SAY THAT HIS POSITION

00:15:07.207 --> 00:15:08.575 line:78%
IS CORRECT AS A MATTER OF LAW.

00:15:08.308 --> 00:15:09.342 line:78%
IS HE NOT?

00:15:08.675 --> 00:15:10.076 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HE'S SAYING HIS POSITION IS

00:15:09.442 --> 00:15:11.177 line:78%
CORRECT BECAUSE HE INTERPRETS

00:15:10.176 --> 00:15:11.578 line:78%
THE CONSTITUTION THAT WAY.

00:15:11.277 --> 00:15:12.212 line:78%
&gt;&gt; CORRECT.

00:15:11.678 --> 00:15:13.113 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THIS IS WHAT HE SAYS --

00:15:12.312 --> 00:15:14.080 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND HE'S ASKING -- HE'S

00:15:13.213 --> 00:15:15.048 line:78%
SUBMITTING HIS POSITION TO THE

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.316 line:78%
COURT AND ASKING US TO AGREE

00:15:15.148 --> 00:15:17.050 line:78%
WITH HIM.

00:15:16.416 --> 00:15:17.784 line:78%
HE WENT, FIRST, TO THE DISTRICT

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:18.151 line:78%
COURT AND HE PETITIONED IN THIS

00:15:17.884 --> 00:15:19.285 line:78%
COURT.

00:15:18.251 --> 00:15:20.020 line:78%
HE'S NOT -- HE HAS, HIMSELF,

00:15:19.386 --> 00:15:20.587 line:78%
INVOKED THE JUDICIAL PROCESS AND

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.321 line:78%
HE IS COMMITTED TO IT.

00:15:20.687 --> 00:15:22.389 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THAT'S NOT ENTIRELY

00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:23.156 line:78%
CORRECT, MR. JUSTICE.

00:15:22.489 --> 00:15:23.790 line:78%
&gt;&gt; DIDN'T HE FILE A MOTION TO

00:15:23.256 --> 00:15:24.457 line:78%
QUASH THE SUBPOENAS IN THE

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:35.268 line:78%
DISTRICT COURT OR THE UNITED

00:15:24.557 --> 00:15:36.436 line:78%
STATES?

00:15:35.368 --> 00:15:37.103 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHILE THE MOTION TO QUASH THE

00:15:36.536 --> 00:15:37.837 line:78%
SUBPOENA IN SIRICA HAS ALSO

00:15:37.203 --> 00:15:38.505 line:78%
TAKEN THE POSITION THAT WE HAVE

00:15:37.937 --> 00:15:39.272 line:78%
NO STANDING IN THIS COURT TO

00:15:38.605 --> 00:15:40.306 line:78%
HAVE THIS ISSUE HEARD.

00:15:39.372 --> 00:15:41.441 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AS A MATTER OF LAW.

00:15:40.407 --> 00:15:41.741 line:78%
HE'S MAKING THAT ARGUMENT TO A

00:15:41.541 --> 00:15:42.442 line:78%
COURT.

00:15:41.841 --> 00:15:43.343 line:78%
AS A MATTER OF CONSTITUTIONAL

00:15:42.542 --> 00:15:44.544 line:78%
LAW, HE IS CORRECT.

00:15:43.443 --> 00:15:45.245 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SO THAT, OF COURSE, THIS

00:15:44.644 --> 00:15:45.945 line:78%
COURT COULD THEN NOT PASS UPON

00:15:45.345 --> 00:15:46.513 line:78%
THE CONSTITUTIONAL QUESTION OF

00:15:46.046 --> 00:15:47.414 line:78%
HOW HE INTERPRETS THE

00:15:46.613 --> 00:15:48.481 line:78%
CONSTITUTION IF HIS POSITION

00:15:47.514 --> 00:15:49.482 line:78%
WERE CORRECT, BUT --

00:15:48.581 --> 00:15:51.651 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AS A MATTER OF LAW, IF HIS

00:15:49.582 --> 00:15:52.285 line:78%
POSITION IS CORRECT --

00:15:51.751 --> 00:15:52.986 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT, SIR.

00:15:52.385 --> 00:15:53.553 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THEN HE IS THE SOLE JUDGE.

00:15:53.086 --> 00:15:54.521 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT.

00:15:53.653 --> 00:15:55.588 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND HE'S ASKING THIS COURT TO

00:15:54.621 --> 00:15:57.624 line:78%
AGREE WITH THAT PROPOSITION AS A

00:15:55.689 --> 00:16:03.630 line:78%
MATTER OF CONSTITUTIONAL LAW.

00:15:57.724 --> 00:16:06.633 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT WHAT I'M SAYING IS, IF HE

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:10.603 line:78%
IS THE SOLE JUDGE AND HE IS TO

00:16:06.733 --> 00:16:12.639 line:78%
BE CONSIDERED THE SOLE JUDGE AND

00:16:10.704 --> 00:16:13.606 line:78%
HE IS IN ERROR IN HIS

00:16:12.739 --> 00:16:14.574 line:78%
INTERPRETATION, THEN HE GOES ON

00:16:13.707 --> 00:16:38.832 line:78%
BEING IN ERROR IN HIS

00:16:14.674 --> 00:16:39.799 line:78%
INTERPRETATION.

00:16:38.932 --> 00:16:40.867 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THEN THIS COURT WILL

00:16:39.899 --> 00:16:42.002 line:78%
TELL HIM SO.

00:16:40.967 --> 00:16:42.435 line:78%
THAT'S WHAT THIS CASE IS ABOUT,

00:16:42.102 --> 00:16:43.236 line:78%
ISN'T IT?

00:16:42.535 --> 00:16:43.837 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THAT'S WHAT I THINK THE

00:16:43.336 --> 00:16:45.105 line:78%
CASE IS ABOUT.

00:16:43.937 --> 00:16:45.839 line:78%
YES, SIR.

00:16:45.205 --> 00:16:46.506 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN SUBMITTING HIMSELF TO THE

00:16:45.939 --> 00:16:47.240 line:78%
JUDICIAL PROCESS IN THE SAME

00:16:46.606 --> 00:16:47.941 line:78%
SENSE THAT YOU ARE, IS THAT NOT

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:48.975 line:78%
SO, MR. JAWORSKI?

00:16:48.041 --> 00:16:49.909 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I CAN'T SAY THAT --

00:16:49.075 --> 00:16:50.977 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU TAKE ONE POSITION AND HE

00:16:50.010 --> 00:17:06.192 line:78%
TAKES ANOTHER.

00:16:51.077 --> 00:17:12.165 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL MR. CHIEF JUSTICE, IN MY

00:17:06.292 --> 00:17:13.333 line:78%
VIEW, FRANKLY, IT IS A POSITION

00:17:12.265 --> 00:17:14.067 line:78%
WHERE HE SAYS "A CONSTITUTION

00:17:13.433 --> 00:17:14.768 line:78%
SAYS THIS AND NOBODY IS GOING TO

00:17:14.167 --> 00:17:15.502 line:78%
TELL ME WHAT THE CONSTITUTION

00:17:14.868 --> 00:17:16.236 line:78%
SAYS" BECAUSE, UP TO THIS POINT,

00:17:15.602 --> 00:17:17.203 line:78%
HE SAYS THAT HE AND HE ALONE IS

00:17:16.336 --> 00:17:18.238 line:78%
THE PROPER ONE TO INTERPRET THE

00:17:17.303 --> 00:17:19.372 line:78%
CONSTITUTION.

00:17:18.338 --> 00:17:19.973 line:78%
NOW, THERE'S NOW WAY TO ESCAPE

00:17:19.472 --> 00:17:20.674 line:78%
THAT BECAUSE THE BRIEFS

00:17:20.073 --> 00:17:21.241 line:78%
DEFINITELY POINT THAT OUT TIME

00:17:20.774 --> 00:17:22.375 line:78%
AFTER TIME.

00:17:21.341 --> 00:17:22.876 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THINK THIS MATTER MAY BE

00:17:22.475 --> 00:17:23.476 line:78%
ONE OF SEMANTICS.

00:17:22.976 --> 00:17:24.477 line:78%
EACH OF YOU IS TAKING A

00:17:23.576 --> 00:17:25.145 line:78%
DIFFERENT POSITION ON THE BASIC

00:17:24.577 --> 00:17:26.379 line:78%
QUESTION AND EACH OF YOU IS

00:17:25.245 --> 00:17:26.680 line:78%
SUBMITTING FOR DECISION TO THIS

00:17:26.479 --> 00:17:27.313 line:78%
COURT.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:28.481 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, WE START WITH --

00:17:27.414 --> 00:17:29.215 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT MAY BE, SIR.

00:17:28.581 --> 00:17:29.949 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE START WITH A CONSTITUTION

00:17:29.315 --> 00:17:30.650 line:78%
THAT DOES NOT CONTAIN THE WORDS

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:30.950 line:78%
"EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE," IS THAT

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:31.584 line:78%
RIGHT?

00:17:31.051 --> 00:17:32.385 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT, SIR.

00:17:31.685 --> 00:17:33.520 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SO, WHY DON'T WE GO ON FROM

00:17:32.485 --> 00:17:33.987 line:78%
THERE?

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:34.688 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ALRIGHT, SIR.

00:17:34.087 --> 00:17:35.588 line:78%
THAT IS A VERY GOOD BEGINNING

00:17:34.788 --> 00:17:36.189 line:78%
POINT BUT, OF COURSE, OTHER

00:17:35.689 --> 00:17:36.923 line:78%
THINGS HAVE NEEDED TO BE

00:17:36.289 --> 00:17:49.536 line:78%
DISCUSSED AS MUCH AS THEY'VE

00:17:37.023 --> 00:17:50.570 line:78%
BEEN RAISED.

00:17:49.636 --> 00:17:51.538 line:78%
&gt;&gt; PERHAPS IT WOULD FURTHER

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:52.572 line:78%
NARROW THE AREA IF, AS I TAKE IT

00:17:51.638 --> 00:17:53.573 line:78%
FROM YOUR BRIEFS, YOU DO

00:17:52.672 --> 00:17:54.607 line:78%
EMPHASIZE THERE IS NO CLAIM HERE

00:17:53.673 --> 00:17:55.608 line:78%
OF TYPICAL MILITARY SECRETS OR

00:17:54.708 --> 00:17:56.576 line:78%
DIPLOMATIC SECRETS OR WHAT, IN

00:17:55.709 --> 00:17:57.610 line:78%
THE BURR CASE, WERE REFERRED TO

00:17:56.676 --> 00:17:58.545 line:78%
AS STATE SECRETES.

00:17:57.711 --> 00:18:16.696 line:78%
NONE OF THOSE THINGS ARE IN THIS

00:17:58.645 --> 00:18:17.731 line:78%
CASE.

00:18:16.796 --> 00:18:18.932 line:78%
IS THAT RIGHT?

00:18:17.831 --> 00:18:19.632 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT IS CORRECT, SIR, AND WE

00:18:19.032 --> 00:18:20.367 line:78%
DO POINT TO THE AUTHORITIES TO

00:18:19.733 --> 00:18:20.934 line:78%
SHOW THAT THERE IS A DIFFERENCE

00:18:20.467 --> 00:18:21.768 line:78%
IN THE SITUATION HERE.

00:18:21.034 --> 00:18:26.039 line:78%
I DO THINK THAT IT'S PROPER, AS

00:18:21.868 --> 00:18:39.019 line:78%
MUCH AS I REGRET TO HAVE TO DO

00:18:26.139 --> 00:18:40.020 line:78%
IT, TO POINT THAT THE

00:18:39.119 --> 00:18:40.987 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S INTERPRETATION OF

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:50.196 line:78%
WHAT HIS ACTION SHOULD BE IN

00:18:41.087 --> 00:18:52.298 line:78%
THESE PARTICULAR SET OF

00:18:50.296 --> 00:18:53.299 line:78%
CIRCUMSTANCES AS ONE THAT REALLY

00:18:52.399 --> 00:18:54.267 line:78%
REQUIRES JUDICIAL INTERVENTION,

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.468 line:78%
PERHAPS MORE SO THAN A NORMAL

00:18:54.367 --> 00:18:56.136 line:78%
ONE WOULD.

00:18:55.568 --> 00:18:56.870 line:78%
I THINK THAT WE REALIZE THAT

00:18:56.236 --> 00:18:57.570 line:78%
THERE IS AT STEAK THE MATTER OF

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.304 line:78%
THE SUPPLYING OF EVIDENCE THAT

00:18:57.671 --> 00:18:59.506 line:78%
RELATES TO THE DUE FORM OF CLOSE

00:18:58.405 --> 00:19:00.306 line:78%
AIDS AND DUBIETIES.

00:18:59.606 --> 00:19:01.041 line:78%
I THINK WE'RE AWARE OF THE FACT

00:19:00.407 --> 00:19:01.708 line:78%
THAT THE PRESIDENT HAD PUBLICLY

00:19:01.141 --> 00:19:02.375 line:78%
STATED THAT HE BELIEVED THAT

00:19:01.808 --> 00:19:03.543 line:78%
THESE TWO AIDS OF HIS, MR.

00:19:02.475 --> 00:19:04.244 line:78%
HALDEMAN AND MR. EHRLICHMAN

00:19:03.643 --> 00:19:04.511 line:78%
WOULD COME OUT ALRIGHT IN THE

00:19:04.344 --> 00:19:05.478 line:78%
END.

00:19:04.611 --> 00:19:06.513 line:78%
ADDED TO THAT, THE FACT THAT THE

00:19:05.578 --> 00:19:07.514 line:78%
PRESIDENT HAS SENSITIVITY OR OWN

00:19:06.613 --> 00:19:08.715 line:78%
INVOLVEMENT IS ALSO A MATTER

00:19:07.614 --> 00:19:09.349 line:78%
THAT CALLS FOR THE EXERCISE OF

00:19:08.815 --> 00:19:10.050 line:78%
THE QUESTION TO WHICH MR.

00:19:09.449 --> 00:19:28.668 line:78%
JUSTICE DOUGLAS ALLUDED AS ONE

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:29.669 line:78%
THAT IS SOMEWHAT UNUSUAL.

00:19:28.768 --> 00:19:30.770 line:78%
TURNING NOW TO JURISDICTION,

00:19:29.769 --> 00:19:31.338 line:78%
BEFORE THE COURT ARE THE TWO

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:31.771 line:78%
QUESTIONS OF STATUTORY

00:19:31.438 --> 00:19:32.672 line:78%
JURISDICTION.

00:19:31.871 --> 00:19:33.673 line:78%
THE COURT DIRECTED THE PARTIES

00:19:32.772 --> 00:19:34.841 line:78%
TO BRIEF AND ARGUE.

00:19:33.773 --> 00:19:35.442 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. JAWORSKI, AT THIS POINT,

00:19:34.941 --> 00:19:42.749 line:78%
HELP ME OVER ONE HURDLE.

00:19:35.542 --> 00:19:43.783 line:78%
DO YOU FEEL THAT THE MANDAMUS

00:19:42.849 --> 00:19:57.897 line:78%
CASE AS SUCH AS HERE?

00:19:43.883 --> 00:19:58.932 line:78%
I SEARCHED YOUR PETITION --

00:19:57.998 --> 00:19:59.933 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, WE DO, SIR.

00:19:59.032 --> 00:20:04.037 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I SEARCHED YOUR PETITION FOR

00:20:00.033 --> 00:20:05.071 line:78%
CERTIORARI IN VAIN TO FIND EVEN

00:20:04.137 --> 00:20:06.072 line:78%
A MENTION OF IT, AND I WONDER.

00:20:05.171 --> 00:20:08.041 line:78%
IT'S A TECHNICAL QUESTION BUT

00:20:06.172 --> 00:20:09.075 line:78%
THE -- WHAT IS YOUR POSITION?

00:20:08.141 --> 00:20:17.150 line:78%
THAT THE ISSUE IS IN ANY OF

00:20:09.175 --> 00:20:18.418 line:78%
ENTERED HERE?

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.119 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

00:20:18.518 --> 00:20:19.886 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHETHER THE CASE IS NOT --

00:20:19.219 --> 00:20:20.587 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE SAY IT'S HERE NOT ONLY

00:20:19.986 --> 00:20:21.321 line:78%
BECAUSE OF THE APPEAL ITSELF,

00:20:20.687 --> 00:20:21.755 line:78%
BUT ALSO BECAUSE OF THE PETITION

00:20:21.421 --> 00:20:22.355 line:78%
FOR MANDAMUS.

00:20:21.855 --> 00:20:23.356 line:78%
NOW WE DID, MR. JUSTICE,

00:20:22.455 --> 00:20:23.690 line:78%
DISCUSSED THAT IN ONE OF THE

00:20:23.456 --> 00:20:24.457 line:78%
BRIEFS.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.358 line:78%
NOW, IT MAY BE THAT IT WASN'T

00:20:24.557 --> 00:20:26.559 line:78%
ORIGINALLY WHEN WE FILED THE

00:20:25.458 --> 00:20:27.227 line:78%
ORIGINAL BRIEF ON JURISDICTION.

00:20:26.659 --> 00:20:27.894 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU MENTIONED IT IN YOUR

00:20:27.327 --> 00:20:28.528 line:78%
SECOND BRIEF ON THE MERITS.

00:20:27.994 --> 00:20:29.162 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES.

00:20:28.628 --> 00:20:29.763 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT NOT AT ALL IN YOUR

00:20:29.262 --> 00:20:30.497 line:78%
PETITION FOR CERTIORARI.

00:20:29.863 --> 00:20:31.598 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, WE DID IN THE -- IT WAS

00:20:30.597 --> 00:20:32.165 line:78%
IN THE FOOTNOTE ON PAGE 2 OF THE

00:20:31.698 --> 00:20:32.766 line:78%
PETITIONER FOR WRIT OF

00:20:32.265 --> 00:20:33.500 line:78%
CERTIORARI, MR. JUSTICE.

00:20:32.866 --> 00:20:34.601 line:78%
WELL, I WOULD THINK SO BUT THERE

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:35.268 line:78%
REALLY IS NO ISSUE BETWEEN THE

00:20:34.701 --> 00:20:42.509 line:78%
PARTIES HERE ON THE ISSUE OF

00:20:35.368 --> 00:20:43.510 line:78%
JURISDICTION.

00:20:42.609 --> 00:20:52.552 line:78%
I MEAN, THERE'S NO ARGUMENT AS

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:53.586 line:78%
BETWEEN THE PARTIES ON IT.

00:20:52.652 --> 00:20:54.587 line:78%
AND, WHILE OF COURSE THE PARTIES

00:20:53.687 --> 00:20:55.588 line:78%
CAN'T AGREE ON IT, I MUST SAY

00:20:54.688 --> 00:20:56.589 line:78%
THAT ON THREE DIFFERENT BASES

00:20:55.689 --> 00:20:57.657 line:78%
THE JURISDICTION DOES EXIST AS

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:58.658 line:78%
WE SEE IT.

00:20:57.757 --> 00:20:59.659 line:78%
NOW, I AM NOT YET GETTING TO THE

00:20:58.758 --> 00:21:00.627 line:78%
QUESTION OF THE INTRA-EXECUTIVE

00:20:59.759 --> 00:21:01.661 line:78%
MATTER THAT HAS BEEN RAISED BUT

00:21:00.727 --> 00:21:02.729 line:78%
I AM DISCUSSING NOW THE

00:21:01.761 --> 00:21:03.029 line:78%
STATUTORY BASIS OF JURISDICTION,

00:21:02.829 --> 00:21:19.779 line:78%
AND --

00:21:03.129 --> 00:21:20.814 line:78%
&gt;&gt; (INAUDIBLE)

00:21:19.879 --> 00:21:21.815 line:78%
&gt;&gt; TO ANSWER YOUR QUESTION

00:21:20.914 --> 00:21:22.982 line:78%
DIRECTLY, SIR, THIS IS CORRECT.

00:21:21.915 --> 00:21:23.616 line:78%
WE ARE STANDING UPON NOT ONLY

00:21:23.083 --> 00:21:30.056 line:78%
THE MATTER THAT THIS IS AN

00:21:23.717 --> 00:21:32.025 line:78%
APPEAL THAT PROPERLY HAD BEEN IN

00:21:30.156 --> 00:21:33.059 line:78%
THE COURT OF APPEALS AND, FOR

00:21:32.125 --> 00:21:34.094 line:78%
THAT REASON, HAS BEEN MOVED UP

00:21:33.159 --> 00:21:35.295 line:78%
HERE PROPERLY UNDER 1254-1.

00:21:34.194 --> 00:21:35.995 line:78%
WE ALSO SAY THAT COURT HAS

00:21:35.395 --> 00:21:36.730 line:78%
JURISDICTION OVER THE PETITION

00:21:36.096 --> 00:21:37.430 line:78%
AND CROSS-PETITION UNDER 1254-1

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:38.164 line:78%
BECAUSE IT PRESENT FOR REVIEW

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:39.065 line:78%
ALL QUESTIONS RAISED BY THE

00:21:38.264 --> 00:21:51.444 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S PETITION FOR WRIT OF

00:21:39.165 --> 00:21:52.312 line:78%
MANDAMUS.

00:21:51.544 --> 00:21:54.280 line:78%
AND THEN WE ALSO SAY THAT, IN

00:21:52.412 --> 00:22:04.524 line:78%
ADDITION TO THAT, THE ALL WRITS

00:21:54.381 --> 00:22:05.392 line:78%
ACT GIVES THIS COURT

00:22:04.624 --> 00:22:06.393 line:78%
JURISDICTION TO PROCEED.

00:22:05.492 --> 00:22:07.460 line:78%
&gt;&gt; OF COURSE, IN A MANDAMUS

00:22:06.493 --> 00:22:08.395 line:78%
ACTION, JUDGE SIRICA WOULD BE

00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:10.430 line:78%
THE PARTY RESPONDENT AND HE'S

00:22:08.495 --> 00:22:11.398 line:78%
NOT A PARTY IN THIS CASE AND

00:22:10.530 --> 00:22:12.465 line:78%
HE'S NOT REPRESENTED BY COUNSEL

00:22:11.498 --> 00:22:13.366 line:78%
HERE, IS HE?

00:22:12.565 --> 00:22:14.501 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AS FAR AS I KNOW, HE'S NOT,

00:22:13.466 --> 00:22:15.535 line:78%
NO, SIR.

00:22:14.601 --> 00:22:16.536 line:78%
IN FACT, I'M SURE HE'S NOT.

00:22:15.635 --> 00:22:17.437 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THE MANDAMUS WOULD BE

00:22:16.636 --> 00:22:18.571 line:78%
NIXON VERSUS SIRICA, WOULD IT

00:22:17.537 --> 00:22:27.647 line:78%
NOT?

00:22:18.672 --> 00:22:28.648 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT IT WAS BROUGHT UP BY THE

00:22:27.747 --> 00:22:30.717 line:78%
PRESIDENT IN THEIR PETITION FOR

00:22:28.748 --> 00:22:31.618 line:78%
MANDAMUS AND THAT'S RIGHT.

00:22:30.817 --> 00:22:32.686 line:78%
THAT'S THE WAY IT GOT INTO THIS

00:22:31.718 --> 00:22:33.753 line:78%
COURT.

00:22:32.786 --> 00:22:34.754 line:78%
IT RAISES THE SAME QUESTIONS

00:22:33.853 --> 00:22:35.789 line:78%
ACTUALLY THAT WERE RAISED ON THE

00:22:34.854 --> 00:22:36.723 line:78%
MATTER THAT WE BROUGHT UPON.

00:22:35.889 --> 00:22:37.791 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHAT WAS THE CHRONOLOGY, MR.

00:22:36.823 --> 00:22:42.996 line:78%
JAWORSKI?

00:22:37.891 --> 00:22:43.897 line:78%
THE NOTICE OF APPEAL FROM JUDGE

00:22:43.096 --> 00:22:44.864 line:78%
SIRICA'S ORDER WAS THE FIRST

00:22:43.997 --> 00:22:46.933 line:78%
STEP TAKEN TO GET TO THE COURT

00:22:44.964 --> 00:22:48.868 line:78%
OF APPEALS, WAS IT?

00:22:47.033 --> 00:22:49.969 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S, I BELIEVE, RIGHT, SIR

00:22:48.968 --> 00:22:51.104 line:78%
AND --

00:22:50.070 --> 00:22:51.771 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND WHILE THAT WAS PENDING,

00:22:51.204 --> 00:22:52.439 line:78%
THEN I GATHER, THE PRESIDENT

00:22:51.871 --> 00:22:52.906 line:78%
PETITIONED FOR MANDAMUS WAS

00:22:52.539 --> 00:22:54.007 line:78%
BROUGHT.

00:22:53.006 --> 00:22:54.274 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT, SIR.

00:22:54.107 --> 00:22:54.974 line:78%
YES.

00:22:54.374 --> 00:22:55.875 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THEN THE LAST STEP WAS

00:22:55.075 --> 00:23:03.983 line:78%
THAT YOU FILED THE PETITION TO

00:22:55.975 --> 00:23:06.019 line:78%
BYPASS HERE.

00:23:04.084 --> 00:23:07.020 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT, SIR.

00:23:06.119 --> 00:23:08.021 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THAT PETITION TO BYPASS

00:23:07.120 --> 00:23:10.990 line:78%
FILED, I GATHER, TO WHATEVER

00:23:08.121 --> 00:23:12.058 line:78%
CASE WAS PENDING IN THE COURT OF

00:23:11.091 --> 00:23:13.059 line:78%
APPEALS?

00:23:12.158 --> 00:23:14.094 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR.

00:23:13.159 --> 00:23:15.061 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND AT THAT TIME, THE CASE

00:23:14.194 --> 00:23:16.096 line:78%
PENDING WAS BOTH THE APPEAL FROM

00:23:15.161 --> 00:23:17.197 line:78%
JUDGE SIRICA'S OFFICE --

00:23:16.196 --> 00:23:17.998 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT, SIR.

00:23:17.297 --> 00:23:18.231 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THE PRESIDENT'S PETITION

00:23:18.098 --> 00:23:19.165 line:78%
--

00:23:18.331 --> 00:23:20.200 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MANDAMUS, CORRECT.

00:23:19.265 --> 00:23:20.567 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHICH YOU FEEL THEY ARE NOT

00:23:20.300 --> 00:23:21.167 line:78%
TWO CASES?

00:23:20.667 --> 00:23:22.302 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR.

00:23:21.267 --> 00:23:22.802 line:78%
THEY RAISE THE SAME QUESTIONS

00:23:22.402 --> 00:23:23.536 line:78%
BUT THAT'S --

00:23:22.902 --> 00:23:24.237 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND YET, YOU COULD BRING EACH

00:23:23.636 --> 00:23:25.305 line:78%
UP SEPARATELY IF YOU SO CHOSE.

00:23:24.337 --> 00:23:26.072 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I COULD HAVE, SIR, YES.

00:23:25.405 --> 00:23:26.373 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT SEEMS TO ME THERE'RE TWO

00:23:26.172 --> 00:23:27.273 line:78%
CASES.

00:23:26.473 --> 00:23:28.274 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT IN AS MUCH AS THEY

00:23:27.374 --> 00:23:29.476 line:78%
PRESENT THE SAME QUESTIONS, IT

00:23:28.375 --> 00:23:30.143 line:78%
OCCURRED TO US THAT IT WAS

00:23:29.576 --> 00:23:31.511 line:78%
APPROPRIATE TO RELY UPON THE

00:23:30.243 --> 00:23:32.245 line:78%
JURISDICTION AS TO BOTH OF THEM.

00:23:31.611 --> 00:23:32.879 line:78%
&gt;&gt; EXCEPT, I WOULD SUGGEST AGAIN

00:23:32.345 --> 00:23:33.546 line:78%
THAT, WITH RESPECT TO THE

00:23:32.979 --> 00:23:34.481 line:78%
MANDAMUS ACTION, ONE OF THE

00:23:33.646 --> 00:23:35.048 line:78%
PARTIES ISN'T HERE IN COURT OR

00:23:34.581 --> 00:23:35.715 line:78%
PRESENTED BY COUNSEL.

00:23:35.148 --> 00:23:36.483 line:78%
HE IS THE PARTY RESPONDENT.

00:23:35.815 --> 00:23:38.385 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IT IS -- I DON'T HAVE

00:23:36.583 --> 00:23:41.454 line:78%
THE RECORD BEFORE ME BUT, I MUST

00:23:38.485 --> 00:23:42.455 line:78%
SAY AND I WILL NOT MAKE AN

00:23:41.554 --> 00:23:43.456 line:78%
OUTRIGHT REPRESENTATION THAT

00:23:42.555 --> 00:23:44.457 line:78%
JUDGE SIRICA IS, AND THAT'S WHY

00:23:43.556 --> 00:23:45.458 line:78%
I HESITATED A FEW MINUTES AGO,

00:23:44.557 --> 00:23:57.570 line:78%
WAS MADE A PARTY AFTER ALL THAT

00:23:45.558 --> 00:23:58.571 line:78%
WAS BROUGHT UP BY THE PRESIDENT.

00:23:57.671 --> 00:23:59.572 line:78%
BUT, I AM ADVISED BY A NOTE JUST

00:23:58.672 --> 00:24:00.540 line:78%
PASSED TO ME BY MR. LACOVARA

00:23:59.673 --> 00:24:08.715 line:78%
THAT JUDGE SIRICA IS A PARTY TO

00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:19.092 line:78%
THAT PROCEEDING.

00:24:08.815 --> 00:24:19.793 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHO REPRESENTS HIM HERE?

00:24:19.192 --> 00:24:20.427 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I DON'T KNOW OF ANYONE

00:24:19.893 --> 00:24:20.894 line:78%
REPRESENTING HIM HERE, MR.

00:24:20.527 --> 00:24:21.995 line:78%
JUSTICE.

00:24:20.994 --> 00:24:22.729 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HAS HE FILED ANY BRIEF OR

00:24:22.095 --> 00:24:23.029 line:78%
MADE AN APPEARANCE AT ALL IN ANY

00:24:22.829 --> 00:24:24.030 line:78%
SENSE?

00:24:23.129 --> 00:24:24.998 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SO FAR AS I KNOW, NONE.

00:24:24.130 --> 00:24:26.066 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IF YOU'RE RIGHT THAT,

00:24:25.098 --> 00:24:27.000 line:78%
AT ANY EVENT, JUDGE SIRICA'S

00:24:26.166 --> 00:24:28.201 line:78%
ORDER WAS AN APPEALABLE ORDER.

00:24:27.100 --> 00:24:28.935 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT.

00:24:28.301 --> 00:24:29.636 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IF YOU'RE CORRECT IN THAT

00:24:29.035 --> 00:24:30.337 line:78%
SUBMISSION, DO WE EVER HAVE TO

00:24:29.736 --> 00:24:32.038 line:78%
REACH ANY ISSUES RAISED BY THE

00:24:30.437 --> 00:24:33.073 line:78%
MANDAMUS?

00:24:32.138 --> 00:24:34.040 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, IT WOULD NOT.

00:24:33.173 --> 00:24:35.075 line:78%
WE WERE POINTING OUT THAT THE

00:24:34.140 --> 00:24:37.110 line:78%
JURISDICTION RESTS ON A

00:24:35.175 --> 00:24:38.044 line:78%
THREE-PRONG BASIS.

00:24:37.210 --> 00:24:39.112 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT THE MANDAMUS IS NOT YOUR

00:24:38.144 --> 00:24:40.146 line:78%
ACTION.

00:24:39.212 --> 00:24:42.115 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S NOT, NO, SIR.

00:24:40.246 --> 00:24:43.149 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND YOU'RE NOT OBLIGING THE

00:24:42.215 --> 00:24:45.151 line:78%
DEFENDANT, ARE YOU?

00:24:43.249 --> 00:24:46.186 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR.

00:24:45.251 --> 00:24:47.153 line:78%
WE, HOWEVER, WERE POINTING OUT

00:24:46.286 --> 00:24:48.154 line:78%
THAT THE SAME ISSUES REALLY WERE

00:24:47.253 --> 00:25:09.509 line:78%
RAISED BY IT IF THE PETITIONER

00:24:48.254 --> 00:25:10.477 line:78%
IS PROPERLY BEFORE THE COURT.

00:25:09.609 --> 00:25:11.511 line:78%
NOW, IF THERE ARE NO FURTHER

00:25:10.577 --> 00:25:12.445 line:78%
QUESTIONS ON THE MATTER OF

00:25:11.611 --> 00:25:13.480 line:78%
STATUTORY JURISDICTION, I WOULD

00:25:12.545 --> 00:25:14.514 line:78%
LIKE TO PASS TO THE

00:25:13.580 --> 00:25:15.515 line:78%
INTRA-EXECUTIVE DISPUTE.

00:25:14.614 --> 00:25:16.683 line:78%
FIRST, WE RECOGNIZE, OF COURSE,

00:25:15.615 --> 00:25:17.317 line:78%
THAT JURISDICTION CANNOT BE

00:25:16.783 --> 00:25:18.051 line:78%
WAIVED AND NOTHING THAT IS

00:25:17.417 --> 00:25:18.785 line:78%
PRESENTED HERE IS WITH THE IDEA

00:25:18.151 --> 00:25:19.586 line:78%
OF SUGGESTING EVEN REMOTELY THAT

00:25:18.885 --> 00:25:20.620 line:78%
THERE IS ANY WAIVER WITH RESPECT

00:25:19.686 --> 00:25:21.821 line:78%
TO THE QUESTIONS OF

00:25:20.720 --> 00:25:22.422 line:78%
JURISDICTION.

00:25:21.921 --> 00:25:23.123 line:78%
BUT, WE DO SAY THAT THE

00:25:22.522 --> 00:25:23.857 line:78%
CONTENTION IS THAT THERE IS AN

00:25:23.223 --> 00:25:24.758 line:78%
INTRA-EXECUTIVE DISPUTE AND, FOR

00:25:23.957 --> 00:25:26.726 line:78%
THAT REASON, THIS COURT CANNOT

00:25:24.858 --> 00:25:27.861 line:78%
PASS UP ON THESE QUESTIONS AS

00:25:26.826 --> 00:25:28.962 line:78%
NOT SOUND.

00:25:27.961 --> 00:25:29.662 line:78%
BEFORE DISCUSSING THE CASE AS,

00:25:29.062 --> 00:25:32.866 line:78%
HOWEVER, I THINK THAT IT WOULD

00:25:29.763 --> 00:25:34.801 line:78%
BE APPROPRIATE FOR US TO

00:25:32.966 --> 00:25:40.907 line:78%
UNDERTAKE THE BASES IN THE RIGHT

00:25:34.901 --> 00:25:41.841 line:78%
PERSPECTIVE.

00:25:41.007 --> 00:25:43.910 line:78%
LET ME SAY, FIRST, THAT WE STAND

00:25:41.941 --> 00:25:47.981 line:78%
UPON TWO BASES.

00:25:44.010 --> 00:25:48.982 line:78%
FIRST, THAT, ACTUALLY, THE

00:25:48.081 --> 00:25:49.983 line:78%
ORDERS THAT WERE ENTERED

00:25:49.082 --> 00:25:53.086 line:78%
CREATING THE OFFICE OF THE

00:25:50.083 --> 00:25:55.088 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR AND

00:25:53.186 --> 00:25:56.089 line:78%
DELINEATING HIS AUTHORITY, EVEN

00:25:55.188 --> 00:25:57.057 line:78%
THE ORIGINAL ORDER AT THE TIME

00:25:56.189 --> 00:25:59.092 line:78%
THAT MY PREDECESSOR WAS ACTING

00:25:57.157 --> 00:26:03.163 line:78%
AS SPECIAL PROSECUTOR HAD THE

00:25:59.192 --> 00:26:05.198 line:78%
FORCE AND EFFECT OF LAW.

00:26:03.263 --> 00:26:07.100 line:78%
WE ALSO POINT TO THE FACT THAT

00:26:05.298 --> 00:26:08.201 line:78%
THE ARRANGEMENT MADE ITSELF WITH

00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:10.236 line:78%
THE ACTING ATTORNEY GENERAL THAT

00:26:08.301 --> 00:26:11.237 line:78%
I MADE, IF I MAY POINT TO IT,

00:26:10.337 --> 00:26:12.305 line:78%
AND ONE REASON I HAVE NO

00:26:11.338 --> 00:26:13.273 line:78%
RESONANCE IN DISCUSSING THE

00:26:12.405 --> 00:26:15.342 line:78%
FACTS IS BECAUSE THE FACTS ARE

00:26:13.373 --> 00:26:16.309 line:78%
UNDISPUTED.

00:26:15.442 --> 00:26:18.278 line:78%
THERE HAS BEEN NO DISPUTE RAISED

00:26:16.409 --> 00:26:19.512 line:78%
AS TO JUST WHAT ACTUALLY

00:26:18.378 --> 00:26:20.180 line:78%
TRANSPIRED.

00:26:19.612 --> 00:26:20.880 line:78%
THE SITUATION IS ONE OF THE

00:26:20.280 --> 00:26:21.581 line:78%
ARRANGEMENTS ITSELF WHICH THE

00:26:20.980 --> 00:26:35.762 line:78%
ACTING ATTORNEY GENERAL POINTS

00:26:21.681 --> 00:26:36.696 line:78%
TO, WITH RESPECT TO THE MATTER

00:26:35.862 --> 00:26:37.630 line:78%
OF INDEPENDENCE HAVING BEEN

00:26:36.796 --> 00:26:39.666 line:78%
DISCUSSED BY HIM WITH THE

00:26:37.731 --> 00:26:40.700 line:78%
PRESIDENT.

00:26:39.766 --> 00:26:41.701 line:78%
THUS, MEANING THAT THE

00:26:40.800 --> 00:26:42.769 line:78%
PRESIDENT, HIMSELF, HAD APPROVED

00:26:41.801 --> 00:26:44.838 line:78%
THE SETTING UP OF THIS

00:26:42.869 --> 00:26:45.805 line:78%
PARTICULAR OFFICE AND THE RIGHTS

00:26:44.938 --> 00:26:46.873 line:78%
AND THE RESPONSIBILITIES THAT IT

00:26:45.905 --> 00:26:47.874 line:78%
HAS UNDER THE CHARTER.

00:26:46.973 --> 00:26:48.875 line:78%
NOW, LET ME -- WE SET THIS OUT

00:26:47.974 --> 00:26:49.909 line:78%
IN THE APPENDIX, OF COURSE,

00:26:48.975 --> 00:26:51.978 line:78%
POINTING PRECISELY TO WHAT THE

00:26:50.010 --> 00:26:53.079 line:78%
AUTHORITY AND RESPONSIBILITIES

00:26:52.078 --> 00:26:53.546 line:78%
AND OBLIGATIONS OF THE SPECIAL

00:26:53.179 --> 00:26:54.214 line:78%
PROSECUTOR ARE.

00:26:53.646 --> 00:26:55.015 line:78%
ONE OF THE EXPRESSED DUTIES

00:26:54.314 --> 00:26:55.949 line:78%
THAT'S DELEGATED TO THE SPECIAL

00:26:55.115 --> 00:27:02.022 line:78%
PROSECUTOR IS THAT HE SHALL HAVE

00:26:56.049 --> 00:27:40.493 line:78%
FULL AUTHORITY FOR INVESTIGATING

00:27:02.122 --> 00:27:41.428 line:78%
AND PROSECUTING, AMONG OTHERS,

00:27:40.593 --> 00:27:42.495 line:78%
ALLEGATIONS INVOLVING THE

00:27:41.528 --> 00:27:43.496 line:78%
PRESIDENT.

00:27:42.595 --> 00:27:44.497 line:78%
AND A DELEGATION OF AUTHORITY

00:27:43.596 --> 00:27:45.732 line:78%
EXPRESSLY STATES IN PARTICULAR

00:27:44.597 --> 00:27:46.466 line:78%
THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR SHALL

00:27:45.832 --> 00:27:47.167 line:78%
HAVE FULL AUTHORITY TO DETERMINE

00:27:46.566 --> 00:27:47.901 line:78%
WHETHER OR NOT TO CONTEST THE

00:27:47.267 --> 00:27:54.741 line:78%
ASSERTION OF EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE

00:27:48.001 --> 00:27:55.742 line:78%
OR ANY OTHER TESTIMONIAL

00:27:54.841 --> 00:27:56.743 line:78%
PRIVILEGE.

00:27:55.842 --> 00:27:57.744 line:78%
NOW IN THE INSTANCE OF MY

00:27:56.843 --> 00:27:58.745 line:78%
APPOINTMENT, UNLIKE THE

00:27:57.844 --> 00:27:59.779 line:78%
APPOINTMENT THAT HAD BEEN MADE

00:27:58.845 --> 00:28:00.747 line:78%
PRIOR THERETO, THERE WAS AN

00:27:59.879 --> 00:28:01.781 line:78%
AMENDED ORDER AND IT REFERRED TO

00:28:00.847 --> 00:28:02.782 line:78%
ASSURANCES GIVEN BY THE

00:28:01.881 --> 00:28:03.783 line:78%
PRESIDENT TO THE ATTORNEY

00:28:02.882 --> 00:28:04.818 line:78%
GENERAL THAT THE PRESIDENT WILL

00:28:03.883 --> 00:28:05.819 line:78%
NOT EXERCISE HIS CONSTITUTIONAL

00:28:04.918 --> 00:28:06.886 line:78%
POWERS TO AFFECT THE STORIES OF

00:28:05.919 --> 00:28:07.854 line:78%
THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR OR TO

00:28:06.986 --> 00:28:08.888 line:78%
LIMIT THE INDEPENDENCE THAT HE'S

00:28:07.954 --> 00:28:09.889 line:78%
HEREBY GIVEN, AND THAT HE WILL

00:28:08.988 --> 00:28:10.890 line:78%
NOT BE REMOVED FROM HIS DUTIES

00:28:09.989 --> 00:28:11.958 line:78%
EXCEPT FOR EXTRAORDINARY

00:28:10.990 --> 00:28:14.194 line:78%
IMPROPRIETIES ON HIS PART AND

00:28:12.058 --> 00:28:14.928 line:78%
WITHOUT THE PRESIDENT'S FIRST

00:28:14.294 --> 00:28:16.096 line:78%
CONSULTING THE MAJORITY AND THE

00:28:15.028 --> 00:28:17.063 line:78%
MINORITY LEADERS AND THE

00:28:16.196 --> 00:28:20.166 line:78%
CHAIRMAN IN RANKING THE MINORITY

00:28:17.163 --> 00:28:21.167 line:78%
MEMBERS OF THE JUDICIARY

00:28:20.266 --> 00:28:22.135 line:78%
COMMITTEES AND THE SENATE AND

00:28:21.267 --> 00:28:23.336 line:78%
HOUSE REPRESENTATIVES, AND

00:28:22.235 --> 00:28:24.070 line:78%
ASCERTAINING THAT THEIR

00:28:23.436 --> 00:28:26.206 line:78%
CONSENSUS IS IN ACCORD WITH THE

00:28:24.170 --> 00:28:29.275 line:78%
PROPOSED ACTION.

00:28:26.306 --> 00:28:39.452 line:78%
AND THEN, THAT THE JURISDICTION

00:28:29.376 --> 00:28:40.420 line:78%
OF THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR WILL

00:28:39.552 --> 00:28:41.421 line:78%
NOT BE LIMITED WITHOUT THE

00:28:40.520 --> 00:28:42.589 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S FIRST CONSULTING

00:28:41.521 --> 00:28:43.256 line:78%
WITH SUCH MEMBERS OF CONGRESS

00:28:42.689 --> 00:28:44.491 line:78%
AND ASCERTAINING THAT THEIR

00:28:43.356 --> 00:28:44.958 line:78%
CONSENSUS IS IN ACCORD WITH HIS

00:28:44.591 --> 00:28:46.393 line:78%
PROPOSED ACTION.

00:28:45.058 --> 00:28:47.494 line:78%
NOW, AT THE TIME --

00:28:46.493 --> 00:28:48.128 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S NOT IMPORTANT.

00:28:47.594 --> 00:28:49.396 line:78%
WHAT DOES CONSENSUS MEAN,

00:28:48.228 --> 00:28:50.397 line:78%
UNANIMOUS?

00:28:49.496 --> 00:28:51.464 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR, IT HADN'T BEEN

00:28:50.497 --> 00:28:53.433 line:78%
INTERPRETED BY THE ACTING

00:28:51.564 --> 00:28:56.436 line:78%
ATTORNEY GENERAL IN CONVERSATION

00:28:53.533 --> 00:28:59.439 line:78%
AS MEANING 6 OF 8.

00:28:56.536 --> 00:29:02.442 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I TAKE IT WHEN YOU MAKE

00:28:59.539 --> 00:29:03.510 line:78%
REFERENCE TO THIS YOU ARE, IN

00:29:02.542 --> 00:29:04.544 line:78%
EFFECT, SUGGESTING THAT YOUR

00:29:03.610 --> 00:29:05.545 line:78%
POSITION IS CERTAINLY DIFFERENT

00:29:04.644 --> 00:29:09.516 line:78%
THAN IF A UNITED STATES ATTORNEY

00:29:05.645 --> 00:29:10.583 line:78%
WERE PROSECUTING THIS CASE.

00:29:09.616 --> 00:29:15.755 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR.

00:29:10.684 --> 00:29:22.762 line:78%
I THINK WE HAVE WHAT MIGHT BE

00:29:15.855 --> 00:29:23.763 line:78%
TERMED A QUASI-INDEPENDENT

00:29:22.862 --> 00:29:26.766 line:78%
STATUS WHERE THEY WERE DELEGATED

00:29:23.863 --> 00:29:27.801 line:78%
TO THIS PARTICULAR OFFICE THE

00:29:26.866 --> 00:29:28.768 line:78%
PERFORMANCE OF CERTAIN FUNCTIONS

00:29:27.901 --> 00:29:30.837 line:78%
AND THERE'S NO REASON WHY THE

00:29:28.868 --> 00:29:32.939 line:78%
PRESIDENT COULDN'T HAVE

00:29:30.937 --> 00:29:33.907 line:78%
DELEGATED THOSE TO US.

00:29:33.039 --> 00:29:34.941 line:78%
AS A MATTER OF FACT, WHEN --

00:29:34.007 --> 00:29:41.081 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. JAWORSKI.

00:29:35.041 --> 00:29:42.048 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES?

00:29:41.181 --> 00:29:43.083 line:78%
&gt;&gt; QUASI-INDEPENDENT IN THE

00:29:42.148 --> 00:29:44.050 line:78%
SENSE OF AN AGENCY?

00:29:43.183 --> 00:29:45.085 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR, FOR INSTANCE, AS A

00:29:44.150 --> 00:29:46.052 line:78%
CONTROL OF CURRENCY.

00:29:45.185 --> 00:29:48.054 line:78%
HE HAS A STATE OF SOMEWHAT

00:29:46.152 --> 00:29:50.056 line:78%
SIMILAR TO THAT.

00:29:48.154 --> 00:29:52.092 line:78%
AND, WE KNOW THAT THERE ARE

00:29:50.156 --> 00:29:54.127 line:78%
SUITS BROUGHT BETWEEN THE

00:29:52.192 --> 00:29:56.162 line:78%
DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE AND THE

00:29:54.227 --> 00:29:57.197 line:78%
CONTROLLER JUST THE OTHER DAY.

00:29:56.262 --> 00:29:58.198 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I AM TROUBLED WITH YOUR

00:29:57.297 --> 00:30:00.200 line:78%
POSITION BEING SIMILAR TO US

00:29:58.298 --> 00:30:01.167 line:78%
ATTORNEY BECAUSE THE US ATTORNEY

00:30:00.300 --> 00:30:02.202 line:78%
IS ABSOLUTELY UNDER THE THUMB OF

00:30:01.267 --> 00:30:03.203 line:78%
THE ATTORNEY GENERAL.

00:30:02.302 --> 00:30:05.238 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I DIDN'T IT.

00:30:03.303 --> 00:30:08.274 line:78%
WHAT I MEANT WAS WE HAD AN

00:30:05.338 --> 00:30:09.209 line:78%
INDEPENDENT STATUS THAT WAS

00:30:08.375 --> 00:30:11.211 line:78%
REALLY DIFFERENT FROM THE STATUS

00:30:09.309 --> 00:30:14.347 line:78%
OF THE UNITED STATES ATTORNEY.

00:30:11.311 --> 00:30:16.349 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I'M SORRY.

00:30:14.447 --> 00:30:18.385 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THOUGHT THAT WAS THE WAY I

00:30:16.449 --> 00:30:19.386 line:78%
ANSWERED THE QUESTION.

00:30:18.485 --> 00:30:20.420 line:78%
NOW, I SHOULD SAY THAT IT'S

00:30:19.486 --> 00:30:21.421 line:78%
INTERESTING WHEN THE CASE OF

00:30:20.520 --> 00:30:22.455 line:78%
NIXON VERSUS SIRICA WAS BEFORE

00:30:21.521 --> 00:30:23.456 line:78%
THE COURT OF APPEALS.

00:30:22.555 --> 00:30:24.457 line:78%
PROFESSOR CHARLES ALAN WRIGHT,

00:30:23.556 --> 00:30:26.526 line:78%
WHO WAS THEN ARGUING THE CASE

00:30:24.557 --> 00:30:27.494 line:78%
AND WHO WAS NOT ON THE ORIGINAL

00:30:26.626 --> 00:30:29.529 line:78%
BRIEF BUT HAVE SERVICED ON THE

00:30:27.594 --> 00:30:34.734 line:78%
REPLY BRIEF FILED ON BEHALF OF

00:30:29.629 --> 00:30:36.603 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT, AT THAT TIME

00:30:34.834 --> 00:30:40.607 line:78%
ARGUED WITH RESPECT TO THE

00:30:36.703 --> 00:30:42.709 line:78%
PARTICULAR OFFICE OF THE SPECIAL

00:30:40.707 --> 00:30:44.744 line:78%
PROSECUTOR.

00:30:42.809 --> 00:30:45.779 line:78%
NOW, IN THIS INSTANCE, WE HAVE A

00:30:44.844 --> 00:30:49.816 line:78%
DIVISION OF FUNCTION WITHIN THE

00:30:45.879 --> 00:30:52.852 line:78%
EXECUTIVE AND THAT MY FRIEND MR.

00:30:49.916 --> 00:30:53.987 line:78%
COX, REFERRING TO MR. ARCHIBALD

00:30:52.952 --> 00:30:54.421 line:78%
COX, HAS BEEN GIVEN ABSOLUTE

00:30:54.087 --> 00:30:55.155 line:78%
INDEPENDENCE.

00:30:54.521 --> 00:30:56.923 line:78%
IT IS FOR HIM TO DECIDE WHOM HE

00:30:55.255 --> 00:30:58.925 line:78%
WILL SEEK TO INDICT.

00:30:57.023 --> 00:31:01.995 line:78%
IT IS FOR HIM TO DECIDE TO WHOM

00:30:59.025 --> 00:31:07.200 line:78%
HE WILL GIVE IMMUNITY, A

00:31:02.095 --> 00:31:11.071 line:78%
DECISION THAT ORDINARILY WOULD

00:31:07.300 --> 00:31:13.106 line:78%
BE MADE AT THE LEVEL OF THE

00:31:11.171 --> 00:31:15.141 line:78%
ATTORNEY GENERAL OR, IN AN

00:31:13.206 --> 00:31:18.178 line:78%
IMPORTANT ENOUGH CASE, AT THE

00:31:15.241 --> 00:31:20.213 line:78%
LEVEL OR THE PRESIDENT.

00:31:18.278 --> 00:31:22.248 line:78%
BUT THE PRESIDENT'S PRESENT

00:31:20.313 --> 00:31:23.283 line:78%
COUNSEL IN HIS MOTION TO QUASH,

00:31:22.349 --> 00:31:25.318 line:78%
AS HE DOES HERE ACCEPT THE WORDS

00:31:23.383 --> 00:31:28.355 line:78%
USED ARE DIFFERENT BUT THE

00:31:25.418 --> 00:31:30.323 line:78%
EFFECT IS THE SAME, IS

00:31:28.455 --> 00:31:32.325 line:78%
CONTENDING TO THE COURT THAT THE

00:31:30.423 --> 00:31:37.530 line:78%
PRESIDENT HAS THE RIGHT TO

00:31:32.425 --> 00:31:41.401 line:78%
DETERMINE WHO, WHEN, AND WITH

00:31:37.630 --> 00:31:48.675 line:78%
WHAT INFORMATION INDIVIDUALS

00:31:41.501 --> 00:31:50.577 line:78%
SHOULD BE PROSECUTED.

00:31:48.775 --> 00:31:52.579 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NIXON VERSUS SIRICA WAS

00:31:50.677 --> 00:31:55.582 line:78%
DIFFERENT, IN THAT, THE PARTIES

00:31:52.679 --> 00:31:56.616 line:78%
THERE WHERE THE GRAND JURY, ON

00:31:55.682 --> 00:31:57.650 line:78%
THE ONE HAND, REPRESENTED TO BE

00:31:56.716 --> 00:31:58.685 line:78%
SURE BY THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR.

00:31:57.751 --> 00:32:01.755 line:78%
BUT THE GRAND JURY, WHICH IS AN

00:31:58.785 --> 00:32:02.756 line:78%
ADJUNCT OF THE JUDICIAL BRANCH

00:32:01.855 --> 00:32:03.690 line:78%
OF GOVERNMENT ON THE ONE HAND,

00:32:02.856 --> 00:32:04.824 line:78%
AND THE CHIEF EXECUTIVE ON THE

00:32:03.790 --> 00:32:05.792 line:78%
OTHER.

00:32:04.924 --> 00:32:06.826 line:78%
AND HERE, NOW THAT AN INDICTMENT

00:32:05.892 --> 00:32:07.794 line:78%
HAS BEEN RETURNED, THE TWO

00:32:06.926 --> 00:32:09.863 line:78%
PARTIES ARE BOTH MEMBERS OF THE

00:32:07.894 --> 00:32:11.831 line:78%
EXECUTIVE BRANCH.

00:32:09.963 --> 00:32:13.867 line:78%
ISN'T THAT CORRECT THAT THERE IS

00:32:11.931 --> 00:32:15.869 line:78%
THAT DIFFERENCE?

00:32:13.967 --> 00:32:30.016 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, BUT THE INDEPENDENT --

00:32:15.969 --> 00:32:31.017 line:78%
YES, SIR, THAT IS CORRECT BUT I

00:32:30.116 --> 00:32:31.985 line:78%
DON'T THINK IT'S A DISTINCTION

00:32:31.117 --> 00:32:33.053 line:78%
AS TO THE SUBSTANTIVE RIGHT --

00:32:32.085 --> 00:32:34.054 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOW, YOU ARE A MEMBER.

00:32:33.153 --> 00:32:37.057 line:78%
YOU'RE UNITED STATES AND THE

00:32:34.154 --> 00:32:38.091 line:78%
PEOPLE OF UNITED STATES, WHOM

00:32:37.157 --> 00:32:47.200 line:78%
YOU REPRESENT.

00:32:38.191 --> 00:32:48.234 line:78%
YOU ARE NOT A MEMBER OF THE

00:32:47.300 --> 00:32:49.269 line:78%
JUDICIAL BRANCH UNLIKE THE GRAND

00:32:48.335 --> 00:32:50.270 line:78%
JURY IN NIXON AGAINST SIRICA.

00:32:49.369 --> 00:32:51.338 line:78%
YOU'RE A MEMBER OF THE EXECUTIVE

00:32:50.370 --> 00:32:51.604 line:78%
BRANCH OF GOVERNMENT, ARE YOU

00:32:51.438 --> 00:32:52.339 line:78%
NOT?

00:32:51.705 --> 00:32:53.239 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR, YES.

00:32:52.439 --> 00:32:54.207 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THERE IS THAT DIFFERENCE.

00:32:53.340 --> 00:32:55.275 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THERE IS THAT DIFFERENCE,

00:32:54.307 --> 00:32:56.276 line:78%
YES, BUT --

00:32:55.375 --> 00:32:57.277 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT MIGHT BE A CRUCIAL

00:32:56.376 --> 00:32:58.445 line:78%
DIFFERENCE, WAS IT NOT?

00:32:57.377 --> 00:32:59.112 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I DON'T THINK THAT THE

00:32:58.545 --> 00:33:00.280 line:78%
DESCRIPTION TO WHICH I HAVE

00:32:59.212 --> 00:33:01.348 line:78%
POINTED AS TO THE INDEPENDENT

00:33:00.380 --> 00:33:03.383 line:78%
STATUS OF THE INDEPENDENT

00:33:01.448 --> 00:33:04.317 line:78%
EXECUTOR WOULD BE DIFFERENT IN

00:33:03.483 --> 00:33:05.352 line:78%
THE SIRICA CASE AS IT WOULD BE

00:33:04.417 --> 00:33:08.355 line:78%
IN THIS CASE.

00:33:05.452 --> 00:33:09.422 line:78%
AND, I WAS BARELY --

00:33:08.455 --> 00:33:10.423 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO.

00:33:09.522 --> 00:33:12.392 line:78%
YOU'RE, IF ANYTHING, MORE

00:33:10.523 --> 00:33:14.427 line:78%
INDEPENDENT THAN MR. COX WAS

00:33:12.492 --> 00:33:15.428 line:78%
UNDER THE REGULATION.

00:33:14.527 --> 00:33:17.430 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR.

00:33:15.528 --> 00:33:18.365 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT THAT DOESN'T REALLY GO TO

00:33:17.530 --> 00:33:21.401 line:78%
THE QUESTION THAT I RAISED.

00:33:18.465 --> 00:33:24.504 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

00:33:21.501 --> 00:33:26.506 line:78%
I REALIZE THAT.

00:33:24.604 --> 00:33:28.508 line:78%
NOW MAY I, HOWEVER, INDICATE

00:33:26.606 --> 00:33:29.509 line:78%
VERY BRIEFLY, AND I KNOW THIS IS

00:33:28.608 --> 00:33:31.578 line:78%
AN IMPORTANT QUESTION BUT I DO

00:33:29.609 --> 00:33:33.580 line:78%
FEEL THAT THE FACTS OUGHT TO BE

00:33:31.678 --> 00:33:35.582 line:78%
BEFORE THE COURT IN DETAIL,

00:33:33.680 --> 00:33:36.583 line:78%
INDICATE JUST WHAT DID TRANSPIRE

00:33:35.682 --> 00:33:39.586 line:78%
WITH RESPECT TO HOW THESE

00:33:36.683 --> 00:33:41.654 line:78%
PARTICULAR REGULATIONS, THIS

00:33:39.686 --> 00:33:45.658 line:78%
ORDER, WAS INTERPRETED BY THE

00:33:41.755 --> 00:33:48.661 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S ACTING ATTORNEY

00:33:45.759 --> 00:33:51.665 line:78%
GENERAL AND ALSO BY THE ATTORNEY

00:33:48.762 --> 00:33:52.666 line:78%
GENERAL DESIGNATE AND ALSO BY

00:33:51.765 --> 00:33:54.601 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT, HIMSELF, AND BY

00:33:52.766 --> 00:33:58.672 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT'S CHIEF OF STAFF,

00:33:54.701 --> 00:34:02.709 line:78%
GENERAL HAIG.

00:33:58.772 --> 00:34:06.780 line:78%
MR. BORK, IN HEARINGS AT A TIME

00:34:02.809 --> 00:34:07.747 line:78%
WHEN CONGRESS WAS PRESSING THE

00:34:06.880 --> 00:34:09.849 line:78%
BILL OF AN INDEPENDENT SPECIAL

00:34:07.847 --> 00:34:10.817 line:78%
PROSECUTOR, TESTIFIED THAT

00:34:09.949 --> 00:34:11.885 line:78%
"ALTHOUGH IT IS ANTICIPATED THAT

00:34:10.917 --> 00:34:13.853 line:78%
MR. JAWORSKI WILL RECEIVE

00:34:11.985 --> 00:34:20.860 line:78%
COOPERATION FROM THE WHITE HOUSE

00:34:13.953 --> 00:34:26.933 line:78%
IN GETTING ANY EVIDENCE HE

00:34:20.960 --> 00:34:29.903 line:78%
FEELS, HE NEEDS TO CONDUCT

00:34:27.033 --> 00:34:33.973 line:78%
INVESTIGATIONS FROM

00:34:30.003 --> 00:34:36.976 line:78%
PROSECUTIONS."

00:34:34.074 --> 00:34:38.978 line:78%
IT IS CLEAR AND UNDERSTOOD ON

00:34:37.077 --> 00:34:39.946 line:78%
ALL SIDES THAT HE HAS HE POWER

00:34:39.079 --> 00:34:43.016 line:78%
TO USE JUDICIAL PROCESSES TO

00:34:40.046 --> 00:34:44.050 line:78%
PURSUE EVIDENCE IF DISAGREEMENT

00:34:43.116 --> 00:34:46.119 line:78%
SHOULD DEVELOP.

00:34:44.150 --> 00:34:47.020 line:78%
IT WAS FURTHER POINTED OUT --

00:34:46.219 --> 00:34:49.122 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU'RE QUOTING FROM WHOM AND

00:34:47.120 --> 00:34:50.190 line:78%
WHAT --

00:34:49.222 --> 00:34:52.192 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ACTING ATTORNEY GENERAL

00:34:50.290 --> 00:34:53.226 line:78%
BORK'S TESTIMONY IN THE HOUSE.

00:34:52.292 --> 00:34:54.194 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND IN WHAT OCCASION?

00:34:53.326 --> 00:34:55.195 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AFTER I HAVE BEEN APPOINTED

00:34:54.294 --> 00:34:56.196 line:78%
AND IN CONNECTION WITH THE

00:34:55.295 --> 00:34:57.230 line:78%
HEARINGS ON THE BILL TO

00:34:56.296 --> 00:34:59.165 line:78%
ESTABLISH AN INDEPENDENT

00:34:57.330 --> 00:35:00.367 line:78%
PROSECUTOR BY CONGRESSIONAL ACT.

00:34:59.265 --> 00:35:01.034 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU.

00:35:00.467 --> 00:35:01.735 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THEN, HE FURTHER SAID, I

00:35:01.134 --> 00:35:02.469 line:78%
UNDERSTAND AND IT IS CLEAR TO

00:35:01.835 --> 00:35:03.203 line:78%
ME, THAT "MR. JAWORSKI CAN GO TO

00:35:02.569 --> 00:35:04.237 line:78%
COURT AND TEST OUT," AND THESE

00:35:03.303 --> 00:35:05.238 line:78%
ARE THE IMPORTANT WORDS, "AND

00:35:04.337 --> 00:35:06.239 line:78%
TEST OUT ANY REFUSAL TO PRODUCE

00:35:05.338 --> 00:35:07.307 line:78%
DOCUMENTS ON THE GROUNDS OF

00:35:06.339 --> 00:35:08.308 line:78%
CONFIDENTIALITY."

00:35:07.407 --> 00:35:10.343 line:78%
AND ATTORNEY GENERAL SAXBE, THEN

00:35:08.408 --> 00:35:11.378 line:78%
A DESIGNATE WHO WAS ALSO PRESENT

00:35:10.443 --> 00:35:13.380 line:78%
AT THE TIME THAT THIS MATTER WAS

00:35:11.478 --> 00:35:14.381 line:78%
DISCUSSED AND AT THE TIME THAT I

00:35:13.480 --> 00:35:15.382 line:78%
ACCEPTED THE RESPONSIBILITIES,

00:35:14.481 --> 00:35:17.417 line:78%
TESTIFIED THAT I HAD THE RIGHT

00:35:15.482 --> 00:35:20.420 line:78%
TO CONTEST AN ASSERTION OF

00:35:17.517 --> 00:35:22.389 line:78%
EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE AND STATED

00:35:20.520 --> 00:35:23.423 line:78%
THAT I CAN GO TO COURT AT ANY

00:35:22.489 --> 00:35:27.460 line:78%
TIME TO DETERMINE THAT.

00:35:23.523 --> 00:35:31.498 line:78%
NOW THE PRESIDENT HIMSELF, AS WE

00:35:27.560 --> 00:35:33.500 line:78%
POINT OUT IN OUR BRIEF, IN

00:35:31.598 --> 00:35:38.705 line:78%
ANNOUNCING THE APPOINTMENT OF A

00:35:33.600 --> 00:35:42.609 line:78%
NEW INDEPENDENT PROSECUTOR,

00:35:38.805 --> 00:35:43.576 line:78%
STATED TO THE NATION THAT HE HAD

00:35:42.709 --> 00:35:45.578 line:78%
NO GREATER INTEREST THAN TO SEE

00:35:43.677 --> 00:35:47.614 line:78%
THAT THE NEW SPECIAL PROSECUTOR

00:35:45.679 --> 00:35:48.682 line:78%
HAS THE COOPERATION FROM THE

00:35:47.714 --> 00:35:52.686 line:78%
EXECUTIVE BRANCH AND THE

00:35:48.782 --> 00:35:55.755 line:78%
INDEPENDENCE THAT HE NEEDS TO

00:35:52.786 --> 00:35:58.825 line:78%
BRING ABOUT THAT CONCLUSION OF

00:35:55.855 --> 00:35:59.826 line:78%
THE WATERGATE INVESTIGATION.

00:35:58.925 --> 00:36:01.828 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT'S CHIEF OF STAFF,

00:35:59.926 --> 00:36:03.830 line:78%
AT THE TIME THAT THIS

00:36:01.928 --> 00:36:04.864 line:78%
APPOINTMENT WAS ACCEPTED AND AT

00:36:03.930 --> 00:36:10.036 line:78%
THE TIME THAT THE NEW

00:36:04.964 --> 00:36:11.971 line:78%
REGULATIONS WERE THEN DRAFTED BY

00:36:10.136 --> 00:36:14.007 line:78%
THE ACTING ATTORNEY GENERAL, HAD

00:36:12.072 --> 00:36:16.009 line:78%
ASSURED ME, AND THIS IS A PART

00:36:14.107 --> 00:36:18.078 line:78%
OF THE RECORD, BECAUSE A LETTER

00:36:16.109 --> 00:36:20.080 line:78%
WAS WRITTEN AT THE REQUEST OF

00:36:18.178 --> 00:36:21.114 line:78%
SENATOR HUGH SCOTT TO THE WHITE

00:36:20.180 --> 00:36:23.116 line:78%
HOUSE AS A RESULT OF DISCUSSIONS

00:36:21.214 --> 00:36:27.120 line:78%
THAT HE HAD WITH GENERAL HAIG IN

00:36:23.216 --> 00:36:29.189 line:78%
WHICH I SENT A COPY OF THE

00:36:27.220 --> 00:36:32.258 line:78%
TESTIMONY THAT I HAD GIVEN TO

00:36:29.289 --> 00:36:36.329 line:78%
THE CONGRESSIONAL COMMITTEES, TO

00:36:32.359 --> 00:36:40.400 line:78%
THE WHITE HOUSE SO IT WOULD

00:36:36.429 --> 00:36:43.370 line:78%
FULLY BE AWARE OF IT AND THE

00:36:40.500 --> 00:36:47.374 line:78%
RECEIPT OF IT WAS ACKNOWLEDGED

00:36:43.470 --> 00:36:50.477 line:78%
WITHOUT ANY CHANGE IN THE

00:36:47.474 --> 00:36:52.479 line:78%
TESTIMONY.

00:36:50.577 --> 00:36:56.516 line:78%
SO, I HAD BEEN ASSURED OF THE

00:36:52.579 --> 00:36:58.518 line:78%
RIGHT TO JUDICIAL PROCESS AND BY

00:36:56.616 --> 00:37:00.520 line:78%
HIM AFTER HE HAD REVIEWED THE

00:36:58.618 --> 00:37:05.692 line:78%
MATTER WITH THE PRESIDENT AND HE

00:37:00.620 --> 00:37:06.559 line:78%
CAME AND TOLD ME THAT I WOULD

00:37:05.792 --> 00:37:11.765 line:78%
HAVE THE RIGHT TO TAKE THE

00:37:06.659 --> 00:37:13.633 line:78%
PRESIDENT TO COURT, AND THAT

00:37:11.865 --> 00:37:17.704 line:78%
THESE WERE THE KEY WORDS IN THIS

00:37:13.733 --> 00:37:19.773 line:78%
ARRANGEMENT, AND THAT THE RIGHT

00:37:17.804 --> 00:37:23.843 line:78%
WOULD NOT BE QUESTIONED.

00:37:19.873 --> 00:37:24.844 line:78%
OF COURSE, THIS INDEPENDENCE WAS

00:37:23.943 --> 00:37:25.812 line:78%
GIVEN TO THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR.

00:37:24.944 --> 00:37:26.846 line:78%
ACTUALLY, IT WAS BUT AN ECHO OF

00:37:25.912 --> 00:37:27.881 line:78%
PUBLIC DEMAND.

00:37:26.946 --> 00:37:28.882 line:78%
AND, IF I MAY BE PERMITTED TO

00:37:27.981 --> 00:37:30.083 line:78%
SAY SO, IT WAS THE ONLY BASIS ON

00:37:28.982 --> 00:37:30.717 line:78%
WHICH, AFTER WHAT HAD OCCURRED

00:37:30.183 --> 00:37:31.451 line:78%
AND A PREDECESSOR HAD BEEN

00:37:30.817 --> 00:37:32.152 line:78%
DISCHARGED, IT WAS ON A BASIS ON

00:37:31.551 --> 00:37:32.952 line:78%
WHICH THAT SPECIAL PROSECUTOR

00:37:32.252 --> 00:37:33.953 line:78%
COULD HAVE FELT THAT HE COULD

00:37:33.053 --> 00:37:34.954 line:78%
COME AND SERVE AND UNDERTAKE TO

00:37:34.054 --> 00:37:36.022 line:78%
PERFORM THESE FUNCTIONS.

00:37:35.055 --> 00:37:37.023 line:78%
IT'S IMPORTANT, I THINK, TO

00:37:36.122 --> 00:37:38.024 line:78%
OBSERVE THAT THE COUNSEL FOR THE

00:37:37.123 --> 00:37:40.060 line:78%
PRESIDENT IN HIS BRIEF, BY

00:37:38.124 --> 00:37:41.094 line:78%
ACCEPTING THE PROPOSITION THAT

00:37:40.160 --> 00:37:42.062 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT AND THE ATTORNEY

00:37:41.194 --> 00:37:43.129 line:78%
GENERAL CAN DELEGATE CERTAIN

00:37:42.162 --> 00:37:44.097 line:78%
EXECUTIVE FUNCTIONS TO

00:37:43.229 --> 00:37:45.098 line:78%
SUBORDINATE OFFICERS, IMPLICITLY

00:37:44.197 --> 00:37:46.099 line:78%
HAS CONCEDED, SO WE THINK, THE

00:37:45.198 --> 00:37:47.133 line:78%
VALIDITY OF THE REGULATIONS

00:37:46.199 --> 00:37:48.168 line:78%
DELEGATING PROSECUTORIAL POWERS

00:37:47.233 --> 00:37:49.336 line:78%
TO THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR.

00:37:48.268 --> 00:37:50.070 line:78%
THE REGULATIONS SPECIFICALLY

00:37:49.436 --> 00:37:51.204 line:78%
PROVIDE, AS YOU WILL NOTICE FROM

00:37:50.170 --> 00:37:52.272 line:78%
THE APPENDIX AND WE HAVE SET

00:37:51.304 --> 00:37:53.273 line:78%
THEM OUT, THAT THE ATTORNEY

00:37:52.372 --> 00:37:54.274 line:78%
GENERAL WILL NOT COUNTERMAN OR

00:37:53.373 --> 00:37:56.242 line:78%
INTERFERE WITH THE SPECIAL

00:37:54.374 --> 00:37:57.310 line:78%
PROSECUTOR'S DECISIONS OR

00:37:56.343 --> 00:37:58.244 line:78%
ACTIONS.

00:37:57.410 --> 00:38:00.480 line:78%
THIS IS ALSO A PART OF THE

00:37:58.345 --> 00:38:01.181 line:78%
CHARTER.

00:38:00.580 --> 00:38:01.815 line:78%
JUST TO ARGUE AS HAS BEEN DONE

00:38:01.281 --> 00:38:02.515 line:78%
IN THESE BRIEFS, THAT THE

00:38:01.915 --> 00:38:03.350 line:78%
SEPARATION OF POWERS PRECLUDES

00:38:02.615 --> 00:38:05.352 line:78%
THE COURTS FROM ENTERTAINING

00:38:03.450 --> 00:38:06.319 line:78%
THIS ACTION BECAUSE IT IS THE

00:38:05.452 --> 00:38:07.354 line:78%
EXCLUSIVE PREROGATIVE OF THE

00:38:06.419 --> 00:38:09.356 line:78%
EXECUTIVE BRANCH, NOT THE

00:38:07.454 --> 00:38:10.390 line:78%
JUDICIARY, TO DETERMINE WHOM TO

00:38:09.456 --> 00:38:12.392 line:78%
PROSECUTE, ON WHAT CHARGES, AND

00:38:10.490 --> 00:38:16.463 line:78%
WITH WHAT EVIDENCE, WE THINK,

00:38:12.492 --> 00:38:17.530 line:78%
MISSES THE POINT.

00:38:16.563 --> 00:38:18.531 line:78%
WHAT HAS EVOLVED FROM THE

00:38:17.630 --> 00:38:19.499 line:78%
REGULATIONS, IN OUR VIEW, IS A

00:38:18.631 --> 00:38:23.636 line:78%
PROSECUTORIAL FORCE WITH CERTAIN

00:38:19.599 --> 00:38:26.606 line:78%
EXCLUSIVE RESPONSIBILITIES.

00:38:23.737 --> 00:38:27.640 line:78%
AND THIS IS WHY I SAY THAT TO

00:38:26.706 --> 00:38:28.575 line:78%
SOME DEGREE IT COULD BE

00:38:27.741 --> 00:38:29.676 line:78%
DESCRIBED AS A QUASI-INDEPENDENT

00:38:28.675 --> 00:38:30.677 line:78%
AGENCY.

00:38:29.776 --> 00:38:32.679 line:78%
IT'S NOT UNLIKE OUR SITUATION AS

00:38:30.777 --> 00:38:34.714 line:78%
THE CASE WE ALLUDED TO A FEW

00:38:32.779 --> 00:38:35.782 line:78%
MINUTES AGO, DECIDED BY THE

00:38:34.814 --> 00:38:36.783 line:78%
COURT JUST A WEEK OR SO AGO.

00:38:35.882 --> 00:38:37.751 line:78%
IT'S NOT UNLIKE THE CASE OF THE

00:38:36.883 --> 00:38:39.786 line:78%
SECRETARY OF AGRICULTURE VERSUS

00:38:37.851 --> 00:38:40.820 line:78%
THE UNITED STATES.

00:38:39.886 --> 00:38:41.821 line:78%
THIS IS THE FIRST TIME THAT

00:38:40.920 --> 00:38:43.823 line:78%
THERE HAS BEEN AN ACTION BROUGHT

00:38:41.921 --> 00:38:45.825 line:78%
BY ONE MEMBER OF THE EXECUTIVE

00:38:43.923 --> 00:38:51.031 line:78%
BRANCH AGAINST ANOTHER OFFICIAL

00:38:45.925 --> 00:38:53.833 line:78%
IN THE EXECUTIVE BRANCH.

00:38:51.131 --> 00:38:55.835 line:78%
AND, WE REFER TO THESE CASES IN

00:38:53.933 --> 00:38:56.870 line:78%
OUR BRIEFS IN DETAIL.

00:38:55.935 --> 00:38:57.837 line:78%
NOW, I WANT TO MAKE IT CLEAR

00:38:56.970 --> 00:38:58.872 line:78%
THAT THE PRESIDENT, AT NO POINT

00:38:57.937 --> 00:38:59.839 line:78%
OF COURSE, DELEGATED TO THE

00:38:58.972 --> 00:39:05.045 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR THE EXCLUSIVE

00:38:59.939 --> 00:39:06.980 line:78%
RIGHT TO PASS ON THE QUESTION OF

00:39:05.145 --> 00:39:08.948 line:78%
EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE OR ANY OTHER

00:39:07.080 --> 00:39:10.950 line:78%
PRIVILEGE, ATTORNEY-INCLINED

00:39:09.049 --> 00:39:14.020 line:78%
PRIVILEGE, OR ANY OTHER

00:39:11.051 --> 00:39:16.089 line:78%
TESTIMONIAL PRIVILEGE.

00:39:14.120 --> 00:39:19.125 line:78%
WHAT WE ARE MERELY SAYING IS

00:39:16.189 --> 00:39:23.096 line:78%
THAT WE HAVE THE CLEAR RIGHT TO

00:39:19.225 --> 00:39:28.335 line:78%
TEST IT IN THIS COURT, AND THIS

00:39:23.196 --> 00:39:29.202 line:78%
IS ON WHAT WE STAND.

00:39:28.435 --> 00:39:32.172 line:78%
WELL BECAUSE OF THE PASSAGE OF

00:39:29.302 --> 00:39:34.174 line:78%
TIME, IF I MAY, I THINK I SHOULD

00:39:32.272 --> 00:39:35.141 line:78%
GET TO OTHER DISCUSSIONS UNLESS

00:39:34.274 --> 00:39:36.176 line:78%
THERE ARE QUESTIONS ON THIS

00:39:35.241 --> 00:39:37.177 line:78%
PARTICULAR POINT.

00:39:36.276 --> 00:39:40.280 line:78%
PASSING TO THE MERITS, WE WOULD

00:39:37.277 --> 00:39:41.314 line:78%
SAY THAT IF THERE IS ANY ONE

00:39:40.380 --> 00:39:43.483 line:78%
PRINCIPLE OF LAW THAT MARBURY

00:39:41.414 --> 00:39:44.150 line:78%
VERSUS MADISON CITES, IT IS THAT

00:39:43.583 --> 00:39:44.851 line:78%
IT IS UP TO THE COURT TO SAY

00:39:44.250 --> 00:39:48.388 line:78%
WHAT THE LAW IS AND ALMOST TO

00:39:44.951 --> 00:39:50.423 line:78%
THE POINT OF REDUNDANCY BUT

00:39:48.488 --> 00:39:52.492 line:78%
NECESSARY BECAUSE IT WAS A

00:39:50.523 --> 00:39:54.461 line:78%
LANDMARK DECISION.

00:39:52.592 --> 00:39:55.495 line:78%
CHIEF JUSTICE MARSHALL REASONED,

00:39:54.561 --> 00:39:56.496 line:78%
WE THINK, WITH CLARITY AND

00:39:55.595 --> 00:39:57.464 line:78%
EMPHASIS THAT IT IS EMPHATICALLY

00:39:56.596 --> 00:39:58.398 line:78%
THE PROVINCE AND THE DUTY OF THE

00:39:57.564 --> 00:40:12.545 line:78%
JUDICIAL DEPARTMENT TO SAY WHAT

00:39:58.498 --> 00:40:13.546 line:78%
THE LAW IS.

00:40:12.645 --> 00:40:14.581 line:78%
AND THIS COURT OF COURSE,

00:40:13.646 --> 00:40:16.516 line:78%
THROUGH THE YEARS, HAS

00:40:14.681 --> 00:40:17.584 line:78%
REAFFIRMED CONSISTENTLY APPLIED

00:40:16.616 --> 00:40:18.618 line:78%
THAT RULE.

00:40:17.684 --> 00:40:19.652 line:78%
IT'S DONE IT IN A NUMBER OF

00:40:18.718 --> 00:40:20.653 line:78%
CASES, IN POWELL VERSUS

00:40:19.753 --> 00:40:22.655 line:78%
MCCORMACK, IN THE YOUNGSTOWN

00:40:20.754 --> 00:40:33.867 line:78%
STEEL SEIZURE CASE, AND DOE

00:40:22.756 --> 00:40:34.868 line:78%
VERSUS MCMILLAN.

00:40:33.967 --> 00:40:35.835 line:78%
AND A FOOTNOTE, I THINK A VERY

00:40:34.968 --> 00:40:36.836 line:78%
IMPORTANT ONE, APPEARS IN THAT

00:40:35.935 --> 00:40:39.839 line:78%
OPINION WHEN MR. JUSTICE WHITE

00:40:36.936 --> 00:40:40.874 line:78%
POINTED OUT THAT WHILE AN

00:40:39.939 --> 00:40:42.976 line:78%
INQUIRY SUCH AS INVOLVED IN A

00:40:40.974 --> 00:40:43.977 line:78%
PRESENT CASE, BECAUSE IT

00:40:43.076 --> 00:40:45.011 line:78%
INVOLVES TWO COORDINATE BRANCHES

00:40:44.077 --> 00:40:45.979 line:78%
OF GOVERNMENT, MUST NECESSARILY

00:40:45.111 --> 00:40:53.253 line:78%
HAVE SEPARATION OF POWER

00:40:46.079 --> 00:40:54.120 line:78%
IMPLICATIONS.

00:40:53.353 --> 00:40:55.155 line:78%
THE SEPARATION OF POWERS

00:40:54.220 --> 00:40:56.189 line:78%
DOCTRINE HAS NOT PREVIOUSLY

00:40:55.255 --> 00:40:58.224 line:78%
PREVENTED THIS COURT FROM

00:40:56.289 --> 00:40:59.225 line:78%
REVIEWING THE ACTS OF CONGRESS

00:40:58.324 --> 00:41:00.193 line:78%
EVEN WHEN, IT IS POINTED OUT,

00:40:59.325 --> 00:41:02.295 line:78%
THE EXECUTIVE BRANCH IS ALSO

00:41:00.293 --> 00:41:03.229 line:78%
INVOLVED.

00:41:02.395 --> 00:41:06.333 line:78%
NOW, THERE ARE A NUMBER OF CASES

00:41:03.329 --> 00:41:07.334 line:78%
THAT SPEAK TO THAT.

00:41:06.433 --> 00:41:08.368 line:78%
I THINK ONE OF THE CASES THAT

00:41:07.434 --> 00:41:09.402 line:78%
WENT INTO GREATER DETAIL AND

00:41:08.468 --> 00:41:11.404 line:78%
ALSO POINTS OUT QUITE A

00:41:09.502 --> 00:41:13.406 line:78%
DISTINGUISHING FEATURE IS THE

00:41:11.504 --> 00:41:14.407 line:78%
GRAVEL CASE WHERE AS, IN THE

00:41:13.506 --> 00:41:16.443 line:78%
GRAVEL CASE, THE COURT DID HOLD

00:41:14.507 --> 00:41:18.478 line:78%
THAT IT WAS APPROPRIATE TO GO

00:41:16.543 --> 00:41:19.479 line:78%
INTO CERTAIN MATTERS WHERE A

00:41:18.578 --> 00:41:20.413 line:78%
PRIVILEGE HAD BEEN EXERCISED ON

00:41:19.579 --> 00:41:28.555 line:78%
A PART OF A SENATOR ON BEHALF OF

00:41:20.513 --> 00:41:32.559 line:78%
HIS AID.

00:41:28.655 --> 00:41:34.561 line:78%
THERE ARE TWO THINGS THAT I

00:41:32.659 --> 00:41:35.628 line:78%
BELIEVE CLEARLY HELP US IN THAT

00:41:34.661 --> 00:41:36.629 line:78%
DECISION AND ALSO OTHER

00:41:35.729 --> 00:41:47.774 line:78%
DECISIONS AS FAR AS THE

00:41:36.730 --> 00:41:48.808 line:78%
QUESTIONS HERE ARE INVOLVED.

00:41:47.874 --> 00:41:50.844 line:78%
ONE IS THAT THE SPEECH OR DEBATE

00:41:48.908 --> 00:41:51.845 line:78%
CLAUSE IS IN THE CONSTITUTION,

00:41:50.944 --> 00:41:58.852 line:78%
AS IS THE JOURNAL CLAUSE.

00:41:51.945 --> 00:41:59.886 line:78%
IT'S IN THE CONSTITUTION.

00:41:58.952 --> 00:42:00.920 line:78%
IT'S WRITTEN IN THERE.

00:41:59.986 --> 00:42:01.888 line:78%
AND, THIS IS WHAT WAS INVOKED.

00:42:01.021 --> 00:42:02.889 line:78%
I DON'T FIND ANYTHING WRITTEN IN

00:42:01.988 --> 00:42:04.924 line:78%
THE CONSTITUTION AND NOTHING HAS

00:42:02.989 --> 00:42:05.992 line:78%
BEEN POINTED THAT IS A WRITING

00:42:05.025 --> 00:42:09.029 line:78%
IN THE CONSTITUTION THAT RELATES

00:42:06.092 --> 00:42:10.030 line:78%
TO THE RIGHT OF THE EXERCISE OF

00:42:09.129 --> 00:42:12.132 line:78%
EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE ON THE PART

00:42:10.130 --> 00:42:13.166 line:78%
OF THE PRESIDENT.

00:42:12.232 --> 00:42:15.168 line:78%
ANOTHER VERY IMPORTANT THING

00:42:13.266 --> 00:42:17.203 line:78%
THAT'S POINTED OUT IN THAT CASE

00:42:15.268 --> 00:42:20.173 line:78%
IS THAT IT DID INVOLVE AN

00:42:17.303 --> 00:42:21.207 line:78%
EXAMINATION INTO WRONGDOING ON

00:42:20.273 --> 00:42:25.211 line:78%
THAT PART OF THOSE WHO WERE

00:42:21.307 --> 00:42:27.313 line:78%
SEEKING TO INVOKE THE PRIVILEGE.

00:42:25.311 --> 00:42:34.387 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IS THE TERM "EXECUTIVE

00:42:27.414 --> 00:42:35.388 line:78%
PRIVILEGE" AN ANCIENT ONE?

00:42:34.487 --> 00:42:36.389 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I BEG YOUR PARDON, SIR?

00:42:35.488 --> 00:42:37.390 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IS THE TERM "EXECUTIVE

00:42:36.489 --> 00:42:38.324 line:78%
PRIVILEGE" AN ANCIENT ONE?

00:42:37.490 --> 00:42:39.426 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT HAS BEEN USED OVER A

00:42:38.425 --> 00:42:41.461 line:78%
PERIOD OF TIME.

00:42:39.526 --> 00:42:43.396 line:78%
HOW ANCIENT, MR. JUSTICE

00:42:41.561 --> 00:42:44.464 line:78%
BRENNAN, I'M NOT IN POSITION TO

00:42:43.496 --> 00:42:46.533 line:78%
SAY.

00:42:44.564 --> 00:42:48.535 line:78%
BUT, CERTAINLY, IT HAS BEEN ONE

00:42:46.633 --> 00:42:49.536 line:78%
THAT'S BEEN USED OVER THE YEARS

00:42:48.635 --> 00:42:51.571 line:78%
BUT IT IS NOT ONE THAT I FIND IT

00:42:49.636 --> 00:42:52.572 line:78%
A BASIS FOR IN THE CONSTITUTION.

00:42:51.671 --> 00:42:53.540 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ARE YOU, NOW, ARGUING THAT

00:42:52.672 --> 00:42:54.541 line:78%
THERE IS NO SUCH THING AS

00:42:53.640 --> 00:42:55.575 line:78%
EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE.

00:42:54.641 --> 00:42:56.609 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR.

00:42:55.675 --> 00:42:57.711 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I DIDN'T THINK SO.

00:42:56.710 --> 00:42:58.244 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR, BUT I SAID IT HAD NO

00:42:57.811 --> 00:42:58.778 line:78%
BASIS FOR IT IN THE

00:42:58.345 --> 00:42:59.646 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONS BUT --

00:42:58.878 --> 00:43:00.613 line:78%
&gt;&gt; DO YOU THINK, IF ANYTHING,

00:42:59.746 --> 00:43:01.815 line:78%
IT'S A COMMON LAW PRIVILEGE?

00:43:00.714 --> 00:43:02.482 line:78%
IS THAT YOUR POINT?

00:43:01.915 --> 00:43:03.216 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR, AND THAT IT HAS

00:43:02.582 --> 00:43:03.950 line:78%
BEEN JUDICIALLY RECOGNIZED, AND

00:43:03.316 --> 00:43:04.718 line:78%
APPROPRIATELY SO, IN A NUMBER OF

00:43:04.050 --> 00:43:05.785 line:78%
CASES.

00:43:04.818 --> 00:43:06.786 line:78%
AS WE SEE IT, WE DO NOT THINK

00:43:05.885 --> 00:43:10.824 line:78%
THAT IT IS AN APPROPRIATE ONE IN

00:43:06.886 --> 00:43:12.859 line:78%
THIS CASE BUT WE CERTAINLY DO

00:43:10.924 --> 00:43:16.863 line:78%
NOT, FOR A MOMENT, FEEL THAT IT

00:43:12.959 --> 00:43:19.899 line:78%
HAS ANY CONSTITUTIONAL FACE.

00:43:16.963 --> 00:43:21.935 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN SAWYER AGAINST ROSE I

00:43:20.000 --> 00:43:25.972 line:78%
THOUGHT WE HELD THAT THERE IS A

00:43:22.035 --> 00:43:26.940 line:78%
COMMON LAW PRIVILEGE IN THE

00:43:26.072 --> 00:43:28.041 line:78%
EXECUTIVES DEALING AT THE STATE

00:43:27.040 --> 00:43:28.942 line:78%
LEVEL, BUT THAT IT IS A

00:43:28.141 --> 00:43:31.011 line:78%
QUALIFIED PRIVILEGE, IS THAT NOT

00:43:29.042 --> 00:43:31.978 line:78%
SO?

00:43:31.111 --> 00:43:33.046 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. CHIEF JUSTICE, THAT IS

00:43:32.078 --> 00:43:35.048 line:78%
EXACTLY THE POINT.

00:43:33.146 --> 00:43:37.083 line:78%
THIS COURT HAS EXAMINED A NUMBER

00:43:35.148 --> 00:43:41.154 line:78%
OF SITUATIONS AND IN SOME

00:43:37.183 --> 00:43:42.155 line:78%
SITUATIONS AS, I THINK, WAS

00:43:41.254 --> 00:43:47.160 line:78%
POINTED OUT EARLIER WHERE

00:43:42.255 --> 00:43:54.401 line:78%
MILITARY SECRETS AND SUCH AS

00:43:47.260 --> 00:43:58.438 line:78%
THAT WERE INVOLVED OR NATIONAL

00:43:54.501 --> 00:43:59.406 line:78%
SECRETS OF GREAT IMPORTANCE, THE

00:43:58.538 --> 00:44:00.473 line:78%
COURT HAS TAKEN A GOOD CLOSE

00:43:59.506 --> 00:44:02.409 line:78%
LOOK AND HAS UPHELD PRIVILEGE.

00:44:00.573 --> 00:44:03.376 line:78%
BUT --

00:44:02.509 --> 00:44:04.411 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHEN YOU SAY "HAS TAKEN A

00:44:03.476 --> 00:44:05.445 line:78%
GOOD CLOSE LOOK," WITHOUT

00:44:04.511 --> 00:44:06.546 line:78%
LOOKING AT THE EVIDENCE

00:44:05.545 --> 00:44:07.280 line:78%
SOMETIMES HAS TAKEN A GOOD CLOSE

00:44:06.646 --> 00:44:07.714 line:78%
LOOK AT THE CLAIM AND THE BASIS

00:44:07.380 --> 00:44:08.548 line:78%
OF THE CLAIM.

00:44:07.814 --> 00:44:09.182 line:78%
IS THAT WHAT YOU MEAN?

00:44:08.648 --> 00:44:09.549 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S WHAT I MEAN.

00:44:09.282 --> 00:44:10.483 line:78%
YES, SIR.

00:44:09.649 --> 00:44:11.418 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT HASN'T THIS COURT SAID

00:44:10.583 --> 00:44:12.619 line:78%
THAT IT DID HAVE CONSTITUTIONAL

00:44:11.518 --> 00:44:13.186 line:78%
OVERTONE?

00:44:12.719 --> 00:44:13.887 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT SAID THAT IT HAD

00:44:13.286 --> 00:44:14.688 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL OVERTONES AND I

00:44:13.987 --> 00:44:24.698 line:78%
DON'T KNOW IT MAY HAVE BEEN USED

00:44:14.788 --> 00:44:25.665 line:78%
BUT IT --

00:44:24.798 --> 00:44:26.666 line:78%
&gt;&gt; TORT CLAIMS, I THINK.

00:44:25.765 --> 00:44:30.737 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, BUT IT CERTAINLY HAS

00:44:26.766 --> 00:44:31.738 line:78%
NEVER PLACED IT IN THE

00:44:30.837 --> 00:44:33.740 line:78%
CONSTITUTION, SO FAR AS I'M

00:44:31.838 --> 00:44:34.774 line:78%
AWARE OF, AND PRESIDENT'S

00:44:33.840 --> 00:44:36.843 line:78%
COUNSEL WHO HAVE CAREFULLY

00:44:34.874 --> 00:44:37.844 line:78%
EXAMINED THE AUTHORITIES.

00:44:36.943 --> 00:44:38.778 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT WAS (INAUDIBLE) CHEMICAL

00:44:37.944 --> 00:44:50.790 line:78%
CORPORATION WHO SUPPORTED THE

00:44:38.878 --> 00:44:51.825 line:78%
CLAIMS.

00:44:50.890 --> 00:44:52.859 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES.

00:44:51.925 --> 00:44:53.860 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN THAT GREAT REVIEW.

00:44:52.959 --> 00:44:55.929 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S JUDICIALLY TAILORED?

00:44:53.960 --> 00:45:00.033 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

00:44:56.029 --> 00:45:01.034 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IS IT YOUR VIEW THAT THERE

00:45:00.133 --> 00:45:03.036 line:78%
ARE NO INFERENCES TO BE ARRIVED

00:45:01.134 --> 00:45:09.042 line:78%
FROM THE DOCTRINE OF SEPARATION

00:45:03.136 --> 00:45:10.010 line:78%
OF POWERS OR YOU'RE SAYING THIS

00:45:09.142 --> 00:45:11.077 line:78%
IS PURELY AN EVIDENTIARY

00:45:10.110 --> 00:45:19.152 line:78%
PRIVILEGE?

00:45:11.177 --> 00:45:20.186 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT THE PRIVILEGE, AS

00:45:19.252 --> 00:45:21.221 line:78%
RECOGNIZED JUDICIALLY, MAY HAVE

00:45:20.286 --> 00:45:24.224 line:78%
BEEN TIED INTO THE SEPARATION OF

00:45:21.321 --> 00:45:27.227 line:78%
POWERS DOCTRINE, WE DON'T DENY.

00:45:24.324 --> 00:45:34.267 line:78%
WHAT WE SAY IS THAT SEPARATION

00:45:27.327 --> 00:45:35.268 line:78%
OF POWERS DOCTRINE, IN THE

00:45:34.367 --> 00:45:36.202 line:78%
EXERCISE AND THE CALLING FOR

00:45:35.368 --> 00:45:38.271 line:78%
EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE, HAS NOT

00:45:36.302 --> 00:45:39.272 line:78%
BEEN APPLIED.

00:45:38.371 --> 00:45:42.275 line:78%
IN A NUMBER OF INSTANCES

00:45:39.372 --> 00:45:43.276 line:78%
INVOLVING BOTH CONGRESS AND

00:45:42.375 --> 00:45:45.278 line:78%
INVOLVING ALSO THE EXECUTIVE,

00:45:43.376 --> 00:45:47.280 line:78%
DESPITE THE FACT THAT EVEN IN

00:45:45.378 --> 00:45:49.282 line:78%
CONGRESSIONAL SITUATIONS, SPEECH

00:45:47.380 --> 00:45:50.283 line:78%
AND DEBATE CLAUSE IS THERE.

00:45:49.382 --> 00:45:51.251 line:78%
WHAT I AM SAYING IS THAT THE

00:45:50.383 --> 00:45:52.285 line:78%
SEPARATION OF POWERS DOCTRINE,

00:45:51.351 --> 00:45:53.486 line:78%
AS WAS POINTED TO IN THE DOE

00:45:52.385 --> 00:45:54.187 line:78%
VERSUS MCMILLAN CASE, HAS NOT

00:45:53.586 --> 00:45:54.888 line:78%
BEEN PERMITTED TO STAND IN THE

00:45:54.287 --> 00:45:55.622 line:78%
WAY OF THIS COURT EXAMINING IT

00:45:54.988 --> 00:45:56.322 line:78%
IN THE STANDPOINT OF WHETHER THE

00:45:55.722 --> 00:45:57.357 line:78%
EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE SHOULD BE

00:45:56.423 --> 00:45:58.358 line:78%
PERMITTED OR NOT.

00:45:57.457 --> 00:45:59.359 line:78%
THIS IS WHAT I'M SAYING.

00:45:58.458 --> 00:46:00.427 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN REYNOLDS, THE COURT ENDED

00:45:59.459 --> 00:46:00.994 line:78%
UP TREATING THE ASSERTION OF

00:46:00.527 --> 00:46:01.695 line:78%
PRIVILEGE THERE AS AN

00:46:01.094 --> 00:46:02.429 line:78%
EVIDENTIARY PRIVILEGE, BUT IT

00:46:01.795 --> 00:46:03.430 line:78%
DID ALLUDE TO THE FACT THAT

00:46:02.529 --> 00:46:04.464 line:78%
THERE WAS A CONSTITUTIONAL

00:46:03.530 --> 00:46:05.432 line:78%
QUESTION AND SAID THE COURT

00:46:04.564 --> 00:46:06.433 line:78%
WASN'T REACHING IT, AS I RECALL.

00:46:05.532 --> 00:46:07.434 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE ISSUE OF EXECUTIVE

00:46:06.533 --> 00:46:17.444 line:78%
PRIVILEGE, I SHOULD POINT OUT

00:46:07.534 --> 00:46:19.412 line:78%
HERE, IS A VERY NARROW ONE.

00:46:17.544 --> 00:46:21.448 line:78%
AND, I THINK IT'S IMPORTANT THAT

00:46:19.512 --> 00:46:22.415 line:78%
WE BEAR THIS IN MIND.

00:46:21.548 --> 00:46:23.450 line:78%
IT DOESN'T INVOLVE A VERY LARGE

00:46:22.515 --> 00:46:25.485 line:78%
OR BROAD PRIVILEGE RIGHTS.

00:46:23.550 --> 00:46:26.453 line:78%
WHAT IT REALLY NARROWS DOWN TO

00:46:25.585 --> 00:46:27.487 line:78%
IS SOMEWHAT SIMPLE BUT VERY

00:46:26.553 --> 00:46:31.491 line:78%
IMPORTANT ISSUE IN THE

00:46:27.587 --> 00:46:32.459 line:78%
ADMINISTRATIVE OF CRIMINAL

00:46:31.591 --> 00:46:33.460 line:78%
JUSTICE AND THAT IS WHETHER THE

00:46:32.559 --> 00:46:36.496 line:78%
PRESIDENT, IN A PENDING

00:46:33.560 --> 00:46:37.497 line:78%
PROSECUTION, CAN WITHHOLD

00:46:36.596 --> 00:46:39.532 line:78%
MATERIAL EVIDENCE FROM THE COURT

00:46:37.597 --> 00:46:40.533 line:78%
MERELY ON HIS ASSERTION THAT THE

00:46:39.632 --> 00:46:41.501 line:78%
EVIDENCE INVOLVES CONFIDENTIAL

00:46:40.633 --> 00:46:51.711 line:78%
COMMUNICATIONS AND THIS IS WHAT

00:46:41.601 --> 00:46:52.746 line:78%
REALLY IT GETS DOWN TO.

00:46:51.811 --> 00:46:53.747 line:78%
WE KNOW THAT SOVEREIGN

00:46:52.846 --> 00:46:54.748 line:78%
PREROGATIVES TO PROTECT THE

00:46:53.847 --> 00:46:55.715 line:78%
CONFIDENTIALITY NECESSARY TO

00:46:54.848 --> 00:46:56.750 line:78%
CARRYOUT RESPONSIBILITIES IN THE

00:46:55.815 --> 00:46:57.884 line:78%
FIELDS OF INTERNATIONAL

00:46:56.850 --> 00:46:58.485 line:78%
RELATIONS AND NATIONAL DEFENSE

00:46:57.984 --> 00:46:59.185 line:78%
ARE NOT, HERE, INVOLVED.

00:46:58.585 --> 00:46:59.919 line:78%
AND, THERE IS NO CLAIM OF ANY

00:46:59.285 --> 00:47:00.720 line:78%
STATE SECRETS OR THAT DISCLOSURE

00:47:00.020 --> 00:47:04.791 line:78%
WILL HAVE DIRE EFFECT ON A

00:47:00.820 --> 00:47:05.792 line:78%
NATION OR ITS PEOPLE.

00:47:04.891 --> 00:47:07.827 line:78%
ACTUALLY, I THINK WHEN WE GET TO

00:47:05.892 --> 00:47:14.834 line:78%
WAYNE AND THE NON-DISCLOSURE AS

00:47:07.927 --> 00:47:16.836 line:78%
AGAINST DISCLOSURE AND I THINK

00:47:14.934 --> 00:47:18.838 line:78%
WHEN WE BEGIN TO LAY THE BALANCE

00:47:16.936 --> 00:47:21.841 line:78%
OF INTEREST, IT WOULD SEEM TO ME

00:47:18.938 --> 00:47:22.876 line:78%
THAT THE BALANCE CLEARLY LIES IN

00:47:21.941 --> 00:47:23.877 line:78%
FAVOR OF A DISCLOSURE IN A

00:47:22.976 --> 00:47:25.912 line:78%
SITUATION SUCH AS THE

00:47:23.977 --> 00:47:31.184 line:78%
CIRCUMSTANCE HERE.

00:47:26.012 --> 00:47:32.085 line:78%
OF COURSE --

00:47:31.284 --> 00:47:33.086 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT CERTAINLY WOULD NOT BE

00:47:32.185 --> 00:47:35.021 line:78%
TRUE IN CASE THE FIFTH AMENDMENT

00:47:33.186 --> 00:47:45.298 line:78%
WAS INVOLVED, BUT THAT'S NOT

00:47:35.121 --> 00:47:46.132 line:78%
PRESENT HERE.

00:47:45.398 --> 00:47:47.167 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOT PRESENT, MR. JUSTICE

00:47:46.232 --> 00:47:48.134 line:78%
DOUGLAS, AND THERE IS NO

00:47:47.267 --> 00:47:49.135 line:78%
QUESTION ABOUT WHAT THE FIFTH

00:47:48.234 --> 00:47:50.303 line:78%
AMENDMENT HAS VERY PLAINLY

00:47:49.235 --> 00:47:50.937 line:78%
WRITTEN OUT IN THE CONSTITUTION

00:47:50.403 --> 00:47:52.172 line:78%
AND IS INVOKED AS A CLEAR

00:47:51.037 --> 00:47:53.206 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL PRIVILEGE.

00:47:52.272 --> 00:47:57.210 line:78%
I THINK IT WOULD BE OF HELP IF I

00:47:53.306 --> 00:48:00.246 line:78%
MAY POINT OUT TO THE COURT, THAT

00:47:57.310 --> 00:48:02.248 line:78%
THERE IS AN EXCELLENT ARTICLE

00:48:00.347 --> 00:48:04.284 line:78%
THAT WE HAVE ALLUDED TO IN OUR

00:48:02.349 --> 00:48:07.387 line:78%
BRIEFS BY PROFESSOR BERGER THAT

00:48:04.384 --> 00:48:09.422 line:78%
APPEARS IN A YALE LAW JOURNAL

00:48:07.487 --> 00:48:10.423 line:78%
WHICH DISCUSSES THE EHRENBERG

00:48:09.522 --> 00:48:11.391 line:78%
CASE AT LENGTH AND ALSO OTHER

00:48:10.523 --> 00:48:23.403 line:78%
CASES THAT HAVE BEEN POINTED TO

00:48:11.491 --> 00:48:25.405 line:78%
SINCE THE TIME OF THAT CASE.

00:48:23.503 --> 00:48:26.439 line:78%
AND, IF I MAY JUST SAY VERY

00:48:25.505 --> 00:48:28.508 line:78%
BRIEFLY, THAT SUMMARIZES THE

00:48:26.539 --> 00:48:29.542 line:78%
SITUATION BY SAYING THAT THE

00:48:28.608 --> 00:48:30.510 line:78%
HEART OF MARSHALL'S OPINION WAS,

00:48:29.642 --> 00:48:31.544 line:78%
THEREFORE, JUST AS SUMMARIZED BY

00:48:30.610 --> 00:48:32.579 line:78%
THE COURT OF APPEALS IN THE

00:48:31.644 --> 00:48:33.513 line:78%
NIXON V. SIRICA CASE AND THE

00:48:32.679 --> 00:48:36.649 line:78%
TAPES CASE THAT WE HAVE TALKED

00:48:33.613 --> 00:48:37.717 line:78%
ABOUT.

00:48:36.750 --> 00:48:39.686 line:78%
THE COURT WAS TO SHOW RESPECT

00:48:37.817 --> 00:48:40.653 line:78%
FOR THE PRESIDENT'S REASON, BUT

00:48:39.786 --> 00:48:47.961 line:78%
THE ULTIMATE DECISION REMAINED

00:48:40.754 --> 00:48:48.828 line:78%
WITH THE COURT.

00:48:48.061 --> 00:48:50.964 line:78%
AND WE ARE NOT SUGGESTING, FOR A

00:48:48.928 --> 00:48:51.665 line:78%
MOMENT, HERE THAT THE MATTER OF

00:48:51.064 --> 00:48:52.132 line:78%
EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE SHOULD NOT

00:48:51.765 --> 00:48:52.966 line:78%
BE LOOKED INTO.

00:48:52.232 --> 00:48:53.299 line:78%
THIS IS NOT -- IT DESERVES TO BE

00:48:53.066 --> 00:48:54.034 line:78%
TESTED.

00:48:53.400 --> 00:49:04.077 line:78%
IT SHOULD BE TESTED AND WE URGE

00:48:54.134 --> 00:49:06.913 line:78%
THAT IT BE TESTED.

00:49:04.177 --> 00:49:08.948 line:78%
BUT, THE ULTIMATE DECISION IS

00:49:07.013 --> 00:49:10.016 line:78%
NOT ONE OF SAYING THAT IT IS

00:49:09.049 --> 00:49:10.984 line:78%
ABSOLUTE THAT IT RESTS ON THE

00:49:10.116 --> 00:49:11.985 line:78%
CONSTITUTION THAT IT DOESN'T

00:49:11.084 --> 00:49:14.054 line:78%
ENTITLE ANYONE AND DOESN'T

00:49:12.085 --> 00:49:15.021 line:78%
AUTHORIZE ANYONE.

00:49:14.154 --> 00:49:23.096 line:78%
IT DOESN'T EVEN AUTHORIZE THIS

00:49:15.121 --> 00:49:24.097 line:78%
COURT TO LOOK INTO IT, BECAUSE

00:49:23.196 --> 00:49:25.065 line:78%
IF THE COURTS ARE THE ULTIMATE

00:49:24.197 --> 00:49:27.067 line:78%
INTERPRETERS OF THE CONSTITUTION

00:49:25.165 --> 00:49:28.134 line:78%
AND CAN RESTRAIN CONGRESS TO

00:49:27.167 --> 00:49:31.371 line:78%
OPERATE WITHIN THE

00:49:28.234 --> 00:49:32.105 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL BALANCE, THEYCE'D

00:49:31.471 --> 00:49:32.839 line:78%
AND LEST TO MEASURE PRESIDENTIAL

00:49:32.205 --> 00:49:33.573 line:78%
CLAIMS OF CONSTITUTIONAL POWERS.

00:49:32.939 --> 00:49:34.407 line:78%
I WANTED BRIEFLY TO MAKE MENTION

00:49:33.673 --> 00:49:50.590 line:78%
OF THE QUESTIONS THAT HAS BEEN

00:49:34.507 --> 00:49:52.592 line:78%
RAISED BY COUNSEL FOR THE

00:49:50.690 --> 00:49:53.593 line:78%
PRESIDENT THAT INVOLVES A MOTION

00:49:52.692 --> 00:49:55.595 line:78%
TO EXPUNGE THE FINDING OF THE

00:49:53.693 --> 00:49:56.563 line:78%
GRAND JURY'S ACTION THAT THE

00:49:55.695 --> 00:49:58.598 line:78%
PRESIDENT IS TO BE NAMED AS AN

00:49:56.663 --> 00:50:00.600 line:78%
UNINDICTED CO-CONSPIRATOR ALONG

00:49:58.698 --> 00:50:01.568 line:78%
WITH A NUMBER OF OTHERS WHEN THE

00:50:00.700 --> 00:50:04.437 line:78%
PRETRIAL PROCEEDINGS ARE GOING

00:50:01.668 --> 00:50:10.410 line:78%
INTO, AND A BILL OF PARTICULARS

00:50:04.537 --> 00:50:12.379 line:78%
AND I SAY THAT THE GRAND JURY'S

00:50:10.510 --> 00:50:13.413 line:78%
FINDING, PAINFUL AS IT IS, I

00:50:12.479 --> 00:50:14.414 line:78%
THINK, ON THE PART OF THE COURT,

00:50:13.513 --> 00:50:19.552 line:78%
MUST BE CONSIDERED AS BEING

00:50:14.514 --> 00:50:20.453 line:78%
VALID AND SUFFICIENT TO SHOW A

00:50:19.652 --> 00:50:21.454 line:78%
PRIMA FACIE.

00:50:20.553 --> 00:50:22.455 line:78%
IT IS SUFFICIENT TO SHOW A PRIMA

00:50:21.554 --> 00:50:24.491 line:78%
FACIE THAT THE PRESIDENT WAS

00:50:22.555 --> 00:50:26.493 line:78%
INVOLVED IN THE PROCEEDINGS IN

00:50:24.591 --> 00:50:28.495 line:78%
THE COURSE AND THE CONTINUATION

00:50:26.593 --> 00:50:29.596 line:78%
OF THE PARTICULAR CONSPIRACY

00:50:28.595 --> 00:50:33.566 line:78%
THAT WAS CHARGED.

00:50:29.696 --> 00:50:34.701 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IS THAT THE ISSUE, MR.

00:50:33.666 --> 00:50:35.301 line:78%
JAWORSKI, OR IS THE ISSUE

00:50:34.801 --> 00:50:35.802 line:78%
WHETHER THERE COULD BE A

00:50:35.402 --> 00:50:39.606 line:78%
COLLATERAL ATTACK?

00:50:35.902 --> 00:50:40.640 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S ALSO ANOTHER ISSUE.

00:50:39.706 --> 00:50:41.641 line:78%
BUT I MERELY WANTED TO POINT OUT

00:50:40.740 --> 00:50:44.644 line:78%
THAT I BELIEVE THAT THIS COURT

00:50:41.741 --> 00:50:46.646 line:78%
WOULD NOT GO INTO THE GRAND

00:50:44.744 --> 00:50:47.680 line:78%
JURY'S FINDINGS, BUT IT'S A

00:50:46.746 --> 00:50:49.649 line:78%
PRIMA FACIE MATTER AND THAT THIS

00:50:47.781 --> 00:50:50.683 line:78%
COURT WOULD NOT GO INTO IT FOR

00:50:49.749 --> 00:50:54.754 line:78%
THE PURPOSE OF DETERMINING A

00:50:50.784 --> 00:50:55.755 line:78%
MATTER OF THAT KIND.

00:50:54.854 --> 00:50:57.757 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THOUGHT WE HAVE PUT THAT

00:50:55.855 --> 00:51:01.761 line:78%
ISSUE ASIDE A WHILE AGO.

00:50:57.857 --> 00:51:04.731 line:78%
I JUST DON'T UNDERSTAND WHAT

00:51:01.861 --> 00:51:06.766 line:78%
RELEVANCE IT IS TO THIS CASE.

00:51:04.831 --> 00:51:07.767 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I HAVE TO AGREE WITH

00:51:06.866 --> 00:51:09.803 line:78%
YOU, NEITHER DO I SEE WHAT THE

00:51:07.867 --> 00:51:11.838 line:78%
RELEVANCE IS OF THE MATTER OF

00:51:09.903 --> 00:51:12.872 line:78%
SAYING THAT THERE'S ANOTHER

00:51:11.938 --> 00:51:13.807 line:78%
ARGUMENT ADVANCED HERE AND THAT

00:51:12.972 --> 00:51:15.909 line:78%
IS THAT THE PRESIDENT CAN'T BE

00:51:13.907 --> 00:51:16.910 line:78%
INDICTED.

00:51:16.009 --> 00:51:17.911 line:78%
AND, I DON'T KNOW WHAT THE

00:51:17.010 --> 00:51:18.912 line:78%
RELEVANCE OF THAT IS IN THIS

00:51:18.011 --> 00:51:19.846 line:78%
CASE EITHER, VERY FRANKLY,

00:51:19.012 --> 00:51:20.947 line:78%
BECAUSE IT ISN'T BEFORE THE

00:51:19.946 --> 00:51:22.916 line:78%
COURT.

00:51:21.047 --> 00:51:23.883 line:78%
AND, YET, THE ARGUMENT IS MADE

00:51:23.016 --> 00:51:24.918 line:78%
AND MANY PAGES OF BRIEFS ARE

00:51:23.983 --> 00:51:30.123 line:78%
DEVOTED TO IT.

00:51:25.018 --> 00:51:30.990 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I JUST WONDER, MR. JAWORSKI,

00:51:30.223 --> 00:51:32.992 line:78%
WHY YOU DON'T, ON CONTENT, WITH

00:51:31.090 --> 00:51:33.960 line:78%
JUST ARGUING IT IS IRRELEVANT

00:51:33.092 --> 00:51:35.028 line:78%
WITHOUT THINKING ON THE RIGHT --

00:51:34.060 --> 00:51:35.995 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THIS IS WHY I SKIPPED

00:51:35.128 --> 00:51:36.963 line:78%
THE ARGUMENT WITH RESPECT TO THE

00:51:36.095 --> 00:51:42.202 line:78%
MATTER OF WHETHER HE COULD BE

00:51:37.063 --> 00:51:43.069 line:78%
INDICTED OR NOT.

00:51:42.302 --> 00:51:47.106 line:78%
BUT AS MUCH AS THE QUESTION HAD

00:51:43.169 --> 00:51:48.074 line:78%
BEEN RAISED AND BRIEFED AND A

00:51:47.207 --> 00:51:49.075 line:78%
MOTION EXIST BEFORE THE COURT, I

00:51:48.174 --> 00:51:50.076 line:78%
HAVE TO AGREE THAT IT IS

00:51:49.175 --> 00:51:51.077 line:78%
IRRELEVANT BUT IT IS A PART OF

00:51:50.176 --> 00:51:52.111 line:78%
THE CASE, AND THAT'S THE ONLY

00:51:51.177 --> 00:51:53.246 line:78%
REASON I ALLUDED TO IT AND I

00:51:52.212 --> 00:51:53.713 line:78%
HAVE NO INTERESTING IN SPENDING

00:51:53.346 --> 00:51:54.380 line:78%
MUCH TIME ON IT.

00:51:53.813 --> 00:51:58.184 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, EXCEPT, PART OF THE

00:51:54.481 --> 00:51:59.152 line:78%
GROUNDS ON WHICH YOU REST IN

00:51:58.284 --> 00:52:00.186 line:78%
SUBPOENAING THIS MATERIAL IS THE

00:51:59.252 --> 00:52:01.287 line:78%
FACT THAT THE PRESIDENT HAS

00:52:00.286 --> 00:52:01.988 line:78%
HIMSELF BEEN NAMED AS A

00:52:01.387 --> 00:52:04.257 line:78%
CO-CONSPIRATOR, AN UNINDICTED

00:52:02.088 --> 00:52:08.328 line:78%
ONE.

00:52:04.357 --> 00:52:08.928 line:78%
AND, THAT'S TRUE, ISN'T IT?

00:52:08.428 --> 00:52:09.295 line:78%
THAT'S A PART OF --

00:52:09.028 --> 00:52:10.230 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT.

00:52:09.395 --> 00:52:11.197 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THESE TWO GROUNDS UPON WHICH

00:52:10.330 --> 00:52:15.268 line:78%
YOU REST IN SUBPOENAING THIS

00:52:11.297 --> 00:52:16.236 line:78%
MATERIAL.

00:52:15.368 --> 00:52:17.270 line:78%
AND, THE RESPONSE TO THAT IS,

00:52:16.336 --> 00:52:18.271 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT CANNOT

00:52:17.370 --> 00:52:20.306 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONALLY BE NAMED AS AN

00:52:18.371 --> 00:52:21.207 line:78%
UNINDICTED CO-CONSPIRATOR.

00:52:20.406 --> 00:52:22.342 line:78%
SO, TO THAT EXTENT, IT'S IN THIS

00:52:21.307 --> 00:52:25.445 line:78%
CASE.

00:52:22.442 --> 00:52:26.412 line:78%
THE QUESTION'S IN THIS CASE.

00:52:25.545 --> 00:52:27.413 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I DON'T THINK IT'S A

00:52:26.513 --> 00:52:30.416 line:78%
MATTER THAT, VERY FRANKLY, HAS

00:52:27.514 --> 00:52:32.385 line:78%
ANY PARTICULAR BASIS TO IT

00:52:30.517 --> 00:52:34.420 line:78%
BECAUSE I DON'T SEE HOW THIS

00:52:32.485 --> 00:52:35.388 line:78%
COURT COULD BE ASKED TO

00:52:34.521 --> 00:52:36.422 line:78%
SUBSTITUTE ITS JUDGMENT FOR THAT

00:52:35.488 --> 00:52:38.458 line:78%
OF THE GRAND JURY.

00:52:36.523 --> 00:52:39.526 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THAT'S SOMETHING QUITE

00:52:38.558 --> 00:52:40.560 line:78%
DIFFERENT AGAIN, WHETHER OR NOT

00:52:39.626 --> 00:52:41.528 line:78%
THERE WAS SUFFICIENT EVIDENCE

00:52:40.660 --> 00:52:42.495 line:78%
BEFORE THE GRAND JURY TO JUSTIFY

00:52:41.628 --> 00:52:44.597 line:78%
THE GRAND JURY IN NAMING THE

00:52:42.595 --> 00:52:46.499 line:78%
PRESIDENT.

00:52:44.697 --> 00:52:47.534 line:78%
THAT'S QUITE A DIFFERENT AND, AS

00:52:46.599 --> 00:52:48.535 line:78%
CHIEF JUSTICE SUGGESTED, A

00:52:47.634 --> 00:52:49.569 line:78%
COLLATERAL ISSUE.

00:52:48.635 --> 00:52:50.537 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT.

00:52:49.669 --> 00:52:52.572 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT THE ISSUE OF WHETHER OR

00:52:50.637 --> 00:52:54.574 line:78%
NOT THE PRESIDENT CAN

00:52:52.672 --> 00:52:57.577 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONALLY BE NAMED BY A

00:52:54.674 --> 00:52:58.578 line:78%
GRAND JURY AS A CO-CONSPIRATOR,

00:52:57.677 --> 00:53:01.614 line:78%
EVEN THOUGH AN UNINDICTED ONE,

00:52:58.678 --> 00:53:03.650 line:78%
IT IS AT LEAST TANGENTIALLY

00:53:01.714 --> 00:53:09.689 line:78%
BEFORE US BECAUSE THAT'S -- IT'S

00:53:03.750 --> 00:53:10.723 line:78%
THE FACT THAT HE'S PART OF THE

00:53:09.789 --> 00:53:11.724 line:78%
GROUNDS AND PART OF THE

00:53:10.823 --> 00:53:13.793 line:78%
FOUNDATION UPON WHICH YOU HAVE

00:53:11.824 --> 00:53:14.794 line:78%
BASED YOUR SUBPOENA DUCES TECUM.

00:53:13.893 --> 00:53:18.798 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOT ONLY THAT, I THINK THAT

00:53:14.894 --> 00:53:20.800 line:78%
IT HAS, TO PINPOINT IT IN OUR

00:53:18.898 --> 00:53:24.938 line:78%
VIEW, A MATERIALITY BECAUSE IT

00:53:20.900 --> 00:53:27.907 line:78%
DOES RELATE TO THE QUESTION OF

00:53:25.038 --> 00:53:29.876 line:78%
THE PROOF THAT WE ARE SEEKING

00:53:28.007 --> 00:53:31.978 line:78%
THE RELEVANCE OF THE PROOF THAT

00:53:29.976 --> 00:53:34.013 line:78%
WE ARE SEEKING.

00:53:32.078 --> 00:53:35.014 line:78%
AND THIS GETS INTO, OF COURSE, A

00:53:34.113 --> 00:53:36.149 line:78%
DISCUSSION OF MATTERS THAT ARE

00:53:35.114 --> 00:53:36.749 line:78%
SEALED AND WHICH I CANNOT

00:53:36.249 --> 00:53:38.051 line:78%
DISCUSS WITH THE COURT.

00:53:36.849 --> 00:53:41.054 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I UNDERSTAND, RIGHT.

00:53:38.151 --> 00:53:43.056 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT WHETHER OR NOT HE HAD THE

00:53:41.154 --> 00:53:45.024 line:78%
AUTHORITY, THEY DID, IT IS A

00:53:43.156 --> 00:53:50.263 line:78%
FACT THAT THE GRAND JURY DID IT.

00:53:45.124 --> 00:53:51.264 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR.

00:53:50.363 --> 00:53:51.998 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SO IT DOESN'T -- I DON'T SEE

00:53:51.364 --> 00:53:52.699 line:78%
HOW WE HAVE ANYTHING TO DO WITH

00:53:52.098 --> 00:53:53.032 line:78%
WHETHER THEY HAD AUTHORITY OR

00:53:52.799 --> 00:53:56.035 line:78%
NOT.

00:53:53.132 --> 00:53:58.137 line:78%
IT'S A FACT.

00:53:56.135 --> 00:54:04.043 line:78%
ISN'T THAT TRUE?

00:53:58.237 --> 00:54:06.145 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S, I THINK, CORRECT.

00:54:04.143 --> 00:54:07.113 line:78%
NOW --

00:54:06.245 --> 00:54:09.182 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THOUGHT THE HEART OF THIS

00:54:07.213 --> 00:54:13.119 line:78%
CASE WERE THE RIGHTS OF

00:54:09.282 --> 00:54:17.156 line:78%
DEFENDANTS IN CRIMINAL TRIAL?

00:54:13.219 --> 00:54:18.191 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT --

00:54:17.256 --> 00:54:19.192 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NEVERTHELESS --

00:54:18.291 --> 00:54:20.226 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT IS VERY MUCH --

00:54:19.292 --> 00:54:23.262 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT MAY BE EXCULPATORY AND

00:54:20.326 --> 00:54:24.330 line:78%
FREE THEM OF ALL LIABILITIES.

00:54:23.363 --> 00:54:25.331 line:78%
I DON'T KNOW BUT I --

00:54:24.430 --> 00:54:28.401 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, CERTAINLY, IT'S IN THE

00:54:25.431 --> 00:54:29.369 line:78%
CASE NOW AND, OF COURSE, WHICH

00:54:28.501 --> 00:54:30.436 line:78%
YOU HAVE REFERENCE TOO ALSO, I'M

00:54:29.469 --> 00:54:33.406 line:78%
SURE, MR. JUSTICE DOUGLAS, AS

00:54:30.536 --> 00:54:35.375 line:78%
THE BRAY AND THE JINKS, MARYLAND

00:54:33.506 --> 00:54:44.450 line:78%
VERSUS BRAY AND THE JINKS.

00:54:44.684 --> 00:54:46.552 line:78%
 AND, THIS IS A PART OF THE

00:54:45.551 --> 00:54:47.553 line:78%
CASE.

00:54:46.653 --> 00:54:49.555 line:78%
HOWEVER, IT HAPPENS NOT TO BE A

00:54:47.654 --> 00:54:50.590 line:78%
PART OF THE APPEAL, ALTHOUGH IT

00:54:49.656 --> 00:54:52.592 line:78%
IS A PART OF THE CASE.

00:54:50.690 --> 00:54:53.559 line:78%
BUT AS FAR AS OUR POSITION IS

00:54:52.692 --> 00:54:54.694 line:78%
CONCERNED, IT DOESN'T RELATE TO

00:54:53.660 --> 00:54:55.695 line:78%
THAT.

00:54:54.794 --> 00:54:56.729 line:78%
BUT, CERTAINLY, IT'S TRUE THAT

00:54:55.795 --> 00:54:58.798 line:78%
THIS MATERIAL, AS WE HAD POINTED

00:54:56.829 --> 00:54:59.799 line:78%
OUT IN OUR COMMUNICATIONS TO THE

00:54:58.898 --> 00:55:00.800 line:78%
PRESIDENT, MAY WELL INVOLVE

00:54:59.899 --> 00:55:02.835 line:78%
EXCULPATORY MATTERS AND WE, TIME

00:55:00.900 --> 00:55:03.836 line:78%
AND AGAIN, POINTED OUT WE WANTED

00:55:02.935 --> 00:55:04.837 line:78%
THEM NOT SIMPLY BECAUSE WE FELT

00:55:03.936 --> 00:55:05.872 line:78%
THAT THERE WERE MATTERS THAT

00:55:04.937 --> 00:55:07.874 line:78%
NEEDED TO BE DEVELOPED IN

00:55:05.972 --> 00:55:08.841 line:78%
CONNECTION WITH THE PROSECUTION,

00:55:07.974 --> 00:55:10.877 line:78%
BUT THAT THEY COULD WELL CONTAIN

00:55:08.941 --> 00:55:12.912 line:78%
EXCULPATORY MATTERS.

00:55:10.977 --> 00:55:13.846 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT THE BRADY QUESTION REALLY

00:55:13.012 --> 00:55:14.981 line:78%
LURKS JUST IN THE BACKGROUND,

00:55:13.946 --> 00:55:15.915 line:78%
DOES IT NOT?

00:55:15.081 --> 00:55:17.984 line:78%
THAT IS, IF YOU GET INFORMATION,

00:55:16.015 --> 00:55:18.985 line:78%
WHATEVER YOU GET --

00:55:18.084 --> 00:55:20.019 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WOULD BE AVAILABLE.

00:55:19.085 --> 00:55:21.020 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU WOULD CONCEDE IS

00:55:20.119 --> 00:55:21.954 line:78%
AVAILABLE TO ANY DEFENDANT --

00:55:21.120 --> 00:55:23.056 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT, MR. CHIEF

00:55:22.055 --> 00:55:24.023 line:78%
JUSTICE.

00:55:23.156 --> 00:55:25.058 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHO CAN MAKE THE SHOWING.

00:55:24.123 --> 00:55:26.059 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR.

00:55:25.158 --> 00:55:28.061 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THE QUESTION OF WHETHER

00:55:26.159 --> 00:55:29.062 line:78%
OR NOT THE DEFENDANTS, UNDER THE

00:55:28.161 --> 00:55:31.097 line:78%
BRADY DOCTRINE, ARE ENTITLED TO

00:55:29.162 --> 00:55:32.098 line:78%
SUBPOENAING INFORMATION.

00:55:31.197 --> 00:55:33.099 line:78%
AND MATERIAL THAT'S NOT NOW IN

00:55:32.198 --> 00:55:35.101 line:78%
YOUR POSSESSION, BUT IS IN THE

00:55:33.199 --> 00:55:36.069 line:78%
POSSESSION OF THE PRESIDENT, WAS

00:55:35.201 --> 00:55:37.070 line:78%
AN ISSUE THAT WAS LEFT UNDECIDED

00:55:36.169 --> 00:55:38.071 line:78%
BY THE DISTRICT COURT.

00:55:37.170 --> 00:55:42.075 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR.

00:55:38.171 --> 00:55:44.143 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AM I RIGHT ABOUT THAT?

00:55:42.175 --> 00:55:45.178 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S NOT BEFORE THIS COURT.

00:55:44.243 --> 00:55:46.179 line:78%
I BELIEVE, WITH THE PERMISSION

00:55:45.278 --> 00:55:47.213 line:78%
OF THE COURT, UNLESS THERE ARE

00:55:46.279 --> 00:55:48.147 line:78%
FURTHER QUESTIONS, I'LL RESERVE

00:55:47.313 --> 00:56:03.563 line:78%
THE REST OF THE TIME FOR THE

00:55:48.247 --> 00:56:04.063 line:78%
CLOSE.

00:56:03.663 --> 00:56:04.797 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. ST. CLAIR.

00:56:04.163 --> 00:56:13.406 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. CHIEF JUSTICE AND MEMBERS

00:56:04.897 --> 00:56:14.407 line:78%
OF THE COURT.

00:56:13.506 --> 00:56:15.408 line:78%
MY LEARNED BROTHERS APPROACHED

00:56:14.507 --> 00:56:16.409 line:78%
THIS CASE I THINK IN THE

00:56:15.508 --> 00:56:17.410 line:78%
TRADITIONAL POINT OF VIEW,

00:56:16.509 --> 00:56:19.412 line:78%
NAMELY, THIS IS AN ATTEMPT BY A

00:56:17.510 --> 00:56:20.379 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR TO OBTAIN

00:56:19.512 --> 00:56:21.447 line:78%
WHAT HE THINKS IS DESIRABLE

00:56:20.480 --> 00:56:23.483 line:78%
EVIDENCE IN A CRIMINAL

00:56:21.547 --> 00:56:29.589 line:78%
PROSECUTION THAT HE HAS A

00:56:23.583 --> 00:56:30.590 line:78%
RESPONSIBILITY FOR.

00:56:29.689 --> 00:56:32.592 line:78%
NOT ONCE, HOWEVER, HAVE I HEARD

00:56:30.690 --> 00:56:37.797 line:78%
HIM MENTION WHAT I THINK IS

00:56:32.692 --> 00:56:38.564 line:78%
REALLY INVOLVED, AT LEAST IN A

00:56:37.897 --> 00:56:39.599 line:78%
SIGNIFICANT PART, AND THAT IS

00:56:38.664 --> 00:56:41.601 line:78%
THE CO-PENDENCY OF THE

00:56:39.699 --> 00:56:42.635 line:78%
IMPEACHMENT PROCEEDINGS BEFORE

00:56:41.701 --> 00:56:43.636 line:78%
THE HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES.

00:56:42.735 --> 00:56:44.670 line:78%
AND, THE REALISTIC FUSION THAT

00:56:43.736 --> 00:56:47.673 line:78%
HAS TAKEN PLACE WITH RESPECT TO

00:56:44.771 --> 00:56:48.674 line:78%
THESE TWO PROCEEDINGS AND THE

00:56:47.774 --> 00:56:49.642 line:78%
PROMISE OF CONTINUED FUSION, AS

00:56:48.775 --> 00:56:50.710 line:78%
I UNDERSTAND MY BROTHER'S

00:56:49.742 --> 00:56:53.813 line:78%
POSITION.

00:56:50.810 --> 00:56:54.480 line:78%
MAY I QUOTE FROM PAGE 50 --

00:56:53.913 --> 00:56:54.781 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NONE OF OUR PROBLEMS, ARE

00:56:54.580 --> 00:56:55.715 line:78%
THEY?

00:56:54.881 --> 00:56:58.818 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THINK, SIR, THEY REALLY

00:56:55.815 --> 00:56:59.819 line:78%
ARE.

00:56:58.918 --> 00:57:02.889 line:78%
FIRST, BY WAY OF FACTUAL

00:56:59.919 --> 00:57:03.856 line:78%
BACKGROUND --

00:57:02.989 --> 00:57:05.825 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE SOLE AUTHORITY TO IMPEACH

00:57:03.956 --> 00:57:06.859 line:78%
THIS IN THE HOUSE --

00:57:05.925 --> 00:57:08.828 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT.

00:57:06.959 --> 00:57:09.862 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE SOLE AUTHORITY TO TRY

00:57:08.928 --> 00:57:11.864 line:78%
THIS IN THE SENATE.

00:57:09.962 --> 00:57:12.865 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT, AND THE COURT SHALL

00:57:11.964 --> 00:57:14.834 line:78%
NOT BE USED TO IMPLEMENT OR AID

00:57:12.965 --> 00:57:16.869 line:78%
THAT PROCESS WHICH WHAT HAS

00:57:14.934 --> 00:57:17.837 line:78%
HAPPENED IN THIS CASE.

00:57:16.969 --> 00:57:18.871 line:78%
THIS CASE WOULDN'T BE HERE ON

00:57:17.937 --> 00:57:19.939 line:78%
JULY 8.

00:57:18.971 --> 00:57:23.042 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HOW IS THAT?

00:57:20.039 --> 00:57:23.476 line:78%
&gt;&gt; JUST HOW IS THIS DONE?

00:57:23.142 --> 00:57:25.144 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ALL RIGHT.

00:57:23.910 --> 00:57:25.845 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HOW IS THIS CASE IMPLEMENTED?

00:57:25.244 --> 00:57:27.013 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I WOULD LIKE TO REVIEW SOME

00:57:25.945 --> 00:57:28.080 line:78%
OF THE FACTS FOR YOU IN THIS

00:57:27.113 --> 00:57:29.182 line:78%
REGARD.

00:57:28.181 --> 00:57:29.916 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHICH ARE IN THE RECORD?

00:57:29.282 --> 00:57:30.316 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, MY BROTHER HAS MENTIONED

00:57:30.016 --> 00:57:32.118 line:78%
THEM TO YOU.

00:57:30.416 --> 00:57:33.052 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, BUT ARE THEY IN THE

00:57:32.218 --> 00:57:34.153 line:78%
RECORD, NOT WHAT HE'S MENTIONED.

00:57:33.152 --> 00:57:35.121 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

00:57:34.253 --> 00:57:37.223 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, WE'RE JUST AN ADJUNCT

00:57:35.221 --> 00:57:39.225 line:78%
OF THE HOUSE.

00:57:37.323 --> 00:57:40.226 line:78%
THIS CASE SHOULD BE DISMISSED AS

00:57:39.325 --> 00:57:43.262 line:78%
IMPROVIDENTLY GRANTED, ISN'T IT?

00:57:40.326 --> 00:57:45.231 line:78%
&gt;&gt; EXACTLY RIGHT, SIR.

00:57:43.362 --> 00:57:48.201 line:78%
NOT ONLY THAT, IT MAKES THE CASE

00:57:45.331 --> 00:57:49.268 line:78%
UNJUSTICIABLE AT LEAST.

00:57:48.301 --> 00:57:50.236 line:78%
NOW --

00:57:49.368 --> 00:57:51.270 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT THE DISTRICT COURT'S

00:57:50.336 --> 00:57:52.271 line:78%
DECISION STANDS.

00:57:51.370 --> 00:57:53.239 line:78%
IS THAT WHAT YOU WANT?

00:57:52.371 --> 00:57:56.242 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, THE CASE SHOULD BE

00:57:53.339 --> 00:57:57.343 line:78%
DISMISSED, SIR.

00:57:56.342 --> 00:57:59.378 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IF WE DISMISS AS

00:57:57.443 --> 00:58:00.346 line:78%
IMPROVIDENTLY GRANTED, I SUBMIT

00:57:59.478 --> 00:58:01.280 line:78%
THE DISTRICT COURT'S PREMIUM

00:58:00.446 --> 00:58:02.381 line:78%
WOULD -- THE JUDGMENT WOULD

00:58:01.380 --> 00:58:03.282 line:78%
STAND.

00:58:02.481 --> 00:58:04.383 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THEN I WOULD RETRACT WHAT I

00:58:03.382 --> 00:58:05.384 line:78%
SAID.

00:58:04.483 --> 00:58:09.555 line:78%
THIS CASE SHOULD BE

00:58:05.484 --> 00:58:10.556 line:78%
DISMISSED.[LAUGHTER]

00:58:09.655 --> 00:58:11.490 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE CASE WOULD BE ON APPEAL

00:58:10.656 --> 00:58:14.560 line:78%
IN THE COURT OF APPEALS IF WE

00:58:11.591 --> 00:58:14.994 line:78%
DISMISSED IT.

00:58:14.660 --> 00:58:16.495 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ALL RIGHT.

00:58:15.394 --> 00:58:18.030 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ARE YOU NOW TALKING ABOUT THE

00:58:17.496 --> 00:58:19.532 line:78%
BYPASSING OF THE COURT OF

00:58:18.130 --> 00:58:21.634 line:78%
APPEALS?

00:58:19.632 --> 00:58:22.668 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR.

00:58:21.734 --> 00:58:24.670 line:78%
I'M TALKING ABOUT THE PROCEEDING

00:58:22.768 --> 00:58:25.605 line:78%
BEFORE THE DISTRICT COURT

00:58:24.770 --> 00:58:26.639 line:78%
THROUGH THE COURT OF APPEALS TO

00:58:25.705 --> 00:58:28.674 line:78%
THIS COURT.

00:58:26.739 --> 00:58:30.710 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IF WE DISMISS THIS

00:58:28.774 --> 00:58:31.644 line:78%
APPEAL AS IMPROVIDENTLY GRANTED,

00:58:30.810 --> 00:58:32.745 line:78%
IT WOULD GO BACK TO THE COURT OF

00:58:31.744 --> 00:58:33.746 line:78%
APPEALS.

00:58:32.845 --> 00:58:35.748 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, AS I SAY, I THINK THIS

00:58:33.846 --> 00:58:36.782 line:78%
CASE SHOULD BE DISMISSED.

00:58:35.848 --> 00:58:38.784 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, REALLY WHAT YOU MEAN,

00:58:36.883 --> 00:58:39.752 line:78%
ISN'T IT, YOU THINK THAT THE

00:58:38.885 --> 00:58:40.887 line:78%
ORDER OF JUDGE SIRICA SHOULD BE

00:58:39.852 --> 00:58:41.320 line:78%
VACATED --

00:58:40.987 --> 00:58:41.854 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SET ASIDE.

00:58:41.420 --> 00:58:42.889 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND SET ASIDE.

00:58:41.954 --> 00:58:43.856 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT, YES.

00:58:42.989 --> 00:58:44.824 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S QUITE DIFFERENT FROM

00:58:43.956 --> 00:58:45.858 line:78%
DISMISSING THE CASE.

00:58:44.924 --> 00:58:46.926 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I AGREE.

00:58:45.958 --> 00:58:47.260 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S DECIDING IT ON THE

00:58:47.026 --> 00:58:47.894 line:78%
MERITS.

00:58:47.360 --> 00:58:48.928 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT.

00:58:47.994 --> 00:58:49.962 line:78%
THAT'S WHY I'M TRYING TO GET

00:58:49.028 --> 00:58:51.998 line:78%
ACROSS TO THIS COURT, PERHAPS ON

00:58:50.062 --> 00:58:52.999 line:78%
OUR PLEA, THIS CASE SHOULD BE

00:58:52.098 --> 00:58:55.067 line:78%
DISPOSED OF, BE IT BY VACATING

00:58:53.099 --> 00:58:57.103 line:78%
THE ORDER BELOW OR NOT.

00:58:55.167 --> 00:58:58.070 line:78%
BUT, IN ANY EVENT, IT IS

00:58:57.203 --> 00:58:59.071 line:78%
IMPROPER IN OUR VIEW THAT THIS

00:58:58.170 --> 00:59:06.078 line:78%
CASE SHOULD BE HEARD IN THE

00:58:59.171 --> 00:59:08.047 line:78%
CONTEXT IT IS NOW BEING HEARD.

00:59:06.178 --> 00:59:09.081 line:78%
WE WOULDN'T BE HERE ON JULY 8

00:59:08.147 --> 00:59:10.082 line:78%
BEFORE A CROWDED COURTROOM IF IT

00:59:09.181 --> 00:59:11.150 line:78%
WAS NOT RECOGNIZED GENERALLY.

00:59:10.182 --> 00:59:11.617 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IT'S A POLITICAL

00:59:11.250 --> 00:59:12.118 line:78%
QUESTION HERE --

00:59:11.717 --> 00:59:13.052 line:78%
&gt;&gt; EXACTLY RIGHT.

00:59:12.218 --> 00:59:14.120 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S A POLITICAL QUESTION IN

00:59:13.152 --> 00:59:15.154 line:78%
THE DISTRICT COURT.

00:59:14.220 --> 00:59:16.155 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND, THEREFORE, IT'S A

00:59:15.254 --> 00:59:19.091 line:78%
NON-JUSTICIABLE ISSUE IN THIS

00:59:16.255 --> 00:59:20.159 line:78%
AND IN THE DISTRICT COURT.

00:59:19.191 --> 00:59:21.227 line:78%
WHAT HAS HAPPENED IN THIS CASE

00:59:20.259 --> 00:59:22.228 line:78%
IS --

00:59:21.327 --> 00:59:27.433 line:78%
&gt;&gt; DID YOU ARGUE THAT TO THE

00:59:22.328 --> 00:59:28.367 line:78%
DISTRICT JUDGE?

00:59:27.533 --> 00:59:29.302 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I BELIEVE WE ARGUED A

00:59:28.467 --> 00:59:30.369 line:78%
NON-JUSTICIABILITY ARGUMENT.

00:59:29.402 --> 00:59:35.574 line:78%
YES, SIR.

00:59:30.469 --> 00:59:36.475 line:78%
I KNOW WE DID, BUT IF YOU'RE --

00:59:35.675 --> 00:59:39.512 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOUR POSITION IS THAT THE

00:59:36.575 --> 00:59:40.446 line:78%
ISSUANCE OF A SUBPOENA DUCES

00:59:39.612 --> 00:59:43.549 line:78%
TECUM IS NOT A JUSTICIABLE

00:59:40.546 --> 00:59:45.451 line:78%
ISSUE.

00:59:43.649 --> 00:59:48.521 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN THIS CONTEXT AT THIS TIME,

00:59:45.551 --> 00:59:51.524 line:78%
SIR.

00:59:48.621 --> 00:59:53.559 line:78%
WHAT HAS HAPPENED IS THIS.

00:59:51.624 --> 00:59:55.561 line:78%
AS YOU KNOW, ON FEBRUARY 24, A

00:59:53.659 --> 00:59:56.595 line:78%
GRAND JURY SECRETLY NAMED THE

00:59:55.661 --> 00:59:58.631 line:78%
PRESIDENT AMONG OTHERS AS AN

00:59:56.696 --> 01:00:02.768 line:78%
UNINDICTED CO-CONSPIRATOR.

00:59:58.731 --> 01:00:04.804 line:78%
THAT FACT WAS NOT MADE KNOWN.

01:00:02.868 --> 01:00:05.771 line:78%
ON MARCH 1, AN INDICTMENT WAS

01:00:04.904 --> 01:00:09.842 line:78%
RETURNED AGAINST A NUMBER OF THE

01:00:05.871 --> 01:00:11.811 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S CHIEF AIDS.

01:00:09.942 --> 01:00:13.813 line:78%
COINCIDENT WITH THAT IN AN OPEN

01:00:11.911 --> 01:00:15.848 line:78%
COURTROOM, THE ASSISTANT

01:00:13.913 --> 01:00:17.883 line:78%
PROSECUTOR, SPECIAL PROSECUTOR,

01:00:15.948 --> 01:00:19.919 line:78%
HANDED UP TO THE JUDGE A BAG

01:00:17.984 --> 01:00:20.953 line:78%
TOGETHER WITH A SEALED LETTER

01:00:20.019 --> 01:00:23.956 line:78%
REQUESTING THAT THIS MATERIAL BE

01:00:21.053 --> 01:00:26.025 line:78%
SENT OVER TO THE HOUSE OF

01:00:24.056 --> 01:00:28.027 line:78%
REPRESENTATIVES.

01:00:26.125 --> 01:00:29.028 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT TOOK NO POSITION

01:00:28.127 --> 01:00:33.032 line:78%
REGARDING THAT PROPOSAL BECAUSE

01:00:29.128 --> 01:00:34.000 line:78%
HE CONSIDERED IT TO BE PROBABLY

01:00:33.132 --> 01:00:36.035 line:78%
APPROPRIATE, UNDER THE BELIEF

01:00:34.100 --> 01:00:39.105 line:78%
THAT THERE WAS NOTHING

01:00:36.135 --> 01:00:40.106 line:78%
ACCUSATORY IN THAT MATERIAL.

01:00:39.205 --> 01:00:43.142 line:78%
JUDGE SIRICA, HIMSELF, REVIEWED

01:00:40.206 --> 01:00:45.277 line:78%
THE MATERIAL, FOUND NOTHING

01:00:43.242 --> 01:00:46.245 line:78%
ACCUSATORY AND SAID IT WOULD

01:00:45.378 --> 01:00:47.279 line:78%
THEREFORE BE QUITE APPROPRIATE

01:00:46.345 --> 01:00:48.280 line:78%
TO SEND THIS MATERIAL TO THE

01:00:47.380 --> 01:00:49.281 line:78%
HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES NOT

01:00:48.381 --> 01:00:51.283 line:78%
REALIZING AND NOT KNOWING THAT

01:00:49.382 --> 01:00:55.221 line:78%
THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR HAD

01:00:51.384 --> 01:00:56.956 line:78%
PREVIOUSLY OBTAINED A SECRET

01:00:56.322 --> 01:00:57.623 line:78%
CHARGE AGAINST THE PRESIDENT AND

01:00:57.056 --> 01:01:00.393 line:78%
OTHERS WHICH WAS DEFINITELY

01:00:58.090 --> 01:01:02.395 line:78%
ACCUSATORY.

01:01:00.493 --> 01:01:03.462 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT THAT, AS I UNDERSTAND IT,

01:01:02.495 --> 01:01:04.497 line:78%
WAS NOT AMONG THE MATERIAL THAT

01:01:03.562 --> 01:01:06.532 line:78%
WAS CONVEYED TO THE GRAND JURY.

01:01:04.597 --> 01:01:07.500 line:78%
THERE SEEMS TO BE, IF I'M -- AT

01:01:06.632 --> 01:01:08.467 line:78%
LEAST THAT'S WHAT I UNDERSTOOD

01:01:07.600 --> 01:01:11.604 line:78%
MR. JAWORSKI TO TELL US THIS

01:01:08.567 --> 01:01:12.571 line:78%
MORNING.

01:01:11.704 --> 01:01:14.540 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE MATERIAL WAS TURNED OVER.

01:01:12.671 --> 01:01:16.575 line:78%
IT WAS BEFORE THE GRAND JURY.

01:01:14.640 --> 01:01:17.576 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOW, JUST A MOMENT.

01:01:16.675 --> 01:01:18.577 line:78%
I UNDERSTOOD MR. JAWORSKI TO

01:01:17.676 --> 01:01:20.579 line:78%
TELL US THIS MORNING, VERY

01:01:18.677 --> 01:01:22.648 line:78%
UNAMBIGUOUSLY AND EXPLICITLY,

01:01:20.679 --> 01:01:23.649 line:78%
THAT THE FACT THAT THE PRESIDENT

01:01:22.748 --> 01:01:24.650 line:78%
WAS NAMED AS AN UNINDICTED

01:01:23.749 --> 01:01:27.753 line:78%
CO-CONSPIRATOR WAS NOT CONVEYED

01:01:24.750 --> 01:01:29.822 line:78%
TO THE GRAND JURY.

01:01:27.853 --> 01:01:30.823 line:78%
&gt;&gt; A GRAND JURY --

01:01:29.922 --> 01:01:31.791 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT WAS RELEASED, I THINK, TO

01:01:30.923 --> 01:01:32.792 line:78%
THE HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES.

01:01:31.891 --> 01:01:33.826 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, IT WAS NOT.

01:01:32.892 --> 01:01:34.827 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THOUGHT-

01:01:33.926 --> 01:01:35.795 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE MATERIAL WAS SENT TO THE

01:01:34.927 --> 01:01:37.830 line:78%
HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES IN THE

01:01:35.895 --> 01:01:40.933 line:78%
BELIEF THAT IT WAS

01:01:37.930 --> 01:01:41.867 line:78%
NON-ACCUSATORY IN NATURE.

01:01:41.033 --> 01:01:44.970 line:78%
IT WAS SIMPLY A RECITAL OF

01:01:41.967 --> 01:01:47.006 line:78%
FACTS.

01:01:45.071 --> 01:01:48.007 line:78%
&gt;&gt; EXACTLY, AND THAT'S WHAT MR.

01:01:47.106 --> 01:01:48.941 line:78%
JAWORSKI HAS REPRESENTED AGAIN

01:01:48.107 --> 01:01:51.043 line:78%
TO US THIS MORNING, WAS THE FACT

01:01:49.041 --> 01:01:52.044 line:78%
OF THE MATTER.

01:01:51.143 --> 01:01:53.045 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT THE --MR. JAWORSKI HAD

01:01:52.144 --> 01:01:54.013 line:78%
AVAILABLE TO HIM, UNKNOWN TO THE

01:01:53.145 --> 01:01:55.081 line:78%
JUDGE AND UNKNOWN TO COUNSEL FOR

01:01:54.113 --> 01:01:56.048 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT, A SECRET

01:01:55.181 --> 01:02:00.086 line:78%
INDICTMENT NAMING THE PRESIDENT

01:01:56.148 --> 01:02:02.154 line:78%
AS A CO-CONSPIRATOR.

01:02:00.186 --> 01:02:02.455 line:78%
THE ACCUSATORY PART FOLLOWED

01:02:02.254 --> 01:02:05.057 line:78%
LATER.

01:02:02.555 --> 01:02:08.094 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOW, FOLLOWED IN WHAT FORM?

01:02:05.157 --> 01:02:09.128 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BY A NEWSPAPER LEAK.

01:02:08.194 --> 01:02:10.096 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, IT WASN'T SENT FROM THE

01:02:09.228 --> 01:02:11.230 line:78%
COURT OVER TO THE HOUSE, WAS IT?

01:02:10.196 --> 01:02:11.964 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT DIDN'T HAVE TO BE.

01:02:11.330 --> 01:02:13.132 line:78%
ALL THEY HAD TO DO WAS READ THE

01:02:12.064 --> 01:02:14.033 line:78%
NEWSPAPER.

01:02:13.232 --> 01:02:17.203 line:78%
THERE CAN BE NO QUESTION ABOUT

01:02:14.166 --> 01:02:18.204 line:78%
IT.

01:02:17.303 --> 01:02:19.238 line:78%
AND THEREFORE, I SAY, THIS CASE

01:02:18.304 --> 01:02:20.206 line:78%
HAS TO BE VIEWED REALISTICALLY

01:02:19.338 --> 01:02:24.276 line:78%
IN THE CONTEXT THAT IT IS NOW

01:02:20.306 --> 01:02:25.177 line:78%
BEING HEARD.

01:02:24.376 --> 01:02:28.247 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I'M NOT SURE, PERHAPS YOU CAN

01:02:25.277 --> 01:02:30.282 line:78%
HELP ME.

01:02:28.347 --> 01:02:34.320 line:78%
ARE YOU SUGGESTING THAT THERE

01:02:30.382 --> 01:02:36.322 line:78%
WAS SOME DUTY ON THE PART OF THE

01:02:34.420 --> 01:02:38.357 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR TO DISCLOSE

01:02:36.422 --> 01:02:41.393 line:78%
TO THE DISTRICT JUDGE THAT THERE

01:02:38.457 --> 01:02:44.396 line:78%
WAS THIS SECRET INDICTMENT

01:02:41.494 --> 01:02:45.364 line:78%
BEFORE THE JUDGE PASSED ON

01:02:44.497 --> 01:02:48.400 line:78%
WHETHER THE MATERIAL SHOULD BE

01:02:45.464 --> 01:02:49.401 line:78%
SENT TO THE HOUSE?

01:02:48.501 --> 01:02:51.403 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THINK IT WOULD'VE BEEN

01:02:49.502 --> 01:02:52.404 line:78%
QUITE APPROPRIATE BECAUSE THE

01:02:51.504 --> 01:02:53.372 line:78%
JUDGE'S DECISION WAS BASED ON

01:02:52.505 --> 01:02:55.441 line:78%
THE PROPOSITION THERE WAS

01:02:53.472 --> 01:02:58.410 line:78%
NOTHING ACCUSATORY.

01:02:55.541 --> 01:03:00.513 line:78%
THAT, UNDER THE CIRCUMSTANCES,

01:02:58.511 --> 01:03:01.480 line:78%
ABSOLUTE FAIRNESS WAS

01:03:00.613 --> 01:03:02.448 line:78%
APPROPRIATE AND REQUIRED IN SO

01:03:01.580 --> 01:03:04.517 line:78%
FAR AS THE PRESIDENT WAS

01:03:02.548 --> 01:03:06.552 line:78%
CONCERNED.

01:03:04.617 --> 01:03:07.520 line:78%
NO ONE COULD ARGUE THAT THE

01:03:06.652 --> 01:03:09.522 line:78%
INDICTMENT AS A CO-CONSPIRATOR

01:03:07.620 --> 01:03:13.559 line:78%
OR NAMING AS A CO-CONSPIRATOR

01:03:09.622 --> 01:03:14.527 line:78%
DOES ANYTHING BUT IMPAIR THE

01:03:13.659 --> 01:03:16.529 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S POSITION BEFORE THE

01:03:14.627 --> 01:03:18.564 line:78%
HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES.

01:03:16.629 --> 01:03:19.498 line:78%
THAT SHOULD, IN MY JUDGMENT,

01:03:18.664 --> 01:03:20.599 line:78%
HAVE BEEN MADE KNOWN TO THE

01:03:19.598 --> 01:03:22.668 line:78%
JUDGE.

01:03:20.699 --> 01:03:23.669 line:78%
I DON'T KNOW WHAT HE WOULD'VE

01:03:22.768 --> 01:03:25.704 line:78%
DONE UNDER THOSE CIRCUMSTANCES.

01:03:23.769 --> 01:03:26.739 line:78%
HIS DECISION WAS BASED SOLIDLY

01:03:25.804 --> 01:03:29.675 line:78%
ON THE PROPOSITION THERE WAS

01:03:26.839 --> 01:03:34.947 line:78%
NOTHING ACCUSATORY IN THE

01:03:29.775 --> 01:03:35.748 line:78%
MATERIAL.

01:03:35.047 --> 01:03:36.749 line:78%
NOW, MY BROTHER SAYS IN HIS

01:03:35.848 --> 01:03:39.752 line:78%
BRIEF THAT THIS MATERIAL HE NOW

01:03:36.849 --> 01:03:42.788 line:78%
SEEKS, OF COURSE, WOULD BE

01:03:39.852 --> 01:03:43.822 line:78%
AVAILABLE TO THE HOUSE COMMITTEE

01:03:42.888 --> 01:03:44.823 line:78%
AND WILL BE USED TO DETERMINE

01:03:43.923 --> 01:03:45.891 line:78%
WHETHER OR NOT THE PRESIDENT

01:03:44.924 --> 01:03:46.825 line:78%
SHOULD BE IMPEACHED.

01:03:45.991 --> 01:03:49.995 line:78%
SO, THIS FUSION IS GOING TO

01:03:46.926 --> 01:03:50.996 line:78%
CONTINUE.

01:03:50.095 --> 01:03:53.966 line:78%
AND UNDER THE CONSTITUTION, AS

01:03:51.096 --> 01:03:56.001 line:78%
WE VIEW IT, ONLY THE LEGISLATURE

01:03:54.066 --> 01:04:00.039 line:78%
HAS THE RIGHT TO CONDUCT

01:03:56.101 --> 01:04:01.040 line:78%
IMPEACHMENT PROCEEDINGS.

01:04:00.139 --> 01:04:02.007 line:78%
THE COURTS HAVE BEEN, FROM THE

01:04:01.140 --> 01:04:03.042 line:78%
HISTORY INVOLVED AND FROM THE

01:04:02.107 --> 01:04:07.079 line:78%
LANGUAGE OF THE PROVISIONS,

01:04:03.142 --> 01:04:08.113 line:78%
EXCLUDED FROM THAT FUNCTION.

01:04:07.179 --> 01:04:09.181 line:78%
AND, YET, THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR

01:04:08.214 --> 01:04:10.082 line:78%
IS DRAWING THIS COURT IN TO

01:04:09.281 --> 01:04:17.156 line:78%
THOSE PROCEEDINGS INEVITABLY AND

01:04:10.182 --> 01:04:18.157 line:78%
INEXORABLY.

01:04:17.256 --> 01:04:20.159 line:78%
NO ONE COULD STAND HERE AND

01:04:18.257 --> 01:04:21.160 line:78%
ARGUE WITH ANY CANDOR THAT THE

01:04:20.259 --> 01:04:23.162 line:78%
DECISION OF THIS COURT WOULD

01:04:21.260 --> 01:04:25.197 line:78%
HAVE NO IMPACT WHATSOEVER ON THE

01:04:23.262 --> 01:04:27.166 line:78%
PENDING INQUIRY BEFORE THE HOUSE

01:04:25.297 --> 01:04:28.133 line:78%
OF REPRESENTATIVES CONCERNING

01:04:27.266 --> 01:04:33.405 line:78%
THE IMPEACHMENT OF THE

01:04:28.234 --> 01:04:40.312 line:78%
PRESIDENT.

01:04:33.505 --> 01:04:42.281 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HOW FAR DOES YOUR POINT GO?

01:04:40.412 --> 01:04:44.316 line:78%
LET'S ASSUME THAT A MURDER TOOK

01:04:42.381 --> 01:04:50.389 line:78%
PLACE ON THE STREETS OF

01:04:44.416 --> 01:04:51.423 line:78%
WASHINGTON OF WHICH THE

01:04:50.489 --> 01:04:52.391 line:78%
PRESIDENT HAPPENED TO BE ONE OF

01:04:51.523 --> 01:04:53.392 line:78%
THE VERY FEW EYEWITNESSES, AND

01:04:52.491 --> 01:04:54.560 line:78%
SOMEBODY WAS INDICTED FOR THAT

01:04:53.492 --> 01:04:55.160 line:78%
MURDER AND THE PRESIDENT WAS

01:04:54.660 --> 01:04:55.794 line:78%
SUBPOENAED AS A WITNESS.

01:04:55.261 --> 01:04:56.528 line:78%
WOULD YOU SAY HE CANNOT BE

01:04:55.894 --> 01:04:58.464 line:78%
SUBPOENAED NOW BECAUSE THERE IS

01:04:56.629 --> 01:04:59.465 line:78%
AN IMPEACHMENT INQUIRY GOING ON

01:04:58.564 --> 01:05:00.466 line:78%
AND THE COURTS ABSOLUTELY HAVE

01:04:59.565 --> 01:05:01.367 line:78%
TO STOP DEAD ON THEIR TRACKS OF

01:05:00.566 --> 01:05:02.434 line:78%
DOING THEIR ORDINARY JUDICIAL

01:05:01.467 --> 01:05:04.436 line:78%
BUSINESS?

01:05:02.534 --> 01:05:05.437 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I WOULD NOT SAY THAT.

01:05:04.536 --> 01:05:06.472 line:78%
I DON'T THINK HE COULD BE

01:05:05.537 --> 01:05:07.439 line:78%
NECESSARILY SUBPOENAED.

01:05:06.572 --> 01:05:09.441 line:78%
I DON'T THINK THE PRESIDENT IS

01:05:07.539 --> 01:05:10.476 line:78%
SUBJECT TO THE PROCESS OF THE

01:05:09.541 --> 01:05:11.510 line:78%
COURT, UNLESS HE SO DETERMINES

01:05:10.576 --> 01:05:13.479 line:78%
HE WOULD GIVE EVIDENCE.

01:05:11.610 --> 01:05:14.446 line:78%
BUT, THE MURDER WOULD HAVE --

01:05:13.579 --> 01:05:15.547 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SETTING THAT TO ONE SIDE.

01:05:14.546 --> 01:05:16.582 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN THIS CASE --

01:05:15.648 --> 01:05:18.617 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU'RE SAYING THAT THE

01:05:16.682 --> 01:05:19.585 line:78%
COURTS, AS I UNDERSTAND IT, HAVE

01:05:18.717 --> 01:05:22.655 line:78%
TO STOP DEAD IN THEIR TRACKS

01:05:19.685 --> 01:05:23.622 line:78%
FROM DOING THEIR ORDINARY

01:05:22.755 --> 01:05:25.691 line:78%
BUSINESS IN ANY MATTER INVOLVING

01:05:23.722 --> 01:05:26.692 line:78%
EVEN, TANGENTIALLY, THE

01:05:25.791 --> 01:05:28.761 line:78%
PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES

01:05:26.792 --> 01:05:34.700 line:78%
IF OR AS OF WHEN THE COMMITTEE

01:05:28.861 --> 01:05:37.870 line:78%
OF THE HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVE

01:05:36.702 --> 01:05:38.871 line:78%
S IS INVESTIGATING IMPEACHMENT.

01:05:37.970 --> 01:05:39.905 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, JUSTICE STEWART, I'M NOT.

01:05:38.971 --> 01:05:40.973 line:78%
THE SUBJECT MATTER -- THESE TWO

01:05:40.005 --> 01:05:41.307 line:78%
MATTERS, IS THE SAME SUBJECT

01:05:41.073 --> 01:05:41.907 line:78%
MATTER.

01:05:41.407 --> 01:05:42.941 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, HERE ARE --

01:05:42.007 --> 01:05:43.876 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SHOULD THE PRESIDENT --

01:05:43.042 --> 01:05:44.977 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SEVEN PEOPLE HAVE BEEN

01:05:43.976 --> 01:05:46.011 line:78%
INDICTED.

01:05:45.077 --> 01:05:46.412 line:78%
SIX OF WHOM REMAIN UNDER

01:05:46.111 --> 01:05:47.012 line:78%
INDICTMENT.

01:05:46.512 --> 01:05:47.946 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT.

01:05:47.112 --> 01:05:49.081 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE TRIAL IS SCHEDULED FOR

01:05:48.047 --> 01:05:49.448 line:78%
NEXT SEPTEMBER 9.

01:05:49.181 --> 01:05:50.149 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT.

01:05:49.548 --> 01:05:50.983 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE PROSECUTOR IS PREPARING

01:05:50.249 --> 01:05:52.051 line:78%
FOR THAT TRIAL.

01:05:51.083 --> 01:05:57.222 line:78%
HE IS TRYING TO, UNDER RULE 17

01:05:52.151 --> 01:05:58.157 line:78%
OF THE FEDERAL RULES OF CRIMINAL

01:05:57.323 --> 01:05:58.824 line:78%
PROCEDURE, TO ADDUCE MATTERS TO

01:05:58.257 --> 01:06:00.159 line:78%
BE USED IN EVIDENCE AT THAT

01:05:58.924 --> 01:06:03.128 line:78%
TRIAL.

01:06:00.259 --> 01:06:05.197 line:78%
YOU SAY THAT CANNOT GO FORWARD

01:06:03.228 --> 01:06:08.267 line:78%
BECAUSE OF SOME TANGENTIAL

01:06:05.297 --> 01:06:13.238 line:78%
EFFECT OR, YOU SAY, DIRECT

01:06:08.367 --> 01:06:16.175 line:78%
EFFECT UPON SOME OTHER MATTER

01:06:13.339 --> 01:06:18.243 line:78%
GOING OUT IN ANOTHER BRANCH OF

01:06:16.275 --> 01:06:20.279 line:78%
THE GOVERNMENT.

01:06:18.344 --> 01:06:21.280 line:78%
AND HOW FAR DOES YOUR --

01:06:20.379 --> 01:06:23.282 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I SAY IT SHOULD NOT GO

01:06:21.380 --> 01:06:26.285 line:78%
FORWARD A THIS TIME, AT THE VERY

01:06:23.382 --> 01:06:27.319 line:78%
LEAST, BECAUSE THE SUBJECT

01:06:26.385 --> 01:06:28.354 line:78%
MATTER BEING INQUIRED OF IN THE

01:06:27.419 --> 01:06:29.355 line:78%
LARGE MEASURE BEFORE THE HOUSE

01:06:28.454 --> 01:06:30.322 line:78%
COMMITTEE IS EXACTLY THE SAME

01:06:29.455 --> 01:06:31.323 line:78%
SUBJECT MATTER BEING INVOLVED IN

01:06:30.422 --> 01:06:32.358 line:78%
THIS ARGUMENT.

01:06:31.423 --> 01:06:33.325 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HOW DO WE KNOW?

01:06:32.458 --> 01:06:34.293 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NAMELY, SHOULD THE PRESIDENT

01:06:33.425 --> 01:06:35.327 line:78%
PRODUCE TAPES?

01:06:34.393 --> 01:06:36.328 line:78%
SHOULD HE --

01:06:35.427 --> 01:06:37.363 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, WHAT --

01:06:36.428 --> 01:06:38.364 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOT STAND ON --

01:06:37.463 --> 01:06:39.365 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ONE IN THESE TAPES INVOLVES

01:06:38.464 --> 01:06:40.399 line:78%
THE IMPEACHMENT PROCEEDINGS.

01:06:39.465 --> 01:06:41.467 line:78%
&gt;&gt; PARDON?

01:06:40.499 --> 01:06:42.568 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHAT, IN ANY OF THESE TAPES,

01:06:41.567 --> 01:06:42.968 line:78%
IS INVOLVED IN THE IMPEACHMENT

01:06:42.668 --> 01:06:43.669 line:78%
PROCEEDINGS?

01:06:43.068 --> 01:06:44.503 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IF YOUR HONOR PLEASE,

01:06:43.769 --> 01:06:45.404 line:78%
THE HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES

01:06:44.603 --> 01:06:46.505 line:78%
HAVE SUBPOENAED THESE AND MORE

01:06:45.504 --> 01:06:47.439 line:78%
TAPES.

01:06:46.605 --> 01:06:48.474 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I DON'T KNOW WHICH OF

01:06:47.539 --> 01:06:49.475 line:78%
THE TAPES.

01:06:48.574 --> 01:06:50.576 line:78%
I ASSUME YOU DO.

01:06:49.575 --> 01:06:51.744 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, I DON'T.

01:06:50.676 --> 01:06:52.378 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU DON'T KNOW EITHER.

01:06:51.844 --> 01:06:53.178 line:78%
WELL, HOW DO YOU KNOW THAT

01:06:52.478 --> 01:06:57.616 line:78%
THEY'RE SUBJECT TO THE GREATER

01:06:53.278 --> 01:06:58.650 line:78%
PRIVILEGE?

01:06:57.716 --> 01:07:03.856 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I DO KNOW THAT THERE'S

01:06:58.751 --> 01:07:04.757 line:78%
A PRELIMINARY SHOWING THAT THEY

01:07:03.956 --> 01:07:05.824 line:78%
ARE CONVERSATIONS BETWEEN THE

01:07:04.857 --> 01:07:06.125 line:78%
PRESIDENT AND HIS CLOSE AIDS,

01:07:05.924 --> 01:07:06.792 line:78%
AND --

01:07:06.225 --> 01:07:07.726 line:78%
&gt;&gt; REGARDLESS OF WHAT IT IS.

01:07:06.892 --> 01:07:08.694 line:78%
&gt;&gt; REGARDLESS OF WHAT IT IS AND

01:07:07.826 --> 01:07:09.728 line:78%
MAY INVOLVE A NUMBER OF

01:07:08.794 --> 01:07:10.763 line:78%
SUBJECTS.

01:07:09.828 --> 01:07:11.730 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT YOU DON'T KNOW.

01:07:10.863 --> 01:07:12.765 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT DOES NOT THE SPECIAL

01:07:11.830 --> 01:07:14.867 line:78%
PROSECUTOR CLAIM THAT THE

01:07:12.865 --> 01:07:15.834 line:78%
SUBJECT MATTER IS THE SAME?

01:07:14.967 --> 01:07:17.870 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HE CLAIMS THAT, BUT HE HAS NO

01:07:15.934 --> 01:07:18.837 line:78%
WAY OF SHOWING IT.

01:07:17.970 --> 01:07:20.873 line:78%
IN FACT, HE SAYS IT'S ONLY

01:07:18.937 --> 01:07:22.875 line:78%
PROBABLE OR LIKELY.

01:07:20.973 --> 01:07:23.842 line:78%
THERE IS NO WAY OF SHOWING THAT

01:07:22.975 --> 01:07:24.877 line:78%
THEY, IN FACT, INVOLVE THE

01:07:23.942 --> 01:07:26.845 line:78%
SUBJECTS OF WATERGATE.

01:07:24.977 --> 01:07:28.881 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THIS CLAIM WAS HONORED BUT

01:07:26.945 --> 01:07:30.916 line:78%
THIS COURT -- ALL WOULD HAVE TO

01:07:28.981 --> 01:07:31.917 line:78%
LEAVE THE EVIDENCE AND GO TO

01:07:31.016 --> 01:07:34.987 line:78%
JUDGE SIRICA WHO WOULD TAKE IT,

01:07:32.017 --> 01:07:35.988 line:78%
EXAMINE IT IN CAMERAS.

01:07:35.087 --> 01:07:37.990 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I PRESUME THAT'S SO AND HE

01:07:36.088 --> 01:07:38.991 line:78%
WOULD THEN -- IT WOULD BE MADE

01:07:38.090 --> 01:07:42.060 line:78%
AVAILABLE TO THE SPECIAL

01:07:39.091 --> 01:07:43.095 line:78%
PROSECUTOR.

01:07:42.161 --> 01:07:44.129 line:78%
THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR SAYS

01:07:43.195 --> 01:07:45.097 line:78%
THAT, OF COURSE, THIS WOULD THEN

01:07:44.229 --> 01:07:47.099 line:78%
BECOME PART OF THE IMPEACHMENT

01:07:45.197 --> 01:07:48.100 line:78%
PROCEEDINGS, AND HERE WE ARE.

01:07:47.199 --> 01:07:50.135 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. ST. CLAIR, GOING BACK TO

01:07:48.200 --> 01:07:52.137 line:78%
THIS MURDER WITNESS SITUATION.

01:07:50.235 --> 01:07:54.106 line:78%
IF THE PRESIDENT, ANY PRESIDENT,

01:07:52.237 --> 01:07:55.107 line:78%
WITNESSED AN AUTOMOBILE ACCIDENT

01:07:54.206 --> 01:07:59.244 line:78%
AND WAS THE SOLE WITNESS OF

01:07:55.207 --> 01:08:02.214 line:78%
MURDER, AS MR. JUSTICE STEWART

01:07:59.344 --> 01:08:04.249 line:78%
SUGGESTED, YOU'RE NOT INDICATING

01:08:02.314 --> 01:08:05.284 line:78%
THAT HIS TESTIMONY, HIS

01:08:04.349 --> 01:08:06.285 line:78%
EVIDENCE, WOULD NOT BE AVAILABLE

01:08:05.384 --> 01:08:07.286 line:78%
TO THE COURT BUT MERELY THAT HE

01:08:06.385 --> 01:08:09.288 line:78%
CAN'T BE SUBPOENAED BUT MIGHT

01:08:07.386 --> 01:08:10.389 line:78%
GIVE IT BACK BY DEPOSITION AS

01:08:09.388 --> 01:08:10.689 line:78%
SEVERAL PRESIDENTS HAVE IN THE

01:08:10.489 --> 01:08:12.391 line:78%
PAST.

01:08:10.789 --> 01:08:13.392 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT IS QUITE CORRECT.

01:08:12.491 --> 01:08:15.394 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE TESTIMONY OF THE JUSTICES

01:08:13.492 --> 01:08:18.363 line:78%
OF THIS COURT HAS BEEN GIVEN IN

01:08:15.494 --> 01:08:23.635 line:78%
PAST TIMES BY DEPOSITIONS, HAS

01:08:18.464 --> 01:08:24.570 line:78%
IT NOT?

01:08:23.735 --> 01:08:28.607 line:78%
&gt;&gt; REALLY, IT'S A MATTER OF

01:08:24.670 --> 01:08:30.576 line:78%
ACCOMMODATION NOT AS A MATTER OF

01:08:28.707 --> 01:08:31.610 line:78%
ASSERTION OF A RIGHT OF ONE

01:08:30.676 --> 01:08:32.611 line:78%
BRANCH OVER ANOTHER.

01:08:31.710 --> 01:08:33.612 line:78%
BUT THE POINT I WANT TO MAKE,

01:08:32.711 --> 01:08:35.614 line:78%
JUSTICE BURGER, IS THAT THE SAME

01:08:33.712 --> 01:08:36.648 line:78%
SUBJECT MATTER IS INEXORABLY

01:08:35.714 --> 01:08:37.616 line:78%
INVOLVED IN BOTH PROCEEDINGS,

01:08:36.748 --> 01:08:38.650 line:78%
NOW PROCEEDING ON AT THE SAME

01:08:37.716 --> 01:08:39.818 line:78%
TIME.

01:08:38.750 --> 01:08:40.519 line:78%
AND, THE HOUSE OF

01:08:39.918 --> 01:08:40.819 line:78%
REPRESENTATIVES HAS NOT SOUGHT

01:08:40.619 --> 01:08:42.754 line:78%
THE --

01:08:40.919 --> 01:08:43.789 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IF THAT'S TRUE, WHY ARE YOU

01:08:42.855 --> 01:08:45.791 line:78%
WILLING TO GIVE UP 20 OR SO?

01:08:43.889 --> 01:08:47.793 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THAT'S A VERY GOOD

01:08:45.891 --> 01:08:48.760 line:78%
QUESTION I'D LIKE TO ANSWER.

01:08:47.893 --> 01:08:50.762 line:78%
THE DECISIONS THAT ARE MADE IN

01:08:48.861 --> 01:08:51.797 line:78%
AN IMPEACHMENT PROCEEDING,

01:08:50.863 --> 01:08:54.867 line:78%
JUSTICE MARSHALL, ARE

01:08:51.897 --> 01:08:55.968 line:78%
ESSENTIALLY POLITICAL DECISIONS.

01:08:54.967 --> 01:08:56.268 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I'M TALKING ABOUT THIS

01:08:56.068 --> 01:08:57.002 line:78%
CASE.

01:08:56.368 --> 01:08:59.872 line:78%
YOU SAY YOU'LL GIVE UP 20 OF

01:08:57.102 --> 01:09:00.839 line:78%
THEM IN THIS CASE.

01:08:59.972 --> 01:09:03.876 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, WE WILL BECAUSE THEY'VE

01:09:00.939 --> 01:09:04.843 line:78%
ALREADY BEEN MADE PUBLIC.

01:09:03.976 --> 01:09:07.946 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE TAPES OR THE

01:09:04.943 --> 01:09:11.950 line:78%
TRANSCRIPTION?

01:09:08.046 --> 01:09:20.025 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE ARE -- AS SOON AS A JUDGE

01:09:12.050 --> 01:09:23.996 line:78%
APPROVES SOME METHOD OF

01:09:20.125 --> 01:09:24.997 line:78%
VALIDATING THE ACCURACY OF THESE

01:09:24.096 --> 01:09:26.265 line:78%
TAPES, THEY CAN HAVE --

01:09:25.097 --> 01:09:26.999 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE TAPES?

01:09:26.365 --> 01:09:27.599 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THEY CAN HAVE THE TAPES, BUT

01:09:27.099 --> 01:09:28.300 line:78%
YOU HAVE TO UNDERSTAND.

01:09:27.699 --> 01:09:29.067 line:78%
THE TAPE IS A PART OF A REEL.

01:09:28.400 --> 01:09:30.135 line:78%
A REEL MAY COVER A DOZEN

01:09:29.167 --> 01:09:31.169 line:78%
CONVERSATIONS.

01:09:30.235 --> 01:09:32.170 line:78%
SO, THERE'S A MECHANICAL PROBLEM

01:09:31.270 --> 01:09:33.171 line:78%
OF TRYING TO VALIDATE OR BE SURE

01:09:32.271 --> 01:09:34.206 line:78%
THAT THIS IS CORRECT BUT IT'S

01:09:33.272 --> 01:09:35.207 line:78%
ONLY A MECHANICAL PROBLEM.

01:09:34.306 --> 01:09:36.208 line:78%
BUT ONCE THAT'S SOLVED, SUBJECT

01:09:35.307 --> 01:09:37.142 line:78%
TO THE JUDGE BELLOW'S APPROVAL,

01:09:36.308 --> 01:09:38.377 line:78%
THEY HAVE THE AVAILABILITY OF

01:09:37.242 --> 01:09:39.144 line:78%
THAT BUT --

01:09:38.477 --> 01:09:40.212 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WOULD THE TAPES THAT YOU'RE

01:09:39.244 --> 01:09:41.113 line:78%
WILLING TO RELEASE BE VALUABLE

01:09:40.312 --> 01:09:42.147 line:78%
TO THE WATERGATE COMMITTEE IN

01:09:41.213 --> 01:09:43.181 line:78%
TIME?

01:09:42.247 --> 01:09:44.182 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE THINK SO.

01:09:43.282 --> 01:09:45.250 line:78%
THAT'S WHY WE MADE THEM.

01:09:44.283 --> 01:09:46.251 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I THOUGHT YOU SAID YOU

01:09:45.350 --> 01:09:46.618 line:78%
DIDN'T WANT THEM TO HAVE

01:09:46.351 --> 01:09:47.219 line:78%
ANYTHING.

01:09:46.718 --> 01:09:48.287 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR.

01:09:47.319 --> 01:09:49.254 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THIS WAS MERELY AN

01:09:48.387 --> 01:09:50.255 line:78%
EVIDENT WAY OF GETTING STUFF

01:09:49.354 --> 01:09:51.256 line:78%
OVER TO HIM, BUT YOU WERE

01:09:50.355 --> 01:09:52.357 line:78%
GETTING SOME.

01:09:51.356 --> 01:09:54.393 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I SAY THIS.

01:09:52.457 --> 01:09:56.428 line:78%
I SAY THE PRESIDENT SHOULD

01:09:54.493 --> 01:09:57.329 line:78%
DECIDE AS A POLITICAL MATTER OF

01:09:56.528 --> 01:09:59.398 line:78%
WHAT SHOULD BE MADE AVAILABLE TO

01:09:57.429 --> 01:10:00.332 line:78%
THE HOUSE, THAT THE COURT OUGHT

01:09:59.498 --> 01:10:03.402 line:78%
NOT TO BE DRAWN INTO THAT

01:10:00.432 --> 01:10:04.403 line:78%
DECISION.

01:10:03.502 --> 01:10:05.337 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S THE PROBLEM.

01:10:04.503 --> 01:10:06.438 line:78%
HE HAS NO RIGHT TO TAKE THAT

