&gt;&gt; YOU FILED A MOTION TO QUASH

01:17:07.993 --> 01:17:10.128 line:78%
IT, DIDN'T YOU?

01:17:08.960 --> 01:17:10.829 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND WE --

01:17:10.228 --> 01:17:11.930 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN

01:17:10.929 --> 01:17:12.964 line:78%
IGNORING AND FILING A MOTION TO

01:17:12.030 --> 01:17:14.099 line:78%
QUASH IS WHAT?

01:17:13.064 --> 01:17:14.399 line:78%
I WANT HIS ANSWER.

01:17:14.199 --> 01:17:15.100 line:78%
WHAT?

01:17:14.499 --> 01:17:17.035 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IF YOUR HONOR PLEASE,

01:17:15.200 --> 01:17:19.037 line:78%
WE ARE SUBMITTING THE MATTER --

01:17:17.135 --> 01:17:20.071 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU'RE SUBMITTING THE MATTER

01:17:19.137 --> 01:17:21.072 line:78%
TO THIS COURT.

01:17:20.171 --> 01:17:22.007 line:78%
&gt;&gt; TO THIS COURT, UNDER A

01:17:21.172 --> 01:17:23.074 line:78%
SPECIAL APPEARANCE ON BEHALF OF

01:17:22.107 --> 01:17:24.075 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT.

01:17:23.174 --> 01:17:25.110 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU STILL LEAVE IT UP TO THIS

01:17:24.175 --> 01:17:26.011 line:78%
COURT TO DECIDE IT.

01:17:25.210 --> 01:17:27.078 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, YES, IN A SENSE.

01:17:26.111 --> 01:17:28.113 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES?

01:17:27.178 --> 01:17:29.147 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN A SENSE.

01:17:28.213 --> 01:17:30.181 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IN WHAT SENSE?

01:17:29.247 --> 01:17:32.217 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN THE SENSE THAT THIS COURT

01:17:30.281 --> 01:17:34.285 line:78%
HAS AN OBLIGATION TO DETERMINE

01:17:32.317 --> 01:17:36.354 line:78%
THE LAW, ALRIGHT?

01:17:34.386 --> 01:17:37.355 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT ALSO HAS AN

01:17:36.454 --> 01:17:39.357 line:78%
OBLIGATION TO CARRY OUT HIS

01:17:37.455 --> 01:17:40.358 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL FUNCTIONS.

01:17:39.457 --> 01:17:41.393 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU ARE SUBMITTING TO THIS

01:17:40.458 --> 01:17:42.360 line:78%
COURT FOR US TO DECIDE WHETHER

01:17:41.493 --> 01:17:46.464 line:78%
OR NOT EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE IS

01:17:42.460 --> 01:17:49.467 line:78%
AVAILABLE IN THIS CASE.

01:17:46.564 --> 01:17:52.470 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, PROBABLY, THE QUESTION

01:17:49.567 --> 01:17:54.472 line:78%
IS EVEN MORE LIMITED THAN THAT.

01:17:52.570 --> 01:17:56.508 line:78%
IS THE EXECUTIVE PRIVILEGE,

01:17:54.572 --> 01:17:57.442 line:78%
WHICH MY BROTHER CONCEDES,

01:17:56.608 --> 01:17:58.510 line:78%
ABSOLUTE OR IS IT ONLY

01:17:57.542 --> 01:18:00.512 line:78%
CONDITIONAL?

01:17:58.610 --> 01:18:01.479 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I SAID, IN THIS CASE.

01:18:00.612 --> 01:18:02.514 line:78%
CAN YOU MAKE IT ANY NARROWER

01:18:01.579 --> 01:18:03.581 line:78%
THAN THAT?

01:18:02.614 --> 01:18:04.616 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, SIR.

01:18:03.681 --> 01:18:05.650 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, DO YOU AGREE THAT

01:18:04.716 --> 01:18:07.619 line:78%
THAT'S WHAT'S BEFORE THIS COURT

01:18:05.750 --> 01:18:08.653 line:78%
AND YOU ARE SUBMITTING IT TO

01:18:07.719 --> 01:18:11.689 line:78%
THIS COURT FOR DECISION?

01:18:08.753 --> 01:18:12.690 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THIS IS BEING SUBMITTED TO

01:18:11.790 --> 01:18:13.591 line:78%
THIS COURT FOR ITS GUIDANCE AND

01:18:12.791 --> 01:18:16.728 line:78%
JUDGMENT WITH RESPECT TO THE

01:18:13.691 --> 01:18:17.762 line:78%
LAW.

01:18:16.828 --> 01:18:19.731 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT, ON THE OTHER

01:18:17.862 --> 01:18:21.833 line:78%
HAND, HAS HIS OBLIGATIONS UNDER

01:18:19.831 --> 01:18:22.834 line:78%
THE CONSTITUTION.

01:18:21.933 --> 01:18:26.871 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ARE YOU SUBMITTING IT TO THIS

01:18:22.934 --> 01:18:27.772 line:78%
COURT FOR THIS COURT'S DECISION?

01:18:26.971 --> 01:18:30.975 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AS TO WHAT THE LAW IS, YES,

01:18:27.872 --> 01:18:31.709 line:78%
OF COURSE.

01:18:31.076 --> 01:18:32.911 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IF IT WERE NOT SO, YOU WOULD

01:18:31.810 --> 01:18:33.945 line:78%
NOT BE HERE.

01:18:33.011 --> 01:18:35.980 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I WOULD NOT BE HERE.

01:18:34.045 --> 01:18:38.016 line:78%
NOW, MY BROTHER SAYS I HAVE NO

01:18:36.081 --> 01:18:40.085 line:78%
RIGHT TO EVEN CHALLENGE HIS

01:18:38.116 --> 01:18:41.086 line:78%
RIGHT TO BE HERE, AND I'D LIKE

01:18:40.185 --> 01:18:43.121 line:78%
TO DEAL WITH THAT FOR A MOMENT.

01:18:41.186 --> 01:18:45.056 line:78%
THIS IS, AS WE POINT OUT IN OUR

01:18:43.221 --> 01:18:46.091 line:78%
BRIEF, ESSENTIALLY AN EXECUTIVE

01:18:45.156 --> 01:18:47.092 line:78%
DEPARTMENT MATTER.

01:18:46.191 --> 01:18:49.127 line:78%
WHATEVER MAY HAVE BEEN THE

01:18:47.192 --> 01:18:50.128 line:78%
ARRANGEMENTS BETWEEN THE

01:18:49.227 --> 01:18:51.129 line:78%
BRANCHES OF THE EXECUTIVE MATTER

01:18:50.228 --> 01:18:52.130 line:78%
WITH RESPECT TO EVIDENTIARY

01:18:51.229 --> 01:18:53.198 line:78%
MATTERS, AND IN FACT THERE WERE

01:18:52.230 --> 01:18:55.200 line:78%
NO ARRANGEMENTS REGARDING

01:18:53.298 --> 01:18:56.201 line:78%
EVIDENTIARY MATTERS, IT IS NOT

01:18:55.300 --> 01:18:58.236 line:78%
THE FUNCTION OF THE COURT TO

01:18:56.301 --> 01:18:59.204 line:78%
DIRECT OR RULE WHAT EVIDENCE

01:18:58.336 --> 01:19:01.239 line:78%
WILL BE PRESENTED TO IT BY THE

01:18:59.304 --> 01:19:02.307 line:78%
EXECUTIVE AND THAT EXECUTIVES

01:19:01.339 --> 01:19:03.341 line:78%
DULLY PROSECUTE IT.

01:19:02.407 --> 01:19:04.275 line:78%
IF THIS WAS A UNITED STATES

01:19:03.441 --> 01:19:08.313 line:78%
ATTORNEY, THIS CASE WOULDN'T BE

01:19:04.375 --> 01:19:11.349 line:78%
HERE, OF COURSE.

01:19:08.413 --> 01:19:15.320 line:78%
IT'S HERE ONLY BECAUSE CERTAIN

01:19:11.449 --> 01:19:17.388 line:78%
THINGS WERE DELEGATED TO THE

01:19:15.420 --> 01:19:19.390 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR.

01:19:17.489 --> 01:19:22.460 line:78%
BUT, THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR WAS

01:19:19.491 --> 01:19:25.563 line:78%
NOT DELEGATED THE RIGHT TO TELL

01:19:22.560 --> 01:19:27.565 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT ONE OF HIS

01:19:25.663 --> 01:19:30.602 line:78%
CONVERSATIONS ARE GOING TO BE

01:19:27.665 --> 01:19:31.603 line:78%
MADE AVAILABLE AS EVIDENCE.

01:19:30.702 --> 01:19:32.604 line:78%
THAT WAS SPECIFICALLY RESERVED

01:19:31.703 --> 01:19:33.605 line:78%
AND THE ONLY THING THAT MY

01:19:32.704 --> 01:19:34.572 line:78%
BROTHER CAN DO IS ARGUE ABOUT

01:19:33.705 --> 01:19:36.574 line:78%
IT, AND THAT'S WHAT HE'S DOING

01:19:34.672 --> 01:19:39.644 line:78%
RIGHT HERE TODAY.

01:19:36.674 --> 01:19:41.813 line:78%
AND, THEREFORE --

01:19:39.744 --> 01:19:42.514 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOW, WHY WOULDN'T THIS CASE

01:19:41.913 --> 01:19:43.781 line:78%
BE HERE IF THIS WERE A UNITED

01:19:42.614 --> 01:19:44.782 line:78%
STATES ATTORNEY?

01:19:43.882 --> 01:19:45.750 line:78%
I THINK I AGREE WITH YOU, BUT

01:19:44.883 --> 01:19:46.818 line:78%
I'D LIKE TO ASK YOU YOUR ANSWER

01:19:45.850 --> 01:19:47.852 line:78%
IN KNOWING WHY.

01:19:46.918 --> 01:19:48.853 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THE UNITED STATES

01:19:47.952 --> 01:19:49.888 line:78%
ATTORNEY WOULD BE DIRECTED.

01:19:48.953 --> 01:19:50.889 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BY WHOM?

01:19:49.988 --> 01:19:51.890 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BY THE PRESIDENT OR THE

01:19:50.989 --> 01:19:53.892 line:78%
ATTORNEY GENERAL AT THE

01:19:51.990 --> 01:19:54.893 line:78%
DIRECTION OF THE PRESIDENT.

01:19:53.992 --> 01:19:55.894 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THOUGHT THE ATTORNEY

01:19:54.993 --> 01:19:56.895 line:78%
GENERAL WAS THE ONE WHO DIRECTED

01:19:55.994 --> 01:19:57.896 line:78%
THE UNITED STATES ATTORNEY.

01:19:56.995 --> 01:19:59.964 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BY THE ATTORNEY GENERAL AT

01:19:57.996 --> 01:20:01.032 line:78%
THE DIRECTION OF THE PRESIDENT.

01:20:00.064 --> 01:20:02.000 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, IN THE NORMAL CASE, THE

01:20:01.132 --> 01:20:02.967 line:78%
PRESIDENT DOESN'T KNOW ANYTHING

01:20:02.100 --> 01:20:05.036 line:78%
ABOUT MINE-RUN FEDERAL

01:20:03.067 --> 01:20:06.037 line:78%
PROSECUTIONS.

01:20:05.136 --> 01:20:07.205 line:78%
THAT'S FAIR TO SAY, ISN'T IT?

01:20:06.137 --> 01:20:07.906 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THINK SO, BUT MOST CASES

01:20:07.305 --> 01:20:10.175 line:78%
DON'T INVOLVE PRESIDENTIAL

01:20:08.006 --> 01:20:11.209 line:78%
CONVERSATIONS.

01:20:10.275 --> 01:20:12.377 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND, IN FACT, IN MINE-RUN

01:20:11.309 --> 01:20:13.111 line:78%
CASES THE ATTORNEY GENERAL

01:20:12.477 --> 01:20:13.711 line:78%
DOESN'T KNOW MUCH ABOUT IT.

01:20:13.211 --> 01:20:14.379 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THINK THAT'S --

01:20:13.811 --> 01:20:15.246 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT LET'S -- JUST A

01:20:14.479 --> 01:20:21.386 line:78%
MOMENT.[LAUGHTER]

01:20:15.346 --> 01:20:21.753 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WITH ALL DUE RESPECT.

01:20:21.486 --> 01:20:22.353 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT.

01:20:21.853 --> 01:20:23.354 line:78%
[LAUGHTER]

01:20:22.453 --> 01:20:24.355 line:78%
SO, THE UNITED STATES ATTORNEY

01:20:23.454 --> 01:20:26.357 line:78%
BRINGS TO PROSECUTION AND IN THE

01:20:24.455 --> 01:20:28.359 line:78%
COURSE OF THAT PROSECUTION HE,

01:20:26.457 --> 01:20:29.327 line:78%
BEFORE TRIAL, SUBPOENAS UNDER

01:20:28.459 --> 01:20:33.431 line:78%
RULE 17 OF THE FEDERAL RULES OF

01:20:29.427 --> 01:20:35.466 line:78%
CRIMINAL PROCEDURE.

01:20:33.531 --> 01:20:37.435 line:78%
THE JURY SUBPOENAS MATERIAL IN

01:20:35.567 --> 01:20:40.471 line:78%
THE CUSTODY OF THE PRESIDENT.

01:20:37.535 --> 01:20:41.472 line:78%
SO, WHAT HAPPENS?

01:20:40.572 --> 01:20:42.507 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE PRESIDENT SAYS TO THE

01:20:41.573 --> 01:20:44.509 line:78%
ATTORNEY GENERAL "I'M NOT GOING

01:20:42.607 --> 01:20:46.544 line:78%
TO PRODUCE THIS MATERIAL."

01:20:44.609 --> 01:20:47.679 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, IT'S THE UNITED STATES

01:20:46.644 --> 01:20:48.279 line:78%
ATTORNEY SUBPOENAING IT UNDER

01:20:47.779 --> 01:20:51.649 line:78%
YOUR HYPOTHETICAL CASE.

01:20:48.379 --> 01:20:54.752 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT.

01:20:51.749 --> 01:20:55.753 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND SO, WHAT HAPPENS?

01:20:54.852 --> 01:20:56.821 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN MY VIEW, THE PRESIDENT

01:20:55.853 --> 01:20:57.822 line:78%
WOULD INSTRUCT THE ATTORNEY

01:20:56.921 --> 01:20:58.723 line:78%
GENERAL TO INSTRUCT THE UNITED

01:20:57.922 --> 01:21:01.826 line:78%
STATES ATTORNEY TO WITHDRAW HIS

01:20:58.823 --> 01:21:02.860 line:78%
MOTION.

01:21:01.926 --> 01:21:03.828 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THE UNITED STATES

01:21:02.961 --> 01:21:05.964 line:78%
ATTORNEY SAYS "I'M NOT GOING TO

01:21:03.928 --> 01:21:06.764 line:78%
DO THAT BECAUSE I'M --

01:21:06.064 --> 01:21:07.832 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THEN WE'D HAVE A NEW UNITED

01:21:06.864 --> 01:21:10.802 line:78%
STATES ATTORNEY.

01:21:07.932 --> 01:21:11.836 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE ONE WHO UPHOLDS JUSTICE

01:21:11.703 --> 01:21:14.906 line:78%
--

01:21:13.771 --> 01:21:16.107 line:78%
WELL, HOW WOULD YOU HAVE A NEW

01:21:15.006 --> 01:21:16.774 line:78%
UNITED STATES ATTORNEY?

01:21:16.207 --> 01:21:17.609 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I MADE A LITTLE --

01:21:16.874 --> 01:21:18.009 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, I'M BEING SERIOUS BECAUSE

01:21:17.875 --> 01:21:19.010 line:78%
--

01:21:18.109 --> 01:21:20.011 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THINK THAT UNITED STATES

01:21:19.110 --> 01:21:21.045 line:78%
ATTORNEY, IN ALL RESPECT, WOULD

01:21:20.111 --> 01:21:21.346 line:78%
AND SHOULD BE REMOVED FROM THAT

01:21:21.145 --> 01:21:23.081 line:78%
CASE.

01:21:21.446 --> 01:21:24.082 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I KNOW.

01:21:23.181 --> 01:21:26.050 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE EXECUTIVE POWER OF THE

01:21:24.182 --> 01:21:27.085 line:78%
GOVERNMENT IS NOT VESTED IN THE

01:21:26.150 --> 01:21:28.086 line:78%
UNITED STATES ATTORNEY.

01:21:27.185 --> 01:21:30.054 line:78%
IT'S VESTED IN ONE MAN, AND THAT

01:21:28.186 --> 01:21:33.091 line:78%
MAN IS THE PRESIDENT OF THE

01:21:30.154 --> 01:21:37.095 line:78%
UNITED STATES.

01:21:33.191 --> 01:21:38.029 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IT'S SET BY STATUTE.

01:21:37.195 --> 01:21:39.163 line:78%
IT'S VESTED IN THE LAW

01:21:38.129 --> 01:21:40.231 line:78%
ENFORCEMENT.

01:21:39.264 --> 01:21:40.565 line:78%
IT'S VESTED IN THE ATTORNEY

01:21:40.331 --> 01:21:41.299 line:78%
GENERAL.

01:21:40.665 --> 01:21:42.100 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, BUT THAT STATUTE, WHICH

01:21:41.399 --> 01:21:43.234 line:78%
MY BROTHER CITES IN HIS BRIEF --

01:21:42.200 --> 01:21:44.235 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES?

01:21:43.334 --> 01:21:45.236 line:78%
&gt;&gt; DOES NOT DEPRIVE NOR COULD IT

01:21:44.335 --> 01:21:46.204 line:78%
DEPRIVE THE PRESIDENT OF HIS

01:21:45.336 --> 01:21:47.171 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL AUTHORITY TO BE

01:21:46.304 --> 01:21:48.339 line:78%
THE CHIEF LAW ENFORCEMENT

01:21:47.272 --> 01:21:49.040 line:78%
OFFICER.

01:21:48.439 --> 01:21:49.574 line:78%
HE SHALL TAKE CARE TO SE THAT

01:21:49.140 --> 01:21:50.308 line:78%
THE LAW IS ENFORCED.

01:21:49.674 --> 01:21:51.209 line:78%
THE EXECUTIVE POWER IS VESTED IN

01:21:50.408 --> 01:21:52.243 line:78%
HIM, IN ONE MAN.

01:21:51.309 --> 01:21:53.211 line:78%
AND, THE ATTORNEY GENERAL IS

01:21:52.343 --> 01:21:54.212 line:78%
NOTHING BUT A SURROGATE FOR THE

01:21:53.311 --> 01:22:01.319 line:78%
PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES.

01:21:54.312 --> 01:22:02.353 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT, I'M AFRAID, YOUR

01:22:01.419 --> 01:22:03.288 line:78%
ARGUMENT WOULD BE -- IS A VERY

01:22:02.453 --> 01:22:04.422 line:78%
GOOD AS A MATTER OF POLITICAL

01:22:03.388 --> 01:22:05.590 line:78%
SCIENCE.

01:22:04.522 --> 01:22:06.257 line:78%
IT WOULD BE A VERY FINE ONE AS A

01:22:05.690 --> 01:22:06.958 line:78%
MATTER OF CONSTITUTIONAL AND

01:22:06.357 --> 01:22:07.425 line:78%
PROBABLY STATUTORY LAW, EXCEPT

01:22:07.058 --> 01:22:08.426 line:78%
IT HASN'T.

01:22:07.525 --> 01:22:10.428 line:78%
YOUR CLIENT DEALT HIMSELF OUT OF

01:22:08.526 --> 01:22:11.396 line:78%
THAT ARGUMENT BY WHAT'S BEEN

01:22:10.528 --> 01:22:12.430 line:78%
DONE IN THE CREATION OF THE

01:22:11.496 --> 01:22:14.465 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR.

01:22:12.530 --> 01:22:16.501 line:78%
&gt;&gt; PERHAPS AS TO EVERYTHING --

01:22:14.565 --> 01:22:17.535 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU'VE JUST POINTED OUT THE

01:22:16.601 --> 01:22:18.536 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR IS QUITE

01:22:17.635 --> 01:22:18.903 line:78%
DIFFERENT FROM THE UNITED STATES

01:22:18.636 --> 01:22:19.537 line:78%
ATTORNEY.

01:22:19.003 --> 01:22:20.571 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT.

01:22:19.637 --> 01:22:21.606 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AS A MATTER --

01:22:20.672 --> 01:22:22.607 line:78%
&gt;&gt; PERHAPS, WITH RESPECT TO

01:22:21.706 --> 01:22:23.641 line:78%
EVERYTHING EXCEPT, THE PRESIDENT

01:22:22.707 --> 01:22:25.710 line:78%
DID NOT DELEGATE TO THE SPECIAL

01:22:23.741 --> 01:22:27.745 line:78%
PROSECUTOR THE RIGHT TO TELL HIM

01:22:25.810 --> 01:22:28.746 line:78%
WHETHER OR NOT HIS CONFIDENTIAL

01:22:27.845 --> 01:22:31.883 line:78%
COMMUNICATION SHOULD BE MADE

01:22:28.846 --> 01:22:32.583 line:78%
AVAILABLE AS EVIDENCE.

01:22:31.983 --> 01:22:33.084 line:78%
SO THAT, WITHIN THE PACKAGE OF

01:22:32.684 --> 01:22:33.818 line:78%
EXECUTIVE POWER --

01:22:33.184 --> 01:22:34.752 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT HE HAS --

01:22:33.918 --> 01:22:36.821 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NORMALLY REPRESENTED --

01:22:34.852 --> 01:22:37.855 line:78%
&gt;&gt; EXCUSE ME.

01:22:36.921 --> 01:22:39.857 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NORMALLY REPRESENTED BY THE

01:22:37.955 --> 01:22:40.858 line:78%
EXECUTIVE DEPARTMENT AS TO WHO

01:22:39.957 --> 01:22:42.860 line:78%
SHALL BE PROSECUTOR THAT'S BEEN

01:22:40.958 --> 01:22:44.862 line:78%
DELEGATED TO THIS GENTLEMAN.

01:22:42.960 --> 01:22:46.931 line:78%
HE HAS EXERCISED THAT POWER.

01:22:44.962 --> 01:22:49.000 line:78%
WHEN, HE'S DONE THAT.

01:22:47.031 --> 01:22:52.036 line:78%
WITH WHAT EVIDENCE, HE'S DONE

01:22:49.100 --> 01:22:54.105 line:78%
THAT AS WE'LL DEAL WITH IN A FEW

01:22:52.136 --> 01:22:56.107 line:78%
MOMENTS.

01:22:54.205 --> 01:22:57.108 line:78%
BUT, NOT WITH THAT PORTION OF

01:22:56.207 --> 01:22:58.076 line:78%
THE EVIDENCE THAT'S AVAILABLE

01:22:57.208 --> 01:23:02.180 line:78%
THAT CONSTITUTES PRESIDENTIAL

01:22:58.176 --> 01:23:02.880 line:78%
CONFIDENTIAL COMMUNICATION.

01:23:02.280 --> 01:23:04.082 line:78%
THAT'S BEEN SPECIFICALLY

01:23:02.980 --> 01:23:05.049 line:78%
RESERVED.

01:23:04.182 --> 01:23:06.084 line:78%
AND THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR

01:23:05.149 --> 01:23:07.085 line:78%
CANNOT, AND EVEN IF THE

01:23:06.184 --> 01:23:08.119 line:78%
PRESIDENT DID GIVE HIM THAT

01:23:07.185 --> 01:23:10.121 line:78%
AUTHORITY, PROBABLY COULD NOT,

01:23:08.219 --> 01:23:11.189 line:78%
AS A CONSTITUTIONAL MATTER,

01:23:10.221 --> 01:23:13.191 line:78%
DELEGATE THAT.

01:23:11.289 --> 01:23:14.225 line:78%
BUT IN ANY EVENT, HE DID NOT --

01:23:13.291 --> 01:23:15.326 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HE DIDN'T WHAT?

01:23:14.325 --> 01:23:15.626 line:78%
HE COULD NOT AND PROBABLY COULD

01:23:15.426 --> 01:23:16.294 line:78%
NOT --

01:23:15.727 --> 01:23:17.295 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE RIGHT TO ORDER THE

01:23:16.394 --> 01:23:18.329 line:78%
PRESIDENT TO GIVE UP

01:23:17.395 --> 01:23:19.364 line:78%
CONFIDENTIAL COMMUNICATIONS.

01:23:18.429 --> 01:23:20.365 line:78%
THAT WAS NOT DELEGATED.

01:23:19.464 --> 01:23:21.332 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I KNOW, NOT THE UNFETTERED

01:23:20.465 --> 01:23:22.367 line:78%
RIGHT TO GET IT BUT THE RIGHT TO

01:23:21.432 --> 01:23:23.301 line:78%
GO TO COURT AND ASK A COURT TO

01:23:22.467 --> 01:23:24.402 line:78%
DECIDE WHETHER OR NOT HE'S

01:23:23.401 --> 01:23:26.437 line:78%
ENTITLED TO IT.

01:23:24.502 --> 01:23:27.438 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT, AND THE PRESIDENT,

01:23:26.537 --> 01:23:28.373 line:78%
UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES, GAVE UP

01:23:27.538 --> 01:23:30.541 line:78%
ANY OF HIS DEFENSES WITH RESPECT

01:23:28.473 --> 01:23:31.442 line:78%
TO THAT.

01:23:30.641 --> 01:23:32.610 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU'RE MAKING THOSE DEFENSES

01:23:31.542 --> 01:23:33.378 line:78%
IN --

01:23:32.710 --> 01:23:33.644 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND I'M MAKING THEM RIGHT

01:23:33.478 --> 01:23:35.580 line:78%
NOW.

01:23:33.745 --> 01:23:38.583 line:78%
AND EVEN IF WE DID AGREE BETWEEN

01:23:35.680 --> 01:23:41.519 line:78%
US THAT WE WOULD VEST THIS COURT

01:23:38.683 --> 01:23:42.553 line:78%
WITH JURISDICTION SIMPLY BECAUSE

01:23:41.619 --> 01:23:43.588 line:78%
OF THE POLITICS OF THE

01:23:42.653 --> 01:23:47.592 line:78%
SITUATION, THIS COURT IN ITS

01:23:43.688 --> 01:23:51.596 line:78%
DECISIONS WOULD NOT ACCEPT THE

01:23:47.692 --> 01:23:52.663 line:78%
VESTING OF SUCH JURISDICTION.

01:23:51.696 --> 01:23:53.598 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHY NOT?

01:23:52.764 --> 01:23:55.600 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BECAUSE THIS COURT DETERMINES

01:23:53.698 --> 01:23:58.669 line:78%
ITS JURISDICTION.

01:23:55.700 --> 01:23:59.637 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE DON'T KNOW THAT.

01:23:58.770 --> 01:24:00.671 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE PARTIES CAN AGREE THAT IT

01:23:59.737 --> 01:24:01.672 line:78%
HASN'T BUT-

01:24:00.772 --> 01:24:02.707 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, BUT -- AND IF SURELY

01:24:01.773 --> 01:24:03.674 line:78%
YOU'RE RIGHT, AS I SAY, A

01:24:02.807 --> 01:24:04.675 line:78%
LAWSUIT BETWEEN THE SECRETARY OF

01:24:03.775 --> 01:24:06.677 line:78%
COMMERCE, FOR EXAMPLE, SUING THE

01:24:04.776 --> 01:24:07.645 line:78%
PRESIDENT OVER A MATTER OF

01:24:06.778 --> 01:24:09.680 line:78%
EXECUTIVE POLICY, WE BOTH AGREE,

01:24:07.745 --> 01:24:11.716 line:78%
WOULD BE UNTHINKABLE.

01:24:09.781 --> 01:24:13.718 line:78%
AND SINCE ANY CABINET OFFICER IS

01:24:11.816 --> 01:24:14.719 line:78%
THE CREATURE OF THE PRESIDENT

01:24:13.818 --> 01:24:15.686 line:78%
WHO APPOINTED HIM, THE ANSWER

01:24:14.819 --> 01:24:16.754 line:78%
WOULD BE "YOU'RE FIRED," IF YOU

01:24:15.787 --> 01:24:17.722 line:78%
WANT TO --

01:24:16.854 --> 01:24:18.723 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IF IT GOES THAT FAR.

01:24:17.822 --> 01:24:19.757 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IF IT GOES THAT FAR.

01:24:18.823 --> 01:24:23.795 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT.

01:24:19.857 --> 01:24:26.831 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT AREN'T WE HERE BOTH

01:24:23.895 --> 01:24:28.800 line:78%
FACTUALLY AND, I SUGGEST,

01:24:26.931 --> 01:24:29.867 line:78%
LEGALLY WITH QUITE A DIFFERENT

01:24:28.900 --> 01:24:30.835 line:78%
SITUATION?

01:24:29.967 --> 01:24:32.870 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THINK NOT IN THE TERMS OF

01:24:30.935 --> 01:24:33.838 line:78%
SEPARATION OF POWERS, IF I MAY.

01:24:32.970 --> 01:24:34.839 line:78%
MY BROTHER'S POINT OF VIEW IS,

01:24:33.938 --> 01:24:36.841 line:78%
HE VIEWS HIMSELF AS THE UNITED

01:24:34.939 --> 01:24:38.843 line:78%
STATES AS DISTINGUISHED FROM A

01:24:36.941 --> 01:24:39.877 line:78%
MEMBER OF THE EXECUTIVE BRANCH.

01:24:38.943 --> 01:24:41.913 line:78%
AND, IN HIS BRIEF, HE INVOKES

01:24:39.977 --> 01:24:44.015 line:78%
THE UNITED STATES IS REALLY A

01:24:42.013 --> 01:24:47.018 line:78%
FOURTH ENTITY.

01:24:44.115 --> 01:24:49.086 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THE SOVEREIGN PEOPLE OF

01:24:47.118 --> 01:24:51.088 line:78%
THE UNITED STATES.

01:24:49.187 --> 01:24:54.058 line:78%
&gt;&gt; CONSTITUTIONALLY, A SPECIAL

01:24:51.189 --> 01:24:55.026 line:78%
PROSECUTOR WITH THE POWERS THAT

01:24:54.158 --> 01:24:57.061 line:78%
MY BROTHER SUGGESTS HE HAS IS A

01:24:55.126 --> 01:24:58.062 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL ANOMALY.

01:24:57.161 --> 01:25:03.234 line:78%
WE HAVE ONLY THREE BRANCHES, NOT

01:24:58.162 --> 01:25:08.339 line:78%
THREE-AND-A THIRD OR THREE-AND-A

01:25:03.334 --> 01:25:09.207 line:78%
HALF OR FOUR.

01:25:08.439 --> 01:25:12.210 line:78%
THERE'S ONLY ONE EXECUTIVE

01:25:09.307 --> 01:25:13.211 line:78%
BRANCH AND THE EXECUTIVE POWER

01:25:12.310 --> 01:25:14.212 line:78%
IS VESTED IN A PRESIDENT.

01:25:13.311 --> 01:25:16.214 line:78%
NOW IF, FOR POLITICAL REASONS,

01:25:14.312 --> 01:25:17.215 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT WANTS TO DOLE OUT

01:25:16.314 --> 01:25:19.283 line:78%
SOME OF THOSE POWERS, HE MAY SO

01:25:17.315 --> 01:25:21.352 line:78%
DO AND HAS DONE IN THIS CASE.

01:25:19.383 --> 01:25:23.421 line:78%
BUT, HE CANNOT VEST JURISDICTION

01:25:21.452 --> 01:25:24.489 line:78%
ON A COURT THAT, OTHERWISE, THE

01:25:23.521 --> 01:25:27.558 line:78%
COURT WOULD NOT HAVE NOR SHOULD

01:25:24.589 --> 01:25:28.593 line:78%
THE COURT ACCEPT JURISDICTION.

01:25:27.658 --> 01:25:29.594 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT HASN'T YOUR CLIENT ALSO

01:25:28.693 --> 01:25:30.661 line:78%
INHIBITED HIMSELF FROM THE

01:25:29.694 --> 01:25:31.629 line:78%
ULTIMATE SANCTION THAT YOU

01:25:30.761 --> 01:25:34.632 line:78%
SUGGESTED HE COULD IMPOSE WITH

01:25:31.729 --> 01:25:35.633 line:78%
RESPECT TO YOUR HYPOTHETICAL

01:25:34.732 --> 01:25:36.601 line:78%
UNITED STATES ATTORNEY, I.E. THE

01:25:35.733 --> 01:25:38.603 line:78%
SANCTION OF DISMISSING THE

01:25:36.701 --> 01:25:39.637 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR.

01:25:38.703 --> 01:25:40.638 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT IS CORRECT.

01:25:39.737 --> 01:25:41.772 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND AS A MATTER OF LAW,

01:25:40.738 --> 01:25:42.106 line:78%
REGULATIONS THAT HAVE THE FORCE

01:25:41.873 --> 01:25:42.807 line:78%
OF LAW.

01:25:42.206 --> 01:25:44.742 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT IS CORRECT, AND HE HAS

01:25:42.907 --> 01:25:46.744 line:78%
NOT BEEN DISMISSED.

01:25:44.842 --> 01:25:47.712 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND UNTIL OR UNLESS HE IS --

01:25:46.844 --> 01:25:48.779 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOR IS HE LIKELY TO BE

01:25:47.812 --> 01:25:49.714 line:78%
DISMISSED.

01:25:48.880 --> 01:25:51.816 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE HAVE A CASE OF CONTROVERSY

01:25:49.814 --> 01:25:52.850 line:78%
OF A VERY REAL KIND.

01:25:51.916 --> 01:25:53.851 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE POINT IS, IF I MAY MAKE

01:25:52.950 --> 01:25:54.819 line:78%
IT, THE ONLY ISSUE HERE IS

01:25:53.951 --> 01:25:55.820 line:78%
WHETHER THE PRESIDENT GAVE UP

01:25:54.919 --> 01:25:57.788 line:78%
HIS RIGHT TO PROTECT THE

01:25:55.920 --> 01:26:00.825 line:78%
CONFIDENTIALITY OF HIS

01:25:57.889 --> 01:26:03.861 line:78%
CONVERSATIONS.

01:26:00.925 --> 01:26:04.862 line:78%
&gt;&gt; CERTAINLY, HE HASN'T.

01:26:03.961 --> 01:26:05.863 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO CLAIM IS MADE THAT HE DID.

01:26:04.962 --> 01:26:06.864 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU'RE A LIVING TESTIMONY OF

01:26:05.963 --> 01:26:07.765 line:78%
THE FACT THAT HE DID NOT GIVE UP

01:26:06.964 --> 01:26:09.867 line:78%
HIS RIGHT TO DEFEND HIS POSITION

01:26:07.865 --> 01:26:10.234 line:78%
IN COURT.

01:26:09.967 --> 01:26:15.907 line:78%
[LAUGHTER]

01:26:12.737 --> 01:26:18.142 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND MY BROTHER

01:26:17.875 --> 01:26:20.044 line:78%
CONCEDES.

01:26:18.876 --> 01:26:21.078 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE VERY FACT THAT THE

01:26:20.144 --> 01:26:22.113 line:78%
DELEGATION TO MR. JAWORSKI GAVE

01:26:21.178 --> 01:26:23.080 line:78%
HIM THE RIGHT TO CONTEST THE

01:26:22.213 --> 01:26:25.283 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S CLAIM OF PRIVILEGE

01:26:23.180 --> 01:26:25.917 line:78%
PRESUPPOSES THAT THE PRESIDENT

01:26:25.383 --> 01:26:27.118 line:78%
HAD A RIGHT TO ASSERT THE

01:26:26.017 --> 01:26:29.086 line:78%
PRIVILEGE BUT NOT THE RIGHT TO

01:26:27.218 --> 01:26:31.222 line:78%
ASSERT IT NECESSARILY WITH

01:26:29.186 --> 01:26:31.689 line:78%
COMPLETE FINALITY.

01:26:31.322 --> 01:26:32.223 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S --

01:26:31.789 --> 01:26:33.224 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S THE --

01:26:32.323 --> 01:26:34.292 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S WHAT WE --

01:26:33.324 --> 01:26:35.393 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S WHAT WE'RE REALLY

01:26:34.392 --> 01:26:35.693 line:78%
ARGUING ABOUT HERE TODAY, ISN'T?

01:26:35.493 --> 01:26:36.427 line:78%
NOW --

01:26:35.793 --> 01:26:39.363 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IF WE GET BEYOND THE SUBJECT

01:26:36.527 --> 01:26:40.398 line:78%
MATTER SITUATION.

01:26:39.463 --> 01:26:42.400 line:78%
NOW, IF THIS WERE THE NIXON

01:26:40.498 --> 01:26:43.367 line:78%
AGAINST SIRICA CASE WHERE YOU

01:26:42.500 --> 01:26:46.370 line:78%
DIDN'T HAVE WHAT I THINK IS A

01:26:43.467 --> 01:26:47.371 line:78%
DISPOSITIVE PROBLEM IN THIS

01:26:46.470 --> 01:26:49.373 line:78%
CASE, NAMELY, THE LACK OF

01:26:47.471 --> 01:26:53.578 line:78%
JURISDICTION IN THE JUDICIAL

01:26:49.473 --> 01:26:54.545 line:78%
BRANCH TO DETERMINE THIS

01:26:53.678 --> 01:26:57.615 line:78%
INTRA-EXECUTIVE BRANCH IF WE HAD

01:26:54.645 --> 01:26:58.549 line:78%
A GRAND JURY SUBPOENA, AS WAS

01:26:57.715 --> 01:26:59.684 line:78%
TRUE IN THE NIXON AGAINST SIRICA

01:26:58.649 --> 01:27:02.753 line:78%
CASE.

01:26:59.784 --> 01:27:04.755 line:78%
THEN, YOU HAVE INTRA-BRANCH AND

01:27:02.853 --> 01:27:05.823 line:78%
THE COURT WOULD HAVE A BETTER

01:27:04.855 --> 01:27:06.824 line:78%
STANDING IN ITS RESPONSIBILITY

01:27:05.923 --> 01:27:08.826 line:78%
TO SEE THE GRAND JURIES WHICH

01:27:06.924 --> 01:27:10.828 line:78%
ARE UNDER ITS JURISDICTION TO

01:27:08.926 --> 01:27:11.896 line:78%
HAVE SUCH EVIDENCE AS THEY

01:27:10.928 --> 01:27:12.797 line:78%
THOUGHT APPROPRIATE.

01:27:11.996 --> 01:27:14.899 line:78%
BUT, WE'RE WELL BEYOND THAT

01:27:12.897 --> 01:27:17.868 line:78%
STAGE.

01:27:14.999 --> 01:27:18.869 line:78%
17C REQUIRES A GREAT, MUCH MORE

01:27:17.969 --> 01:27:19.870 line:78%
RESTRICTED FORM OF EVIDENCE

01:27:18.970 --> 01:27:23.107 line:78%
THAT'S GOT TO BE RELEVANT AND

01:27:19.971 --> 01:27:23.908 line:78%
ADMISSIBLE.

01:27:23.207 --> 01:27:24.976 line:78%
IT'S NOTHING LIKE A GRAND JURY

01:27:24.008 --> 01:27:25.943 line:78%
SUBPOENA.

01:27:25.076 --> 01:27:27.011 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. ST. CLAIR.

01:27:26.043 --> 01:27:28.012 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

01:27:27.111 --> 01:27:29.013 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WITH REFERENCE TO YOUR POINT

01:27:28.112 --> 01:27:30.014 line:78%
ABOUT WHETHER THERE ARE THREE

01:27:29.113 --> 01:27:31.983 line:78%
BRANCHES OR THREE-AND-SOME

01:27:30.114 --> 01:27:34.051 line:78%
FRACTION, IS NOT THE CONTROLLER

01:27:32.083 --> 01:27:42.159 line:78%
GENERAL SOMETHING OF AN

01:27:34.151 --> 01:27:45.196 line:78%
AUTONOMOUS FRACTIONAL MORE THAN

01:27:42.259 --> 01:27:46.197 line:78%
A THIRD BRANCH FIGURE?

01:27:45.296 --> 01:27:49.233 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I DON'T THINK THAT THE

01:27:46.297 --> 01:27:51.268 line:78%
CONTROLLER GENERAL --

01:27:49.333 --> 01:27:53.304 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HE'S A CREATURE --

01:27:51.369 --> 01:27:54.338 line:78%
&gt;&gt; REPRESENTS, IF YOUR HONOR

01:27:53.404 --> 01:27:55.272 line:78%
PLEASE, THAT BASIC

01:27:54.438 --> 01:27:59.343 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL STRUCTURE HAS

01:27:55.373 --> 01:28:00.444 line:78%
BEEN CHANGED.

01:27:59.443 --> 01:28:00.678 line:78%
IT MAY BE THAT HE HAS EXECUTIVE

01:28:00.544 --> 01:28:01.412 line:78%
--

01:28:00.778 --> 01:28:02.313 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT HE MAY PROCEED BUT NOT --

01:28:01.512 --> 01:28:03.414 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND HE MAY HAVE LEGISLATIVE

01:28:02.413 --> 01:28:04.415 line:78%
FUNCTIONS.

01:28:03.514 --> 01:28:05.449 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HE MAY PROCEED WITH REFERENCE

01:28:04.515 --> 01:28:06.417 line:78%
TO THE EXECUTIVE BRANCH AND, I

01:28:05.549 --> 01:28:07.585 line:78%
WOULD ASSUME, WITH REFERENCE TO

01:28:06.517 --> 01:28:08.285 line:78%
EXPENDITURES OF THE LEGISLATIVE

01:28:07.685 --> 01:28:12.623 line:78%
BRANCH AND WITHOUT CONSULTING

01:28:08.386 --> 01:28:13.524 line:78%
EITHER ONE OF THEM.

01:28:12.723 --> 01:28:14.558 line:78%
IS THAT NOT IT?

01:28:13.624 --> 01:28:16.527 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I UNDERSTAND.

01:28:14.659 --> 01:28:17.528 line:78%
HE IS CREATED BY A LEGISLATIVE,

01:28:16.627 --> 01:28:18.562 line:78%
VERY MUCH LIKE A

01:28:17.628 --> 01:28:20.531 line:78%
SEMI-INDEPENDENT AGENCY.

01:28:18.663 --> 01:28:22.566 line:78%
IN ONE ASPECT, HE'S AN AGENT OF

01:28:20.631 --> 01:28:23.534 line:78%
THE LEGISLATURE.

01:28:22.667 --> 01:28:26.570 line:78%
IN THE OTHER ASPECT, HE'S AN

01:28:23.634 --> 01:28:27.538 line:78%
AGENT OF THE EXECUTIVE.

01:28:26.671 --> 01:28:28.539 line:78%
BUT, WE DON'T HAVE ANY MORE THAN

01:28:27.638 --> 01:28:30.608 line:78%
LEGISLATIVE, JUDICIAL, AND

01:28:28.639 --> 01:28:31.609 line:78%
EXECUTIVE BRANCHES.

01:28:30.708 --> 01:28:33.644 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. JAWORSKI, AS I UNDERSTAND

01:28:31.709 --> 01:28:34.645 line:78%
IT, IS CLAIMING THAT HE'S

01:28:33.744 --> 01:28:35.646 line:78%
SOMEWHAT LIKE, NOT NECESSARILY

01:28:34.745 --> 01:28:39.717 line:78%
PRECISELY LIKE BUT SOMEWHAT LIKE

01:28:35.746 --> 01:28:42.720 line:78%
THE CONTROLLER GENERAL.

01:28:39.817 --> 01:28:43.721 line:78%
THAT, HE MAY MAKE DECISIONS AND

01:28:42.820 --> 01:28:44.755 line:78%
THAT CONGRESS CANNOT RECALL HIM

01:28:43.821 --> 01:28:46.791 line:78%
SHORT AS, I BELIEVE, A 15-YEAR

01:28:44.855 --> 01:28:47.792 line:78%
TERM FOR THE CONTROLLER GENERAL

01:28:46.891 --> 01:28:51.896 line:78%
AND NO PRESIDENT CAN FIRE THE

01:28:47.892 --> 01:28:54.832 line:78%
CONTROLLER GENERAL.

01:28:51.996 --> 01:28:55.900 line:78%
AND, I SUPPOSE, THE COURT COULD

01:28:54.932 --> 01:28:56.834 line:78%
NOT FIRE HIM.

01:28:56.000 --> 01:28:59.870 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I'M SURE THE COURT

01:28:56.934 --> 01:29:01.872 line:78%
COULDN'T.

01:28:59.970 --> 01:29:03.874 line:78%
I'M NOT TOO CLEAR ABOUT THE

01:29:01.972 --> 01:29:04.842 line:78%
PRESIDENT UNDER THE MYERS CASE.

01:29:03.974 --> 01:29:06.877 line:78%
I REALLY HAVEN'T THOUGHT THAT

01:29:04.942 --> 01:29:07.912 line:78%
MUCH OF IT.

01:29:06.977 --> 01:29:09.847 line:78%
IT COULD BE THAT HE COULD BE

01:29:08.012 --> 01:29:10.881 line:78%
FIRED, BUT I THINK THAT'S REALLY

01:29:09.947 --> 01:29:12.950 line:78%
SOMEWHAT BESIDE THE POINT

01:29:10.981 --> 01:29:17.054 line:78%
BECAUSE THIS ISSUE REALLY TURNS

01:29:13.050 --> 01:29:18.055 line:78%
ON AN ADMISSION THAT, AS TO THE

01:29:17.154 --> 01:29:21.058 line:78%
ELEMENT OF THE EXECUTIVE POWER

01:29:18.155 --> 01:29:22.026 line:78%
HERE INVOLVED, NAMELY,

01:29:21.158 --> 01:29:25.096 line:78%
PRESIDENTIAL CONVERSATIONS, THEY

01:29:22.126 --> 01:29:26.097 line:78%
WEREN'T DELEGATED.

01:29:25.196 --> 01:29:29.066 line:78%
SO, WHATEVER ELSE MAY HAVE BEEN

01:29:26.197 --> 01:29:31.068 line:78%
DELEGATED, THOSE WERE NOT.

01:29:29.166 --> 01:29:32.069 line:78%
AND, THIS COURT HAS NO

01:29:31.168 --> 01:29:33.104 line:78%
JURISDICTION TO RESOLVE A

01:29:32.169 --> 01:29:35.106 line:78%
DISPUTE AS TO WHETHER OR NOT

01:29:33.204 --> 01:29:37.174 line:78%
THEY SHOULD BE GIVEN UP BECAUSE

01:29:35.206 --> 01:29:39.143 line:78%
THAT WOULD INVOLVE THIS COURT IN

01:29:37.274 --> 01:29:40.277 line:78%
THE PROSECUTION OF THE CASE AND

01:29:39.243 --> 01:29:41.245 line:78%
THE JUDICIAL --

01:29:40.377 --> 01:29:42.246 line:78%
&gt;&gt; CAN THIS COURT DECIDE WHAT'S

01:29:41.345 --> 01:29:45.316 line:78%
NECESSARY FOR TRIAL OF A

01:29:42.346 --> 01:29:46.317 line:78%
CRIMINAL CASE?

01:29:45.416 --> 01:29:49.286 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT CAN, SIR, WITH RESPECT TO

01:29:46.417 --> 01:29:51.322 line:78%
THIRD PARTIES BUT IT SHOULD NOT

01:29:49.386 --> 01:29:52.323 line:78%
INVOLVE ITSELF WITH THE

01:29:51.422 --> 01:29:55.326 line:78%
EXECUTIVE FUNCTION OF

01:29:52.423 --> 01:29:56.360 line:78%
PROSECUTING THE CASE.

01:29:55.426 --> 01:29:58.362 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MY ONLY QUESTION WAS IF THIS

01:29:56.460 --> 01:30:03.534 line:78%
IS A SUBPOENA DUCES TECUM THAT

01:29:58.462 --> 01:30:05.436 line:78%
WAS ISSUED BY A JUDGE, RIGHT?

01:30:03.634 --> 01:30:06.437 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

01:30:05.536 --> 01:30:13.511 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SLIGHTLY JUDICIAL.

01:30:06.537 --> 01:30:14.512 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ENTIRELY JUDICIAL.

01:30:13.611 --> 01:30:15.613 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THAT'S WHAT'S BEFORE US.

01:30:14.612 --> 01:30:15.946 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND, THAT, WE MOVE TO QUASH

01:30:15.713 --> 01:30:16.814 line:78%
AS WE --

01:30:16.046 --> 01:30:17.515 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT THAT'S WHAT'S BEFORE US.

01:30:16.914 --> 01:30:18.549 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE DENIAL OF OUR MOTION TO

01:30:17.615 --> 01:30:18.916 line:78%
QUASH IS ONE OF THE ISSUES

01:30:18.649 --> 01:30:20.718 line:78%
BEFORE US.

01:30:19.016 --> 01:30:21.418 line:78%
THAT'S RIGHT.

01:30:20.818 --> 01:30:22.119 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE ONLY THING BEFORE US IS

01:30:21.519 --> 01:30:24.555 line:78%
WHETHER OR NOT THE SUBPOENA IS

01:30:22.219 --> 01:30:25.556 line:78%
AT ISSUE.

01:30:24.655 --> 01:30:26.557 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I GUESS IT'S ABOUT THE SAME

01:30:25.656 --> 01:30:27.525 line:78%
THING AS WHETHER OR NOT IT

01:30:26.657 --> 01:30:29.627 line:78%
SHOULD BE QUASHED AND I THINK --

01:30:27.625 --> 01:30:30.294 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT.

01:30:29.727 --> 01:30:30.594 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT AMOUNTS TO THE SAME

01:30:30.394 --> 01:30:36.567 line:78%
THING.

01:30:30.694 --> 01:30:38.803 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SO, THAT'S NOT POLITICAL.

01:30:36.667 --> 01:30:39.537 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL IT IS NOT, IN THE

01:30:38.903 --> 01:30:40.638 line:78%
CONTEXT OF THE PROCEEDINGS HERE

01:30:39.637 --> 01:30:41.605 line:78%
BUT, IN THE CONTEXT OF WHETHER

01:30:40.738 --> 01:30:42.640 line:78%
IT'S IN FACT INVOLVED IN THIS

01:30:41.705 --> 01:30:45.709 line:78%
CASE, IT IS, I SUGGEST,

01:30:42.740 --> 01:30:47.812 line:78%
POLITICAL IN THE SENSE THAT THIS

01:30:45.810 --> 01:30:48.813 line:78%
INFORMATION BEING SOUGHT

01:30:47.912 --> 01:30:52.850 line:78%
ADMITTEDLY WILL BECOME AVAILABLE

01:30:48.913 --> 01:30:55.886 line:78%
THEN TO THE HOUSE.

01:30:52.950 --> 01:30:58.889 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE MEAN POLITICAL -- WELL, I

01:30:55.986 --> 01:31:01.025 line:78%
DON'T SEE WHETHER HOUSE HAS GOT

01:30:58.989 --> 01:31:01.692 line:78%
ANYTHING TO DO WITH THE COURT

01:31:01.125 --> 01:31:02.827 line:78%
THAT I'M TALKING ABOUT.

01:31:01.792 --> 01:31:04.028 line:78%
YOU SAID IT'S A POLITICAL AND

01:31:02.927 --> 01:31:04.662 line:78%
NOT JUDICIAL.

01:31:04.128 --> 01:31:05.396 line:78%
AND, I SUBMIT IT COULD BE

01:31:04.762 --> 01:31:06.897 line:78%
JUDICIAL BECAUSE IT INVOLVES THE

01:31:05.496 --> 01:31:08.899 line:78%
ISSUE OF SUBPOENA.

01:31:06.997 --> 01:31:09.934 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL THE QUESTION IS, IS IT A

01:31:08.999 --> 01:31:12.002 line:78%
PROPER ISSUE OF A SUBPOENA.

01:31:10.034 --> 01:31:13.037 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT.

01:31:12.102 --> 01:31:14.038 line:78%
&gt;&gt; JUDGES MAKE MISTAKES, AS DO

01:31:13.137 --> 01:31:16.040 line:78%
LAWYERS, AND MAYBE EVEN

01:31:14.138 --> 01:31:18.042 line:78%
PRESIDENTS, FOR ALL I KNOW, BUT

01:31:16.140 --> 01:31:21.078 line:78%
THE POINT I WANT TO MAKE WITH

01:31:18.142 --> 01:31:22.046 line:78%
YOU, SIR, IS THAT THIS IS AN

01:31:21.178 --> 01:31:23.080 line:78%
EXECUTIVE FUNCTION, AN EXECUTIVE

01:31:22.146 --> 01:31:25.082 line:78%
DECISION, ONE NOT DELEGATED --

01:31:23.180 --> 01:31:26.116 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL THE EXECUTIVE FUNCTION

01:31:25.182 --> 01:31:27.051 line:78%
IS, AS I UNDERSTATED, THE

01:31:26.217 --> 01:31:28.118 line:78%
DISCUSSION AS TO WHETHER HE

01:31:27.151 --> 01:31:32.156 line:78%
SHOULD VOLUNTARILY TURN OVER TO

01:31:28.219 --> 01:31:38.195 line:78%
THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR.

01:31:32.256 --> 01:31:39.196 line:78%
WE HAVE PASSED THAT STAGE.

01:31:38.295 --> 01:31:41.198 line:78%
WE ARE NOW AT THE STAGE WHERE

01:31:39.296 --> 01:31:44.235 line:78%
THE PROSECUTOR HAS ASKED THE

01:31:41.298 --> 01:31:45.302 line:78%
COURT TO ASSIST HIM AND THE

01:31:44.335 --> 01:31:51.308 line:78%
COURT HAS ASSISTED HIM.

01:31:45.402 --> 01:31:52.276 line:78%
DOES THAT NOT TAKE IT A STEP

01:31:51.408 --> 01:31:55.379 line:78%
BEYOND PURE POLITICAL OR

01:31:52.376 --> 01:31:57.414 line:78%
EXECUTIVE?

01:31:55.479 --> 01:31:58.415 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE SUBMIT THAT THE COURT

01:31:57.514 --> 01:32:00.417 line:78%
IMPROPERLY ASSISTED HIM, THAT

01:31:58.515 --> 01:32:01.385 line:78%
THE COURT HAS NO RIGHT TO

01:32:00.517 --> 01:32:02.353 line:78%
DETERMINE WHAT THE EXECUTIVE

01:32:01.485 --> 01:32:03.354 line:78%
WILL OFFER IN EVIDENCE.

01:32:02.453 --> 01:32:04.521 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I GET THAT.

01:32:03.454 --> 01:32:05.256 line:78%
I SEE.

01:32:04.622 --> 01:32:06.423 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND, THIS IS THE FUNCTION OF

01:32:05.356 --> 01:32:07.424 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT.

01:32:06.523 --> 01:32:08.425 line:78%
NO ONE HAS CONTENDED THAT THE

01:32:07.524 --> 01:32:11.462 line:78%
PRESIDENT HAS GIVEN UP HIS

01:32:08.525 --> 01:32:12.463 line:78%
EXECUTIVE RESPONSIBILITIES UNDER

01:32:11.562 --> 01:32:13.464 line:78%
THE CONSTITUTION AND, CERTAINLY,

01:32:12.563 --> 01:32:17.568 line:78%
THE PROSECUTION OF CRIMINAL

01:32:13.564 --> 01:32:18.535 line:78%
CASES IS AN EXECUTIVE FUNCTION.

01:32:17.668 --> 01:32:19.470 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THAT'S ACTUALLY -- NOW,

01:32:18.636 --> 01:32:21.639 line:78%
YOU'RE ARGUING ABSOLUTE

01:32:19.570 --> 01:32:22.039 line:78%
PRIVILEGE.

01:32:21.739 --> 01:32:22.673 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

01:32:22.139 --> 01:32:24.508 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ABSOLUTE EXECUTIVE EVEN

01:32:22.773 --> 01:32:26.510 line:78%
THOUGH EVERYDAY IT'S SO YOU

01:32:24.608 --> 01:32:27.544 line:78%
LOOSE ANOTHER ONE.

01:32:26.610 --> 01:32:28.512 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I BEG YOUR PARDON?

01:32:27.645 --> 01:32:30.581 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU TURN THINGS LOOSE

01:32:28.612 --> 01:32:31.548 line:78%
EVERYDAY, I SUPPOSE.

01:32:30.681 --> 01:32:33.550 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, WE DON'T TURN THEM LOOSE

01:32:31.649 --> 01:32:34.618 line:78%
EVERYDAY BUT WE HAVE TURNED A

01:32:33.651 --> 01:32:35.619 line:78%
NUMBER LOOSE IN THE PRESIDENT'S

01:32:34.718 --> 01:32:37.621 line:78%
DISCRETION IN WHICH HE THOUGHT

01:32:35.719 --> 01:32:38.622 line:78%
WAS AN APPROPRIATE THING TO DO,

01:32:37.721 --> 01:32:40.624 line:78%
AND THAT'S HIS DETERMINATION

01:32:38.722 --> 01:32:41.759 line:78%
THAT GOVERNS, WE SUGGEST.

01:32:40.724 --> 01:32:42.293 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IS HE GETTING READY TO TURN

01:32:41.859 --> 01:32:42.826 line:78%
20 MORE CASE LOOSE.

01:32:42.393 --> 01:32:44.695 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, THIS WOULD BE

01:32:42.927 --> 01:32:45.629 line:78%
REPETITIOUS, YOUR HONOR.

01:32:44.795 --> 01:32:46.730 line:78%
WHEN, ALREADY, IT HAS BEEN MADE

01:32:45.729 --> 01:32:47.698 line:78%
PUBLIC.

01:32:46.830 --> 01:32:48.632 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I THOUGHT YOU SAID IN

01:32:47.798 --> 01:32:49.700 line:78%
YOUR BRIEF YOU WOULD TURN 20

01:32:48.732 --> 01:32:50.734 line:78%
LOOSE?

01:32:49.800 --> 01:32:51.669 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THOSE 20 -- THOSE WOULD BE

01:32:50.834 --> 01:32:54.705 line:78%
THE TAPES OF 20 CONVERSATIONS

01:32:51.769 --> 01:32:55.739 line:78%
ALREADY MADE PUBLIC.

01:32:54.805 --> 01:32:56.774 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU RELEASED THOSE TAPES?

01:32:55.839 --> 01:32:59.743 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE'LL PROVIDE A MEANS WHEREBY

01:32:56.874 --> 01:33:00.811 line:78%
THEIR ACCURACY CAN BE VERIFIED.

01:32:59.843 --> 01:33:01.779 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S --

01:33:00.911 --> 01:33:03.881 line:78%
&gt;&gt; TO RELEASE A WHOLE REEL OF

01:33:01.879 --> 01:33:04.815 line:78%
TAPE INVOLVING A NUMBER OF

01:33:03.981 --> 01:33:05.883 line:78%
CONVERSATIONS POSES A MECHANICAL

01:33:04.915 --> 01:33:06.917 line:78%
PROBLEM.

01:33:05.983 --> 01:33:08.953 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU STILL SAYING THE ABSOLUTE

01:33:07.017 --> 01:33:09.954 line:78%
PRIVILEGE TO DECIDE WHAT SHALL

01:33:09.053 --> 01:33:12.957 line:78%
BE RELEASED AND WHAT SHALL NOT

01:33:10.054 --> 01:33:17.027 line:78%
BE RELEASED IS VESTED IN ONE

01:33:13.057 --> 01:33:17.294 line:78%
PERSON AND NOBODY CAN QUESTION

01:33:17.127 --> 01:33:17.995 line:78%
IT.

01:33:17.394 --> 01:33:18.929 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IN SO FAR AS IT RELATES TO

01:33:18.095 --> 01:33:19.964 line:78%
THE PRESIDENTIAL CONVERSATION

01:33:19.029 --> 01:33:20.898 line:78%
THAT IS CORRECT, SIR.

01:33:20.064 --> 01:33:21.966 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT YOU'RE NOW DEALING, AS I

01:33:20.998 --> 01:33:22.967 line:78%
UNDERSTAND --

01:33:22.066 --> 01:33:24.001 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S ANOTHER ISSUE.

01:33:23.067 --> 01:33:25.035 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. ST. CLAIR WITH THE

01:33:24.101 --> 01:33:27.071 line:78%
JURISDICTIONAL QUESTION AND, AS

01:33:25.135 --> 01:33:29.073 line:78%
I FURTHER UNDERSTAND IT, THAT

01:33:27.171 --> 01:33:31.108 line:78%
THAT ARGUMENT OF YOURS, AT LEAST

01:33:29.173 --> 01:33:32.076 line:78%
I GOT IT FROM THE BRIEF,

01:33:31.208 --> 01:33:33.077 line:78%
INVOLVES AT LEAST TWO SEPARATE

01:33:32.176 --> 01:33:38.282 line:78%
CONCEPTS AND MAYBE THREE.

01:33:33.177 --> 01:33:39.116 line:78%
ONE IS THAT THIS IS AN

01:33:38.382 --> 01:33:40.117 line:78%
INTRA-BRANCH DISPUTE, AND THAT

01:33:39.216 --> 01:33:42.052 line:78%
ARGUMENT WOULD BE FULLY VALID

01:33:40.217 --> 01:33:45.155 line:78%
UNDER THE ANALOGY YOU USE IN

01:33:42.152 --> 01:33:46.156 line:78%
YOUR BRIEF.

01:33:45.255 --> 01:33:48.192 line:78%
IF THIS WERE A DISPUTE BETWEEN,

01:33:46.256 --> 01:33:49.159 line:78%
LET'S SAY, TWO COMMITTEES IN ONE

01:33:48.292 --> 01:33:50.194 line:78%
OF THE HOUSES OF THE CONGRESS

01:33:49.259 --> 01:33:52.229 line:78%
AND ONE COMMITTEE SUED THE OTHER

01:33:50.294 --> 01:33:54.264 line:78%
FOR JURISDICTION OF A PARTICULAR

01:33:52.329 --> 01:33:55.232 line:78%
MATTER, YOU SUGGEST AND PROBABLY

01:33:54.365 --> 01:33:56.233 line:78%
QUITE CORRECTLY, THAT THAT WOULD

01:33:55.332 --> 01:33:58.235 line:78%
NOT BE A MATTER FOR THE

01:33:56.333 --> 01:34:00.270 line:78%
JUDICIARY TO DETERMINE.

01:33:58.335 --> 01:34:01.305 line:78%
THAT'S ONE ARGUMENT.

01:34:00.371 --> 01:34:02.339 line:78%
THAT THIS IS PURELY AN

01:34:01.405 --> 01:34:04.341 line:78%
INTRA-EXECUTIVE BRANCH

01:34:02.439 --> 01:34:07.344 line:78%
CONTROVERSY, AS IT WOULD BE

01:34:04.441 --> 01:34:09.413 line:78%
BETWEEN TWO CONGRESSIONAL

01:34:07.444 --> 01:34:10.414 line:78%
COMMITTEES.

01:34:09.513 --> 01:34:13.517 line:78%
THIS IS INTRA-ARTICLE 2 BRANCH.

01:34:10.514 --> 01:34:16.520 line:78%
THE HYPOTHETICAL CASE WOULD BE

01:34:13.617 --> 01:34:17.554 line:78%
INTRA-ARTICLE 1 BRANCH.

01:34:16.620 --> 01:34:19.590 line:78%
AND THEN, YOU HAVE QUITE A

01:34:17.654 --> 01:34:23.627 line:78%
SEPARATE ARGUMENT, IT SEEMS TO

01:34:19.690 --> 01:34:24.661 line:78%
ME, I.E. THAT THE PRESIDENT

01:34:23.727 --> 01:34:25.596 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONALLY IS THE CHIEF

01:34:24.762 --> 01:34:26.663 line:78%
PROSECUTOR SINCE HE IS THE

01:34:25.696 --> 01:34:27.664 line:78%
EXECUTIVE.

01:34:26.764 --> 01:34:28.665 line:78%
AND, IT IS NOT FOR THE COURTS TO

01:34:27.765 --> 01:34:29.633 line:78%
DECIDE WHAT A PROSECUTOR SHALL

01:34:28.766 --> 01:34:30.768 line:78%
USE IN PROSECUTING A CRIMINAL

01:34:29.733 --> 01:34:31.769 line:78%
CASE.

01:34:30.868 --> 01:34:33.804 line:78%
NOW, ISN'T THAT -- AREN'T THOSE

01:34:31.869 --> 01:34:35.773 line:78%
TWO SEPARATE ARGUMENTS?

01:34:33.904 --> 01:34:41.945 line:78%
YOU MAKE BOTH OF THEM UNDER THIS

01:34:35.873 --> 01:34:42.312 line:78%
RULE BRICK.

01:34:42.046 --> 01:34:44.048 line:78%
-- RUBRIC.

01:34:42.780 --> 01:34:44.815 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, SIR.

01:34:44.148 --> 01:34:45.916 line:78%
I DON'T KNOW HOW SEPARATE THEY

01:34:44.915 --> 01:34:46.984 line:78%
ARE BUT I'LL CERTAINLY MAKE USE

01:34:46.016 --> 01:34:47.918 line:78%
OF BOTH OF THEM.

01:34:47.084 --> 01:34:48.952 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, IT SEEMS TO ME THEY'RE

01:34:48.018 --> 01:34:49.987 line:78%
QUITE SEPARATE.

01:34:49.053 --> 01:34:51.088 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT I'M MAKING BOTH OF THEM

01:34:50.087 --> 01:34:51.688 line:78%
AND IF THEY'RE SEPARATE, FINE.

01:34:51.188 --> 01:34:52.356 line:78%
NOW, WITH RESPECT TO --

01:34:51.789 --> 01:34:53.090 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THE SECOND ARGUMENT

01:34:52.456 --> 01:34:53.924 line:78%
WILL HAVE NO RELEVANCE AT ALL TO

01:34:53.190 --> 01:34:58.095 line:78%
YOUR ANALOGY OF THE LEGISLATIVE

01:34:54.024 --> 01:34:59.096 line:78%
BRANCH.

01:34:58.195 --> 01:35:00.064 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I DON'T WANT TO MISLEAD

01:34:59.196 --> 01:35:01.131 line:78%
THE COURT INTO THINKING THAT I

01:35:00.164 --> 01:35:02.099 line:78%
BELIEVE MR. JAWORSKI HAS NO

01:35:01.231 --> 01:35:05.135 line:78%
RIGHT TO DETERMINE ANY EVIDENCE

01:35:02.199 --> 01:35:06.136 line:78%
THAT HE COMMUNES.

01:35:05.235 --> 01:35:07.171 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT ULTIMATELY, YOU TELL US

01:35:06.236 --> 01:35:09.139 line:78%
THAT, CONSTITUTIONALLY, THE

01:35:07.271 --> 01:35:12.176 line:78%
PRESIDENT AS CHIEF EXECUTIVE

01:35:09.239 --> 01:35:13.143 line:78%
AND, THEREFORE, AS

01:35:12.276 --> 01:35:16.146 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONALLY THE CHIEF

01:35:13.243 --> 01:35:17.314 line:78%
PROSECUTOR OR WHATEVER THE

01:35:16.246 --> 01:35:17.881 line:78%
STATUTES MIGHT PROVIDE --

01:35:17.414 --> 01:35:19.149 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT.

01:35:17.981 --> 01:35:20.150 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HAS UNRESTRICTED DISCRETION

01:35:19.249 --> 01:35:21.151 line:78%
TO DETERMINE WHAT EVIDENCE HE

01:35:20.250 --> 01:35:23.187 line:78%
WILL OR WILL NOT USE IN

01:35:21.251 --> 01:35:24.254 line:78%
PROSECUTING A CASE.

01:35:23.287 --> 01:35:25.255 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT IS CORRECT.

01:35:24.354 --> 01:35:26.256 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHICH IS QUITE A DIFFERENT

01:35:25.355 --> 01:35:28.325 line:78%
CONCEPT FROM THE OTHER CONCEPT.

01:35:26.356 --> 01:35:32.362 line:78%
YOU MAKE THEM BOTH UNDER THE

01:35:28.425 --> 01:35:34.331 line:78%
SAME RULE BRICK, AS I SAY.

01:35:32.463 --> 01:35:35.299 line:78%
BUT I -- IT SEEMS TO ME, THEY'RE

01:35:34.431 --> 01:35:36.333 line:78%
QUITE SEPARATE ARGUMENTS.

01:35:35.399 --> 01:35:37.367 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND I THINK THEY'RE

01:35:36.433 --> 01:35:38.335 line:78%
WELL-FOUNDED IN THE LAW.

01:35:37.468 --> 01:35:39.403 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I KNOW YOU DO OR YOU WOULDN'T

01:35:38.435 --> 01:35:40.404 line:78%
MAKE THEM.

01:35:39.503 --> 01:35:41.438 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOW I'D LIKE TO MOVE, IF I

01:35:40.504 --> 01:35:43.440 line:78%
MAY, TO BRIEFLY -- THE

01:35:41.538 --> 01:35:45.509 line:78%
SUGGESTION THAT THE ISSUE HERE

01:35:43.540 --> 01:35:47.578 line:78%
IS NON-JUSTICIABLE ON THE

01:35:45.609 --> 01:35:48.579 line:78%
GROUNDS OTHER THAN I'VE ALREADY

01:35:47.678 --> 01:35:50.514 line:78%
MENTIONED, NAMELY, THE CONTEXT

01:35:48.679 --> 01:35:51.648 line:78%
IN WHICH THIS CASE UNFORTUNATELY

01:35:50.614 --> 01:35:53.650 line:78%
FINDS ITSELF.

01:35:51.748 --> 01:35:55.652 line:78%
IT SEEMS TO US, BRIEFLY, THAT

01:35:53.750 --> 01:35:59.656 line:78%
THE CASE IS NON-JUSTICIABLE FOR

01:35:55.752 --> 01:36:03.660 line:78%
SOMEWHAT MORE TECHNICAL REASONS.

01:35:59.756 --> 01:36:05.762 line:78%
FIRST, THIS IS AN ISSUE WHERE IF

01:36:03.760 --> 01:36:08.832 line:78%
SOMEONE HAS TO EXERCISE SOME

01:36:05.863 --> 01:36:12.836 line:78%
DISCRETION, THERE ARE NO REAL

01:36:08.932 --> 01:36:13.770 line:78%
BOUNDS OR STANDARDS BY WHICH

01:36:12.936 --> 01:36:14.838 line:78%
THAT DISCRETION SHOULD BE

01:36:13.871 --> 01:36:16.874 line:78%
EXERCISED.

01:36:14.938 --> 01:36:18.909 line:78%
AND, BY TRADITIONAL STANDARDS OF

01:36:16.974 --> 01:36:19.877 line:78%
THIS COURT WHERE THAT EXISTS,

01:36:19.009 --> 01:36:21.912 line:78%
THEN THIS COURT OUGHT NOT TO

01:36:19.977 --> 01:36:23.914 line:78%
TAKE THE CASE.

01:36:22.012 --> 01:36:25.949 line:78%
SECONDLY, IT SEEMS TO ME, THERE

01:36:24.014 --> 01:36:26.950 line:78%
IS A TEXTUAL CONSTITUTIONAL

01:36:26.049 --> 01:36:30.053 line:78%
GRANT IF WE ASSUME THAT THE

01:36:27.050 --> 01:36:32.055 line:78%
GRANT OF EXECUTIVE POWER

01:36:30.154 --> 01:36:33.991 line:78%
INCLUDES THE MEANS BY WHICH THAT

01:36:32.156 --> 01:36:36.960 line:78%
CAN BE EFFECTIVELY EXERCISED,

01:36:34.091 --> 01:36:38.095 line:78%
SECOND GROUND.

01:36:37.060 --> 01:36:39.029 line:78%
THIRD, OF COURSE, THERE IS THE

01:36:38.195 --> 01:36:41.064 line:78%
POLITICAL INVOLVEMENT WHICH I

01:36:39.129 --> 01:36:44.134 line:78%
HAVE SUGGESTED.

01:36:41.165 --> 01:36:46.170 line:78%
THEREFORE, I SUGGEST QUITE

01:36:44.234 --> 01:36:49.206 line:78%
BRIEFLY THAT EVEN IF THERE IS

01:36:46.270 --> 01:36:51.241 line:78%
SUBJECT MATTER JURISDICTION, THE

01:36:49.306 --> 01:36:53.310 line:78%
CASE IS NON-JUSTICIABLE FOR

01:36:51.341 --> 01:36:54.311 line:78%
THESE ADDITIONAL REASONS.

01:36:53.410 --> 01:36:58.248 line:78%
THE STANDARDS OF BAKER AND CARR,

01:36:54.411 --> 01:37:02.352 line:78%
AND POWELL ARE NOT APPLICABLE

01:36:58.348 --> 01:37:03.353 line:78%
HERE.

01:37:02.452 --> 01:37:04.321 line:78%
THERE ARE NO INDIVIDUAL'S RIGHTS

01:37:03.453 --> 01:37:06.323 line:78%
