01:51:58.748 --> 01:52:00.616 line:78%
PRESIDENT HAS WITH HIS ADVISERS,

01:51:59.782 --> 01:52:15.932 line:78%
WE SUGGEST, IS ABSOLUTELY

01:52:00.716 --> 01:52:16.933 line:78%
PRIVILEGE.

01:52:16.032 --> 01:52:19.001 line:78%
IT'S A DISCRETIONARY MATTER THAT

01:52:17.033 --> 01:52:19.602 line:78%
HE HAS TO EXERCISE IN WHAT HE IS

01:52:19.102 --> 01:52:19.936 line:78%
GOING TO RELEASE AND NOT

01:52:19.702 --> 01:52:20.903 line:78%
RELEASE.

01:52:20.036 --> 01:52:21.871 line:78%
AND SINCE MARBURY AND MADISON,

01:52:21.003 --> 01:52:22.905 line:78%
MISSISSIPPI AND JOHNSON, IT'S

01:52:21.971 --> 01:52:44.026 line:78%
BEEN CLEAR THAT THE COURT WILL

01:52:23.005 --> 01:52:46.095 line:78%
NOT DIRECT A PRESIDENT TO

01:52:44.127 --> 01:52:46.429 line:78%
EXERCISE HIS DISCRETION IN ANY

01:52:46.195 --> 01:52:47.096 line:78%
MANNER.

01:52:46.529 --> 01:52:47.997 line:78%
THIS IS NOT TO SAY THE COURT

01:52:47.196 --> 01:52:48.998 line:78%
WON'T STRIKE DOWN, AS IN SAWYER,

01:52:48.097 --> 01:52:49.999 line:78%
EXCESSIVE ACTION ON THE PART OF

01:52:49.098 --> 01:52:51.100 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT OR EXCESSIVE

01:52:50.099 --> 01:52:51.501 line:78%
ACTION ON THE PART OF THE

01:52:51.200 --> 01:52:52.235 line:78%
LEGISLATURE.

01:52:51.601 --> 01:52:53.102 line:78%
THAT HAS HAPPENED IN A NUMBER OF

01:52:52.335 --> 01:52:54.103 line:78%
TIMES.

01:52:53.202 --> 01:52:55.204 line:78%
BUT, IT'S A FAR DIFFERENT THING

01:52:54.203 --> 01:52:55.805 line:78%
TO SUGGEST THAT THE COURT SHOULD

01:52:55.304 --> 01:52:56.439 line:78%
UNDERTAKE TO DIRECT THE

01:52:55.905 --> 01:52:57.173 line:78%
PRESIDENT TO EXERCISE HIS

01:52:56.539 --> 01:52:58.040 line:78%
DISCRETION IN A CERTAIN MANNER.

01:52:57.273 --> 01:52:59.075 line:78%
IT'S NOT A MINISTERIAL DUTY BY

01:52:58.141 --> 01:53:00.109 line:78%
ANY MEANS.

01:52:59.175 --> 01:53:01.244 line:78%
IT'S A MATTER OF DISCRETION.

01:53:00.209 --> 01:53:01.944 line:78%
THERE ARE SOME THINGS HE FEELS

01:53:01.344 --> 01:53:02.645 line:78%
HE PROPERLY SHOULD, UNDER THE

01:53:02.044 --> 01:53:03.312 line:78%
CIRCUMSTANCES, MAKE AVAILABLE

01:53:02.745 --> 01:53:04.080 line:78%
AND OTHERS HE SHOULDN'T.

01:53:03.412 --> 01:53:05.114 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WITH RESPECT WITH THAT

01:53:04.180 --> 01:53:06.249 line:78%
PARTICULAR INCIDENCE, THE ONE

01:53:05.214 --> 01:53:06.949 line:78%
HERE INVOLVES THE RELEVANCY OF

01:53:06.349 --> 01:53:07.650 line:78%
MATERIALS TO A CRIMINAL TRIAL

01:53:07.049 --> 01:53:08.384 line:78%
AND, THAT, NORMALLY HAS BEEN A

01:53:07.750 --> 01:53:09.085 line:78%
PART OF THE JUDICIAL POWER UNDER

01:53:08.484 --> 01:53:28.538 line:78%
ARTICLE III, NOT THE EXECUTIVE

01:53:09.185 --> 01:53:29.605 line:78%
POWER.

01:53:28.638 --> 01:53:30.306 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I'D LIKE TO DISCUSS VERY

01:53:29.705 --> 01:53:30.640 line:78%
BRIEFLY GRAVEL, IF I MAY, FOR

01:53:30.406 --> 01:53:31.541 line:78%
EXAMPLE.

01:53:30.740 --> 01:53:32.608 line:78%
I THINK THIS RAISES A VERY

01:53:31.641 --> 01:53:33.643 line:78%
IMPORTANT QUESTION.

01:53:32.708 --> 01:53:34.610 line:78%
THERE IS, OF COURSE, AN EXPLICIT

01:53:33.743 --> 01:53:35.611 line:78%
SPEECH AND DEBATE IMMUNITY IN

01:53:34.710 --> 01:53:36.646 line:78%
PROVIDING THE CONSTITUTION.

01:53:35.711 --> 01:53:38.714 line:78%
AS OUR BRIEF INDICATES, THE

01:53:36.746 --> 01:53:39.882 line:78%
REASON FOR THIS IS QUITE CLEAR.

01:53:38.814 --> 01:53:40.583 line:78%
IT'S TO PROTECT THE LEGISLATURE

01:53:39.982 --> 01:53:41.284 line:78%
FROM UNWARRANTED INVASION FROM

01:53:40.683 --> 01:53:41.751 line:78%
THE EXECUTIVE AND PERHAPS THE

01:53:41.384 --> 01:53:42.919 line:78%
JUDICIAL.

01:53:41.851 --> 01:53:43.586 line:78%
IT DOES NOT MEAN THAT THE

01:53:43.019 --> 01:53:44.320 line:78%
EXECUTIVE IS NOT ENTITLED TO

01:53:43.686 --> 01:53:44.754 line:78%
SUBSTANTIALLY THE SAME THING BY

01:53:44.420 --> 01:54:04.140 line:78%
IMPLICATION.

01:53:44.854 --> 01:54:04.807 line:78%
AND AT LEAST IN THE CIVIL FIELD,

01:54:04.240 --> 01:54:05.441 line:78%
AS WE HAVE POINTED OUT, THE

01:54:04.907 --> 01:54:06.075 line:78%
COURTS HAVE WORKED OUT BY

01:54:05.541 --> 01:54:07.043 line:78%
IMPLICATION AS A NECESSARY

01:54:06.175 --> 01:54:08.077 line:78%
INGREDIENT TO THE FUNCTION OF

01:54:07.143 --> 01:54:09.078 line:78%
THE DUTIES OF THE EXECUTIVE AN

01:54:08.177 --> 01:54:10.079 line:78%
ABSOLUTE IMMUNITY FROM CIVIL

01:54:09.178 --> 01:54:11.013 line:78%
LIABILITY FOR ACTIONS TAKEN

01:54:10.179 --> 01:54:12.114 line:78%
WITHIN THE SPHERE OF THE

01:54:11.113 --> 01:54:39.609 line:78%
OFFICIAL.

01:54:12.215 --> 01:54:40.309 line:78%
SWELLING AND VIOLAS, I GUESS, IS

01:54:39.709 --> 01:54:41.043 line:78%
THE LEADING CASE AS CITED AND

01:54:40.409 --> 01:54:41.744 line:78%
BARR V. MATEO, AND OTHER CASES.

01:54:41.143 --> 01:54:42.478 line:78%
IF SUCH A MATTER CAN BE WORKED

01:54:41.844 --> 01:54:43.479 line:78%
OUT WITH RESPECT TO THE

01:54:42.578 --> 01:54:44.680 line:78%
EXECUTIVE ON CIVIL MATTERS, WE

01:54:43.579 --> 01:54:45.381 line:78%
SUGGEST THERE IS NO REASON WHY

01:54:44.780 --> 01:54:46.115 line:78%
AND, IN FACT, THE COURT SHOULD

01:54:45.481 --> 01:54:46.816 line:78%
SPELL OUT A SIMILAR EXEMPTION IN

01:54:46.215 --> 01:54:47.516 line:78%
CRIMINAL MATTERS ESPECIALLY AS

01:54:46.916 --> 01:54:48.517 line:78%
THEY RELATE TO THE PRESIDENT,

01:54:47.617 --> 01:54:49.652 line:78%
HIMSELF, BECAUSE WHILE I SAID

01:54:48.618 --> 01:54:50.353 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT IS NOT ABOVE THE

01:54:49.752 --> 01:54:51.053 line:78%
LAW, THE LAW CAN ONLY BE MADE

01:54:50.453 --> 01:54:51.687 line:78%
APPLICABLE TO HIM IN A CERTAIN

01:54:51.153 --> 01:54:52.555 line:78%
WAY WHILE HE IS IN OFFICE.

01:54:51.787 --> 01:54:53.556 line:78%
NOW IF A JUNIOR CONGRESSMAN CAN

01:54:52.655 --> 01:54:54.590 line:78%
COMMIT A CRIME ON THE FLOOR OF

01:54:53.656 --> 01:54:55.591 line:78%
THE HOUSE AS APPARENTLY AS

01:54:54.690 --> 01:55:00.796 line:78%
POSSIBLE, UNDER GRAVEL AND

01:54:55.691 --> 01:55:01.697 line:78%
JOHNSON, IS IT TO BE SAID THAT

01:55:00.896 --> 01:55:02.765 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED

01:55:01.797 --> 01:55:03.299 line:78%
STATES HAS LESS IMMUNITY THAN A

01:55:02.865 --> 01:55:03.699 line:78%
JUNIOR CONGRESSMAN?

01:55:03.399 --> 01:55:19.949 line:78%
I THINK NOT.

01:55:03.799 --> 01:55:21.083 line:78%
SO THAT, I SUGGEST TO YOU THAT

01:55:20.049 --> 01:55:21.817 line:78%
COMMON SENSE AND PROPER

01:55:21.183 --> 01:55:22.485 line:78%
CONSTRUCTION OF THE CONSTITUTION

01:55:21.917 --> 01:55:30.126 line:78%
IMPINGED WITHIN THE GRANT OF

01:55:22.585 --> 01:55:31.093 line:78%
EXECUTIVE POWER ALL OF THOSE

01:55:30.226 --> 01:55:32.194 line:78%
NECESSARY INGREDIENTS TO MAKE IT

01:55:31.193 --> 01:55:32.895 line:78%
WORK TO BE EFFECTIVE WHICH WOULD

01:55:32.295 --> 01:55:33.262 line:78%
INCLUDE IMMUNITY AND CRIMINAL

01:55:32.995 --> 01:55:34.096 line:78%
IMMUNITY.

01:55:33.362 --> 01:55:35.264 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT, WE SUGGEST,

01:55:34.196 --> 01:55:35.931 line:78%
CANNOT BE INDICTED, CAN'T EVEN

01:55:35.364 --> 01:55:36.732 line:78%
BE NAMED AS A CO-CONSPIRATOR

01:55:36.032 --> 01:55:37.466 line:78%
BECAUSE THAT'S AN ASSUMPTION OF

01:55:36.832 --> 01:55:38.301 line:78%
A LEGISLATIVE FUNCTION UNDER THE

01:55:37.566 --> 01:55:39.035 line:78%
CONSTITUTION.

01:55:38.401 --> 01:55:43.339 line:78%
AND, THEREFORE, WE SUGGEST THAT

01:55:39.135 --> 01:55:44.407 line:78%
EVEN IF THIS IS CRIMINAL THE

01:55:43.439 --> 01:55:45.041 line:78%
PRESIDENT IS IMMUNE FROM THE

01:55:44.507 --> 01:56:10.333 line:78%
ORDINARY CRIMINAL PROCESS.

01:55:45.141 --> 01:56:11.334 line:78%
HE IS NOT IMMUNE FROM PROCESS,

01:56:10.433 --> 01:56:12.335 line:78%
BUT THAT PROCESS THAT'S

01:56:11.434 --> 01:56:13.336 line:78%
AVAILABLE TO THE PRESIDENT IS A

01:56:12.435 --> 01:56:30.419 line:78%
PROCESS OF IMPEACHMENT WHICH

01:56:13.436 --> 01:56:31.454 line:78%
DOES NOT INCLUDE THE FUNCTION OF

01:56:30.519 --> 01:56:32.455 line:78%
THE JUDICIARY BRANCH.

01:56:31.554 --> 01:56:33.656 line:78%
AND, THEREFORE, WE SAY THAT IF,

01:56:32.555 --> 01:56:34.357 line:78%
UNDER GRAVEL, THE CONGRESSMAN IS

01:56:33.756 --> 01:56:35.057 line:78%
ENTITLED TO IMMUNITY EVEN FROM

01:56:34.457 --> 01:56:35.725 line:78%
CRIMINAL CONDUCT WHERE ACTIONS

01:56:35.157 --> 01:56:36.726 line:78%
TAKEN WITHIN THE LEGISLATIVE

01:56:35.825 --> 01:56:37.460 line:78%
SPHERE OF HIS CONDUCT, THEN IT

01:56:36.826 --> 01:56:38.194 line:78%
WOULD BE VERY HARD TO SUPPORT A

01:56:37.560 --> 01:56:38.894 line:78%
PROPOSITION THAT THE PRESIDENT,

01:56:38.294 --> 01:56:39.628 line:78%
AS THE CHIEF EXECUTIVE OF THE

01:56:38.994 --> 01:56:40.763 line:78%
COUNTRY, IS ENTITLED TO LESS.

01:56:39.729 --> 01:56:41.263 line:78%
&gt;&gt; EXCEPT THEY DIDN'T PUT HIM IN

01:56:40.863 --> 01:56:41.964 line:78%
THE CONSTITUTION.

01:56:41.364 --> 01:56:42.698 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT, AND THE REASON THEY

01:56:42.064 --> 01:56:43.733 line:78%
DIDN'T, SIR, WAS IT WAS NOT

01:56:42.798 --> 01:56:44.934 line:78%
FOUND TO BE NECESSARY.

01:56:43.833 --> 01:56:45.634 line:78%
THEY DIDN'T PUT CIVIL IMMUNITY

01:56:45.034 --> 01:56:46.335 line:78%
IN THE CONSTITUTION EITHER FOR

01:56:45.735 --> 01:56:49.805 line:78%
THE EXECUTIVE BRANCH AND THIS

01:56:46.435 --> 01:56:50.806 line:78%
COURT HAS FOUND, OF COURSE, THAT

01:56:49.905 --> 01:56:51.774 line:78%
THERE IS SUCH AN IMMUNITY.

01:56:50.906 --> 01:56:53.008 line:78%
I'M SORRY, SIR?

01:56:51.874 --> 01:56:53.709 line:78%
&gt;&gt; [INAUDIBLE]

01:56:53.109 --> 01:56:54.410 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT WAS A SPEECH AND DEBATE

01:56:53.809 --> 01:56:55.144 line:78%
CLAUSE CASE AND IT EVEN FORBAD

01:56:54.510 --> 01:56:55.845 line:78%
AS I UNDERSTAND THE GRAVEL CASE,

01:56:55.244 --> 01:56:56.846 line:78%
THE GRAND JURY INQUIRY INTO

01:56:55.945 --> 01:56:57.913 line:78%
MOTIVATIONS AND ACTIONS OF THE

01:56:56.946 --> 01:57:21.036 line:78%
SENATOR AND HIS AID.

01:56:58.013 --> 01:57:22.138 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BECAUSE THE CONSTITUTION SAID

01:57:21.170 --> 01:57:23.105 line:78%
SO.

01:57:22.238 --> 01:57:24.306 line:78%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT, AND I SUGGEST THE

01:57:23.205 --> 01:57:25.007 line:78%
CONSTITUTION, BY CLEAR

01:57:24.407 --> 01:57:25.708 line:78%
IMPLICATION PROVIDES THE SAME

01:57:25.107 --> 01:57:26.409 line:78%
NOT ONLY FOR THE EXECUTIVE BUT

01:57:25.808 --> 01:57:27.376 line:78%
FOR THE JUDICIAL AS WELL, BUT

01:57:26.509 --> 01:57:28.144 line:78%
CERTAINLY FOR THE EXECUTIVE.

01:57:27.476 --> 01:57:28.844 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND IF WE CAN'T FIND IT IN

01:57:28.244 --> 01:57:29.345 line:78%
THE CONSTITUTION, WHAT HAPPENS

01:57:28.944 --> 01:57:30.212 line:78%
TO YOUR ARGUMENT?

01:57:29.445 --> 01:57:31.347 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I WOULD SUGGEST YOU

01:57:30.312 --> 01:57:31.781 line:78%
SHOULD FIND IT IN THE

01:57:31.447 --> 01:57:32.381 line:78%
CONSTITUTION.

01:57:31.881 --> 01:57:33.282 line:78%
IT NEED NOT BE EXPLICIT.

01:57:32.481 --> 01:57:34.350 line:78%
IT CAN WELL BE IMPLIED.

01:57:33.382 --> 01:57:35.050 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE QUESTION IS IF WE CAN'T

01:57:34.450 --> 01:57:35.418 line:78%
FIND IT, WHAT HAPPENS TO YOUR

01:57:35.151 --> 01:57:36.252 line:78%
ARGUMENT?

01:57:35.518 --> 01:57:37.486 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IF YOU CANNOT FIND IT?

01:57:36.352 --> 01:57:38.187 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

01:57:37.586 --> 01:57:38.921 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THEN, IF YOUR HONOR PLEASE,

01:57:38.287 --> 01:57:39.655 line:78%
THAT PORTION OF THE ARGUMENT IS

01:57:39.021 --> 01:57:40.189 line:78%
LOST AS FAR AS THIS COURT'S

01:57:39.755 --> 01:57:41.090 line:78%
CONCERNED, I GUESS.

01:57:40.289 --> 01:57:41.824 line:78%
&gt;&gt; DON'T YOU -- YOU HAVEN'T LOST

01:57:41.190 --> 01:57:42.525 line:78%
YOUR OTHER POINT WHICH SAYS THIS

01:57:41.924 --> 01:57:44.393 line:78%
COURT CAN SET UP THE SAME KIND

01:57:42.625 --> 01:57:44.760 line:78%
OF PRIVILEGE THAT THEY'VE SET UP

01:57:44.493 --> 01:57:45.428 line:78%
IN OTHERS.

01:57:44.860 --> 01:57:46.429 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT.

01:57:45.528 --> 01:57:47.596 line:78%
AND, WE'RE SUGGESTING THAT IT

01:57:46.529 --> 01:57:48.330 line:78%
SHOULD IN THIS CASE NOT

01:57:47.696 --> 01:57:48.998 line:78%
NECESSARILY BECAUSE A GREAT DEAL

01:57:48.431 --> 01:57:49.732 line:78%
IS NOW LEFT TO BE GAINED BY

01:57:49.098 --> 01:57:50.499 line:78%
EXPUNGING THE GRAND JURY ACTION.

01:57:49.832 --> 01:57:51.500 line:78%
MY BROTHER IS RIGHT.

01:57:50.599 --> 01:57:52.701 line:78%
THE DAMAGES HAS BEEN DONE AND WE

01:57:51.600 --> 01:57:53.402 line:78%
THINK QUITE IMPROPERLY SO.

01:57:52.802 --> 01:57:54.103 line:78%
WE THINK THE TACTICS INVOLVED

01:57:53.502 --> 01:57:54.837 line:78%
WITH THE PROSECUTOR IN SEEKING

01:57:54.203 --> 01:57:55.571 line:78%
TO MAKE, ENLARGING THE SCOPE OF

01:57:54.937 --> 01:57:56.672 line:78%
ADMISSIBLE TESTIMONY IS HARDLY

01:57:55.671 --> 01:57:57.273 line:78%
WORTH WHAT HAS BEEN DONE HERE

01:57:56.772 --> 01:57:57.940 line:78%
BUT IT'S BEEN DONE.

01:57:57.373 --> 01:57:58.641 line:78%
BUT, IT SEEMS TO ME, HISTORY

01:57:58.040 --> 01:57:59.708 line:78%
WOULD E SERVED BY GRANTING OF

01:57:58.741 --> 01:58:00.443 line:78%
THE RELIEF WE HAVE PRAYED FOR

01:57:59.809 --> 01:58:01.110 line:78%
BELOW, NAMELY, TO EXPUNGE THIS.

01:58:00.543 --> 01:58:01.744 line:78%
SECONDLY, IT SEEMS TO ME THE

01:58:01.210 --> 01:58:02.645 line:78%
AMERICAN PEOPLE WOULD FEEL

01:58:01.844 --> 01:58:03.612 line:78%
BETTER ABOUT THE FAIRNESS OF THE

01:58:02.745 --> 01:58:04.613 line:78%
ISSUES NOW PENDING BEFORE THE

01:58:03.712 --> 01:58:05.614 line:78%
HOUSE IS THIS ACT WHICH WE SAY

01:58:04.713 --> 01:58:06.649 line:78%
WAS IMPROPER AND ILLEGAL WERE

01:58:05.714 --> 01:58:07.716 line:78%
EXPUNGED.

01:58:06.749 --> 01:58:08.751 line:78%
BUT IN SO FAR AS THE MECHANISMS

01:58:07.817 --> 01:58:09.752 line:78%
OF THIS CASE ARE CONCERNED, IT

01:58:08.851 --> 01:58:10.753 line:78%
DESTROYS OR REMOVES A BASIS UPON

01:58:09.852 --> 01:58:30.973 line:78%
WHICH THEY CONTEND THEY ARE

01:58:10.853 --> 01:58:31.841 line:78%
ENTITLED TO THESE DOCUMENTS.

01:58:31.073 --> 01:58:32.975 line:78%
I'D LIKE TO ADDRESS THAT FOR A

01:58:31.941 --> 01:58:33.976 line:78%
MOMENT.

01:58:33.075 --> 01:58:35.177 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE'VE BEEN ASKED MANY TIMES

01:58:34.076 --> 01:58:35.845 line:78%
TO DO THAT IN OTHER CASES WITH

01:58:35.277 --> 01:58:36.679 line:78%
RESPECT TO THE GRAND JURIES.

01:58:35.945 --> 01:58:37.379 line:78%
UP TODAY, I DON'T THINK WE'VE

01:58:36.779 --> 01:58:38.147 line:78%
EVER COME NEAR ANYWHERE TO IT.

01:58:37.480 --> 01:58:39.148 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND UP TODAY, YOU'VE NEVER

01:58:38.247 --> 01:58:39.882 line:78%
HAD A PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED

01:58:39.248 --> 01:58:40.282 line:78%
STATES NAMED AS A CO-CONSPIRATOR

01:58:39.982 --> 01:58:41.083 line:78%
EITHER, SIR.

01:58:40.382 --> 01:58:42.251 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S VERY TRUE.

01:58:41.183 --> 01:58:42.885 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THE PRESIDENT OF THE

01:58:42.351 --> 01:58:43.686 line:78%
UNITED STATES --[LAUGHTER]

01:58:42.985 --> 01:58:44.386 line:78%
AND I DON'T MEAN TO BE FACETIOUS

01:58:43.786 --> 01:58:45.087 line:78%
ABOUT IT BUT THE PRESIDENT OF

01:58:44.487 --> 01:58:46.088 line:78%
THE UNITED STATES, WE SUGGEST,

01:58:45.187 --> 01:58:47.256 line:78%
CAN BE PROCEEDED AGAINST ONLY BY

01:58:46.188 --> 01:58:47.957 line:78%
IMPEACHMENT WHILE IN OFFICE AND

01:58:47.356 --> 01:58:48.624 line:78%
HIS POWERS ARE UNABATED UNTIL

01:58:48.057 --> 01:58:49.124 line:78%
SUCH TIME AS HE LEAVES THAT

01:58:48.724 --> 01:58:50.292 line:78%
OFFICE.

01:58:49.225 --> 01:58:50.960 line:78%
NOW, WITH RESPECT TO THIS

01:58:50.392 --> 01:58:51.694 line:78%
SUGGESTION THAT A GRAND JURY

01:58:51.060 --> 01:58:52.127 line:78%
FINDING HIS PRIMA FACIE EVIDENCE

01:58:51.994 --> 01:58:53.095 line:78%
--

01:58:52.228 --> 01:58:54.063 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT, OF COURSE, HAVE NEVER

01:58:53.195 --> 01:59:05.140 line:78%
BEEN DECIDED EITHER.

01:58:54.163 --> 01:59:06.108 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO.

01:59:05.241 --> 01:59:07.209 line:78%
THIS CASE IS UNUSUAL IN MANY

01:59:06.208 --> 01:59:08.410 line:78%
RESPECTS.

01:59:07.309 --> 01:59:09.078 line:78%
THIS SUGGESTION THAT A GRAND

01:59:08.511 --> 01:59:09.745 line:78%
JURY FINDING IS PRIMA FACIE

01:59:09.178 --> 01:59:10.412 line:78%
EVIDENCE AND, THEREFORE, THE

01:59:09.845 --> 01:59:11.313 line:78%
PRESIDENT HAS LOST WHATEVER

01:59:10.513 --> 01:59:12.314 line:78%
PRIVILEGE HE OTHERWISE WOULD

01:59:11.413 --> 01:59:13.482 line:78%
HAVE HAD IT JUST ISN'T BORNE OUT

01:59:12.414 --> 01:59:14.216 line:78%
BY EITHER THE FACTS OR THE LEGAL

01:59:13.582 --> 01:59:14.917 line:78%
ISSUES AND PRINCIPALS INVOLVED.

01:59:14.316 --> 01:59:35.437 line:78%
THE GRAND JURY FINDING IS NOT

01:59:15.017 --> 01:59:36.472 line:78%
PRIMA FACIE EVIDENCE.

01:59:35.538 --> 01:59:37.473 line:78%
EVEN IF IT'S MENTIONED IN AN

01:59:36.572 --> 01:59:38.607 line:78%
OPENING ARGUMENT IN A CRIMINAL

01:59:37.573 --> 01:59:38.974 line:78%
TRIAL, THERE'S A GRAVE RISK OF A

01:59:38.707 --> 01:59:39.675 line:78%
MISTRIAL.

01:59:39.074 --> 01:59:40.576 line:78%
THE CASES CITED BY MY BROTHER,

01:59:39.775 --> 01:59:41.577 line:78%
PARTICULARLY THE CLARK CASE, ARE

01:59:40.676 --> 01:59:45.781 line:78%
CLEARLY CASES WHICH REQUIRE A

01:59:41.677 --> 01:59:46.515 line:78%
SHOWING IN COURT OR, IN CLARK, A

01:59:45.881 --> 01:59:47.182 line:78%
SHOWING TO THE JUDGE THAT THERE

01:59:46.615 --> 01:59:47.683 line:78%
WAS PRIMA FACIE EVIDENCE OF

01:59:47.283 --> 01:59:48.817 line:78%
WRONG DOING.

01:59:47.783 --> 01:59:49.518 line:78%
YOU MAY RECALL THAT'S A CASE

01:59:48.918 --> 01:59:50.219 line:78%
INVOLVING INVESTIGATION INTO A

01:59:49.618 --> 01:59:50.920 line:78%
JUROR AS TO WHETHER OR NOT THE

01:59:50.319 --> 01:59:51.720 line:78%
JUROR HAD PERFORMED PROPERLY,

01:59:51.020 --> 01:59:52.655 line:78%
AND THE JUROR HAD BEEN SHOWN,

01:59:51.820 --> 01:59:53.656 line:78%
HAD TESTIFIED FALSELY IN THE

01:59:52.755 --> 01:59:54.690 line:78%
QUALIFICATIONS THAT SHE HAD

01:59:53.756 --> 01:59:55.824 line:78%
NEVER HAD ANY BUSINESS RELATIONS

01:59:54.790 --> 01:59:56.258 line:78%
WITH ONE OF THE PARTIES WHEN, IN

01:59:55.925 --> 01:59:57.059 line:78%
FACT, SHE HAD.

01:59:56.358 --> 01:59:57.760 line:78%
THE COURT SAID "WELL, THERE'S A

01:59:57.159 --> 01:59:58.761 line:78%
FINDING OF WRONG DOING AND,

01:59:57.860 --> 01:59:59.728 line:78%
BASED ON THAT, NOW I WILL LOOK

01:59:58.861 --> 02:00:04.967 line:78%
INTO THE JUROR'S DELIBERATIONS

01:59:59.828 --> 02:00:05.801 line:78%
TO SEE WHAT SHE DID."

02:00:05.067 --> 02:00:08.804 line:78%
BUT, JUSTICE CARDOZO MADE IT

02:00:05.901 --> 02:00:09.805 line:78%
VERY CLEAR THAT IF HE HADN'T

02:00:08.904 --> 02:00:17.913 line:78%
BEEN ABLE TO MAKE A PRIMA FACIE

02:00:09.905 --> 02:00:18.914 line:78%
SHOWING A WRONG DOING BY

02:00:18.013 --> 02:00:19.949 line:78%
EVIDENCE BEFORE HIM THERE WOULD

02:00:19.014 --> 02:00:32.061 line:78%
HAVE BEEN NO CAUSE FOR "LETTING

02:00:20.049 --> 02:00:33.095 line:78%
IN THE LIGHT," AS HE PUT IT.

02:00:32.161 --> 02:00:34.296 line:78%
AND, THE UN CASE AND OTHER CASES

02:00:33.195 --> 02:00:34.964 line:78%
WHICH ARE RELIED ON BY MY

02:00:34.396 --> 02:00:35.698 line:78%
BROTHERS ARE ALL CASES WHERE

02:00:35.064 --> 02:00:45.441 line:78%
THERE WAS A PRIMA FACIE SHOWING

02:00:35.798 --> 02:00:46.175 line:78%
IN A COURTROOM.

02:00:45.541 --> 02:00:46.475 line:78%
A GRAND JURY CHARGE IS NOT PRIMA

02:00:46.275 --> 02:00:47.443 line:78%
FACIE.

02:00:46.575 --> 02:00:47.843 line:78%
IN THE FIRST PLACE, IT'S ONLY

02:00:47.543 --> 02:00:48.677 line:78%
ACCUSATORY.

02:00:47.943 --> 02:00:54.516 line:78%
IT'S NOT EVEN ADMISSIBLE NOR CAN

02:00:48.777 --> 02:00:55.217 line:78%
IT BE REFERRED TO IN A TRIAL.

02:00:54.617 --> 02:00:55.918 line:78%
SECONDLY, IT CAN WELL INVOLVE

02:00:55.317 --> 02:00:56.752 line:78%
INCOMPETENT EVIDENCE, AS THIS

02:00:56.018 --> 02:00:58.387 line:78%
COURT RECENTLY DECIDED, AND IT'S

02:00:56.852 --> 02:00:59.355 line:78%
TOTALLY INAPPROPRIATE TO SUGGEST

02:00:58.487 --> 02:01:00.389 line:78%
THAT A PRESIDENT WHO OTHERWISE

02:00:59.455 --> 02:01:02.424 line:78%
WOULD HAVE A VERY VALUABLE

02:01:00.489 --> 02:01:03.559 line:78%
PRIVILEGE AND I THINK I SHOULD

02:01:02.524 --> 02:01:04.193 line:78%
EMPHASIZE THE VALUE OF THESE

02:01:03.659 --> 02:01:19.742 line:78%
PRIVILEGES BECAUSE IT IS A

02:01:04.293 --> 02:01:20.376 line:78%
VALUABLE PRIVILEGE.

02:01:19.842 --> 02:01:21.110 line:78%
ALL YOU HAVE TO DO IS READ

02:01:20.476 --> 02:01:21.810 line:78%
JUSTICE REED'S DECISION IN

02:01:21.210 --> 02:01:22.611 line:78%
KAISER ALUMINUM WHEN HE SPELLS

02:01:21.910 --> 02:01:23.812 line:78%
IT OUT QUITE CLEARLY THE

02:01:22.711 --> 02:01:24.546 line:78%
IMPORTANCE AND VALUE OF THIS

02:01:23.912 --> 02:01:25.280 line:78%
PRIVILEGE TO SIMPLY SAY TO HAVE

02:01:24.647 --> 02:01:25.981 line:78%
A GRAND JURY MAKE A CHARGE THAT

02:01:25.381 --> 02:01:26.815 line:78%
DESTROYS THAT PRIVILEGE IS AN

02:01:26.081 --> 02:01:27.249 line:78%
ARGUMENT THAT I DON'T THINK CAN

02:01:26.915 --> 02:01:27.950 line:78%
BE SUSTAINED.

02:01:27.349 --> 02:01:28.717 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MR. ST. CLAIR, YOU HAVE NOT

02:01:28.050 --> 02:01:29.718 line:78%
MENTIONED IN YOUR ARGUMENT A FEW

02:01:28.817 --> 02:01:42.765 line:78%
MOMENTS AGO ON THE QUESTION OF

02:01:29.818 --> 02:01:43.766 line:78%
THE ABSENCE OF ANY PROVISION FOR

02:01:42.865 --> 02:01:44.833 line:78%
IMMUNITY FOR JUDGES OR

02:01:43.866 --> 02:01:52.908 line:78%
PRESIDENTS, YOU HAVEN'T

02:01:44.933 --> 02:01:53.909 line:78%
MENTIONED THE HOLDING OF THIS

02:01:53.008 --> 02:01:55.077 line:78%
COURT IN PIERSON AGAINST RAID

02:01:54.009 --> 02:01:55.811 line:78%
WHEREAS, I RECALL IT, THE COURT

02:01:55.177 --> 02:01:56.412 line:78%
ASSUMED WITH THE SENTENCE OR TWO

02:01:55.911 --> 02:01:57.146 line:78%
THAT THERE WAS ABSOLUTE

02:01:56.512 --> 02:01:57.946 line:78%
PRIVILEGE FOR THE JUDICIARY BUT

02:01:57.246 --> 02:02:05.220 line:78%
THAT THE PRIVILEGES OF THE

02:01:58.047 --> 02:02:06.188 line:78%
EXECUTIVE, IN THAT CASE A

02:02:05.320 --> 02:02:07.156 line:78%
POLICEMAN, WAS QUALIFIED.

02:02:06.288 --> 02:02:17.332 line:78%
THE COURT HAD NO DIFFICULTY IN

02:02:07.256 --> 02:02:18.367 line:78%
CONCLUDING THAT IT DID NOT

02:02:17.433 --> 02:02:19.535 line:78%
REQUIRE AN EXPRESS

02:02:18.467 --> 02:02:20.269 line:78%
CONSTITUTIONAL PROVISION TO

02:02:19.635 --> 02:02:20.669 line:78%
SPELL OUT AN ABSOLUTE PRIVILEGE

02:02:20.369 --> 02:02:21.403 line:78%
FOR JUDGES.

02:02:20.769 --> 02:02:22.538 line:78%
THESE WERE STATE JUDGES IN THAT

02:02:21.503 --> 02:02:23.072 line:78%
CASE OF COURSE.

02:02:22.638 --> 02:02:24.406 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S RIGHT.

02:02:23.172 --> 02:02:25.407 line:78%
WELL, IF YOUR HONOR PLEASE, I

02:02:24.506 --> 02:02:26.408 line:78%
DON'T BELIEVE THAT SIMPLY

02:02:25.507 --> 02:02:33.682 line:78%
BECAUSE THE CONSTITUTION DOES

02:02:26.508 --> 02:02:34.583 line:78%
NOT EXPLICITLY STATE IMMUNITY,

02:02:33.782 --> 02:03:03.779 line:78%
AS IT DOES IN THE SPEECH AND

02:02:34.683 --> 02:03:04.913 line:78%
DEBATE CLAUSE, SHOULD THIS COURT

02:03:03.879 --> 02:03:05.414 line:78%
HOLD IT DOES NOT EXIST IN

02:03:05.013 --> 02:03:06.115 line:78%
CRIMINAL MATTERS.

02:03:05.514 --> 02:03:06.849 line:78%
I WOULD LIKE TO MAKE ONE POINT

02:03:06.215 --> 02:03:07.816 line:78%
WITH THE COURT HOWEVER, BECAUSE

02:03:06.949 --> 02:03:08.951 line:78%
I'M SURE THE POINT WILL BE

02:03:07.916 --> 02:03:09.351 line:78%
RAISED CONCERNING JUSTICE CARR

02:03:09.051 --> 02:03:10.085 line:78%
FOR EXAMPLE.

02:03:09.451 --> 02:03:11.887 line:78%
THERE IS A DISTINCT DIFFERENCE,

02:03:10.185 --> 02:03:26.001 line:78%
AS WE POINTED OUT IN OUR REPLY

02:03:11.987 --> 02:03:27.202 line:78%
BRIEF AS WE VIEW IT, BETWEEN A

02:03:26.101 --> 02:03:27.903 line:78%
PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES,

02:03:27.302 --> 02:03:28.570 line:78%
A SINGLE INDIVIDUAL IN WHO THE

02:03:28.003 --> 02:03:29.071 line:78%
ENTIRE EXECUTIVE FUNCTION IS

02:03:28.670 --> 02:03:30.072 line:78%
VESTED.

02:03:29.171 --> 02:03:33.142 line:78%
A PRESIDENT SERVES 7 DAYS A WEEK

02:03:30.172 --> 02:03:34.176 line:78%
24 HOURS A DAY, AND ONLY HE OR

02:03:33.242 --> 02:03:35.244 line:78%
THOSE UNDER HIM PERFORMING HIS

02:03:34.276 --> 02:03:35.878 line:78%
FUNCTIONS CAN EXERCISE THE

02:03:35.344 --> 02:03:36.278 line:78%
EXECUTIVE FUNCTION OF OUR

02:03:35.978 --> 02:03:37.179 line:78%
GOVERNMENT.

02:03:36.378 --> 02:03:38.347 line:78%
NOW, IF A CONGRESSMAN OR A

02:03:37.279 --> 02:03:38.947 line:78%
SENATOR OR EVEN A JUDGE --

02:03:38.447 --> 02:03:39.581 line:78%
&gt;&gt; OR A VICE PRESIDENT.

02:03:39.047 --> 02:03:40.349 line:78%
&gt;&gt; OR A VICE PRESIDENT IS

02:03:39.681 --> 02:03:40.649 line:78%
REMOVED FROM HIS DUTIES, MATTERS

02:03:40.449 --> 02:03:41.383 line:78%
GO ON.

02:03:40.749 --> 02:03:42.284 line:78%
BUT A PRESIDENT DOESN'T HAVE

02:03:41.483 --> 02:03:43.352 line:78%
THAT OPPORTUNITY TO TAKE A

02:03:42.384 --> 02:03:44.386 line:78%
VACATION AND IT'S VESTED IN ONE

02:03:43.452 --> 02:03:45.521 line:78%
INDIVIDUAL AND DELIBERATELY SO.

02:03:44.486 --> 02:03:46.221 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THIS IS PRETTY FAR-FIELD FROM

02:03:45.621 --> 02:03:46.922 line:78%
THE BASIC QUESTION HERE, WHICH

02:03:46.321 --> 02:03:47.723 line:78%
IS THE TESTIMONIAL PRIVILEGE.

02:03:47.022 --> 02:03:48.524 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE SAY IT'S A CONSTITUTIONAL

02:03:48.390 --> 02:03:49.224 line:78%
--

02:03:48.624 --> 02:03:49.925 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NOT PROSECUTORIAL IMMUNITY,

02:03:49.324 --> 02:03:50.659 line:78%
BUT TESTIMONIAL PRIVILEGES ARE

02:03:50.025 --> 02:03:51.026 line:78%
WHAT WE'RE DEALING WITH HERE

02:03:50.759 --> 02:03:51.593 line:78%
BASICALLY.

02:03:51.126 --> 02:03:52.461 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT.

02:03:51.693 --> 02:03:53.462 line:78%
I THINK SO.

02:03:52.561 --> 02:03:54.463 line:78%
I WOULD WANT TO THE POINT WITH

02:03:53.562 --> 02:03:55.597 line:78%
YOU THAT WE THINK THE PRIVILEGE

02:03:54.563 --> 02:03:56.165 line:78%
WE'RE ARGUING FOR IS BOTH COMMON

02:03:55.697 --> 02:04:12.614 line:78%
LAW AND CONSTITUTION.

02:03:56.265 --> 02:04:13.615 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I UNDERSTAND THAT.

02:04:12.714 --> 02:04:14.683 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S CONSTITUTIONAL BECAUSE

02:04:13.715 --> 02:04:14.983 line:78%
IT'S INHERENT IN THE EXECUTIVE

02:04:14.783 --> 02:04:15.684 line:78%
POWER.

02:04:15.083 --> 02:04:16.752 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I UNDERSTAND YOUR ARGUMENT.

02:04:15.784 --> 02:04:17.519 line:78%
BUT THIS MATTER --

02:04:16.852 --> 02:04:18.086 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND IT'S COMMON LAW BECAUSE

02:04:17.619 --> 02:04:18.821 line:78%
IT HAS ALWAYS EXISTED.

02:04:18.187 --> 02:04:19.822 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WHETHER OR NOT THEY CAN -- A

02:04:18.921 --> 02:04:20.355 line:78%
JUDGE CAN BE PROSECUTED

02:04:19.922 --> 02:04:20.989 line:78%
CRIMINALLY OR IS --

02:04:20.455 --> 02:04:21.690 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT HAS TO DO WITH THESE

02:04:21.089 --> 02:04:22.891 line:78%
QUESTIONS OF IMMUNITY.

02:04:21.790 --> 02:04:23.625 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT HAS NOTHING TO DO WITH

02:04:22.991 --> 02:04:24.293 line:78%
TESTIMONIAL PRIVILEGE, DOES IT?

02:04:23.725 --> 02:04:25.027 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, MY BROTHER SEEMS TO

02:04:24.393 --> 02:04:25.928 line:78%
THINK IT DOES BECAUSE THEY SAY,

02:04:25.127 --> 02:04:26.628 line:78%
BECAUSE OF THE IMPLICATIONS OF

02:04:26.028 --> 02:04:27.362 line:78%
CRIMINALITY HERE THE PRESIDENT

02:04:26.728 --> 02:04:27.896 line:78%
HAS LOST SOMETHING HE OTHERWISE

02:04:27.462 --> 02:04:30.766 line:78%
WOULD NOT HAVE HAD.

02:04:27.996 --> 02:04:31.733 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I UNDERSTAND THAT.

02:04:30.866 --> 02:04:32.901 line:78%
SINCE I HAVE ALREADY INTERRUPTED

02:04:31.834 --> 02:04:33.335 line:78%
YOU, MAY I?

02:04:33.001 --> 02:04:34.069 line:78%
&gt;&gt; PLEASE DO.

02:04:33.435 --> 02:04:34.803 line:78%
&gt;&gt; TO RAIL UPON YOUR GOOD NATURE

02:04:34.169 --> 02:04:35.838 line:78%
A LITTLE MORE MR. ST. CLAIR, TO

02:04:34.903 --> 02:04:36.839 line:78%
ASK YOU WHETHER IT IS YOUR CLAIM

02:04:35.938 --> 02:04:37.873 line:78%
THAT ANY OF THESE MATERIALS HAVE

02:04:36.939 --> 02:04:38.874 line:78%
TO DO WITH WHAT HAVE SOMETIMES

02:04:37.973 --> 02:04:40.909 line:78%
BEEN CALLED MATTERS OF STATE,

02:04:38.974 --> 02:04:49.051 line:78%
I.E. MATTERS OF INTERNATIONAL

02:04:41.009 --> 02:04:50.052 line:78%
RELATIONS OR NATIONAL DEFENSE.

02:04:49.151 --> 02:04:51.253 line:78%
MR. JAWORSKI ASSURE TO US THAT

02:04:50.152 --> 02:04:52.020 line:78%
THEY DID NOT INVOLVE MATTERS OF

02:04:51.353 --> 02:04:52.754 line:78%
STATE, BUT I'M ABOUT TO HEAR

02:04:52.120 --> 02:04:53.455 line:78%
WHAT YOU HAVE TO SAY ABOUT THAT,

02:04:52.855 --> 02:04:54.089 line:78%
BECAUSE AS YOU WELL KNOW BOTH

02:04:53.555 --> 02:04:55.090 line:78%
THE COMMENTATORS AND COURT

02:04:54.189 --> 02:04:56.124 line:78%
DECISIONS HAVE MADE A DICHOTOMY

02:04:55.190 --> 02:04:57.125 line:78%
BETWEEN THE PRIVILEGE THAT EXIST

02:04:56.225 --> 02:05:05.234 line:78%
WITH RESPECT TO ORDINARY GENERAL

02:04:57.226 --> 02:05:06.235 line:78%
CONFIDENTIALITY ON ONE HAND OF

02:05:05.334 --> 02:05:07.269 line:78%
THE EXECUTIVE, AND MATTERS OF

02:05:06.335 --> 02:05:08.303 line:78%
STATE ON THE OTHER TO WHICH A

02:05:07.369 --> 02:05:23.518 line:78%
HIGHER PRIVILEGE HAS SOMETIMES

02:05:08.403 --> 02:05:24.319 line:78%
BEEN THOUGHT TO BE ACCORDED.

02:05:23.619 --> 02:05:25.454 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, I THINK IF A HIGHER

02:05:24.419 --> 02:05:25.854 line:78%
PRIVILEGE HAS BEEN ACCORDED, IT

02:05:25.554 --> 02:05:26.588 line:78%
SHOULD NOT.

02:05:25.954 --> 02:05:27.322 line:78%
BUT IN ANY EVENT, THE PRIVILEGE

02:05:26.688 --> 02:05:28.390 line:78%
OF CONFIDENTIALITY IS NOT

02:05:27.422 --> 02:05:29.524 line:78%
UNIMPORTANT.

02:05:28.490 --> 02:05:29.958 line:78%
HOWEVER, LET ME DIRECT MYSELF TO

02:05:29.625 --> 02:05:30.659 line:78%
YOUR QUESTION.

02:05:30.058 --> 02:05:31.560 line:78%
THE ANSWER TO YOUR QUESTION IS

02:05:30.759 --> 02:05:31.994 line:78%
NO ONE KNOWS.

02:05:31.660 --> 02:05:32.728 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT YOU --

02:05:32.094 --> 02:05:33.462 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU WON'T KNOW UNTIL YOU

02:05:32.828 --> 02:05:42.604 line:78%
LISTEN TO THESE TAPES AS TO WHAT

02:05:33.562 --> 02:05:43.772 line:78%
SUBJECTS ARE DISCUSSED.

02:05:42.704 --> 02:05:44.539 line:78%
MY BROTHER CAN ONLY STATE THAT

02:05:43.872 --> 02:05:45.240 line:78%
IT'S PROBABLE THEY RELATE, AT

02:05:44.640 --> 02:05:45.707 line:78%
LEAST IN PART, TO WHATEVER HE

02:05:45.340 --> 02:05:46.675 line:78%
SAYS, WATERGATE.

02:05:45.807 --> 02:05:47.676 line:78%
OR IT'S LIKELY THAT IT MIGHT.

02:05:46.775 --> 02:05:48.644 line:78%
AND, I HAVE HAD THE EXPERIENCE

02:05:47.776 --> 02:05:49.845 line:78%
FOR EXEMPT WHERE CIRCUMSTANCES

02:05:48.744 --> 02:05:50.479 line:78%
WERE SUCH THAT THE HOUSE

02:05:49.945 --> 02:05:51.213 line:78%
COMMITTEE FELT THAT IT WAS

02:05:50.579 --> 02:05:51.847 line:78%
LIKELY THAT A CONVERSATION TOOK

02:05:51.313 --> 02:05:52.714 line:78%
PLACE BETWEEN THE ATTORNEY

02:05:51.947 --> 02:05:53.682 line:78%
GENERAL, MR. MITCHELL, AND THE

02:05:52.814 --> 02:05:54.650 line:78%
PRESIDENT REGARDING PLANS FOR

02:05:53.782 --> 02:06:03.759 line:78%
SURVEILLANCE OF DEMOCRATIC

02:05:54.750 --> 02:06:04.826 line:78%
PARTIES.

02:06:03.859 --> 02:06:05.727 line:78%
WHEN YOU LOOK AT THE

02:06:04.927 --> 02:06:08.797 line:78%
CONVERSATION, IT WASN'T THERE AT

02:06:05.827 --> 02:06:10.999 line:78%
ALL.

02:06:08.897 --> 02:06:11.733 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT IN THIS TAPE --

02:06:11.099 --> 02:06:12.401 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SO, I HAVE NO WAY OF KNOWING

02:06:11.833 --> 02:06:13.101 line:78%
NOR DOES THE PROSECUTOR KNOW

02:06:12.501 --> 02:06:13.769 line:78%
WHAT ADDITIONAL MATTERS MAY BE

02:06:13.201 --> 02:06:24.846 line:78%
INTERWOVEN INTO THESE

02:06:13.869 --> 02:06:25.881 line:78%
CONVERSATIONS.

02:06:24.947 --> 02:06:26.882 line:78%
ONE THING IS CERTAIN.

02:06:25.981 --> 02:06:28.083 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AM I CORRECT IN BELIEVING,

02:06:26.982 --> 02:06:28.817 line:78%
MR. ST. CLAIR, IN UNDERSTANDING,

02:06:28.183 --> 02:06:29.518 line:78%
MR. ST. CLAIR, THAT IN THIS CASE

02:06:28.917 --> 02:06:30.152 line:78%
TO DATE NO REPRESENTATION HAS

02:06:29.618 --> 02:06:30.953 line:78%
BEEN MADE BY AFFIDAVIT OR

02:06:30.252 --> 02:06:32.054 line:78%
PROFESSIONAL REPRESENTATION OR

02:06:31.053 --> 02:06:32.688 line:78%
OTHERWISE THAT ANY OF THESE

02:06:32.154 --> 02:06:33.221 line:78%
MATERIALS HAVE TO DO WITH

02:06:32.788 --> 02:06:47.235 line:78%
NATIONAL DEFENSE OR

02:06:33.322 --> 02:06:47.903 line:78%
INTERNATIONAL RELATIONS?

02:06:47.336 --> 02:06:48.603 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NO, AND NO REPRESENTATION

02:06:48.003 --> 02:06:48.937 line:78%
COULD BE MADE TO THE CONTRARY

02:06:48.704 --> 02:06:49.671 line:78%
EITHER.

02:06:49.037 --> 02:06:50.272 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND THAT WOULD BE, THEREFORE,

02:06:49.771 --> 02:06:51.273 line:78%
A MATTER TO BE UNDER THE

02:06:50.372 --> 02:06:51.740 line:78%
EXISTING ORDER NOW UNDER REVIEW

02:06:51.373 --> 02:06:52.441 line:78%
OF JUDGE SIRICA.

02:06:51.840 --> 02:06:53.141 line:78%
THAT WOULD BE SUBMITTED TO HIM

02:06:52.541 --> 02:06:54.142 line:78%
LATER IN CAMERA, CORRECT?

02:06:53.241 --> 02:06:58.113 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IF THIS COURT FINDS --

02:06:54.242 --> 02:06:59.181 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I SAY UNDER HIS EXISTING

