02:51:38.257 --> 02:51:42.128 line:78%
THAT'S THE JUDICIAL PROCESS.

02:51:41.227 --> 02:51:44.130 line:78%
SO, SEPARATION OF POWERS HERE

02:51:42.228 --> 02:51:45.097 line:78%
WITH THE NOTION OF POLITICAL

02:51:44.230 --> 02:51:46.132 line:78%
QUESTION WHETHER SOMETHING IS

02:51:45.197 --> 02:51:48.134 line:78%
COMMITTED TO THE FINAL

02:51:46.232 --> 02:51:50.169 line:78%
DETERMINATION OF ANOTHER BRANCH

02:51:48.234 --> 02:51:51.170 line:78%
FAR FROM SUPPORTING THE

02:51:50.269 --> 02:51:53.239 line:78%
PRESIDENT'S POSITION DEMANDS

02:51:51.270 --> 02:51:56.242 line:78%
THAT THE COURT AFFIRM THE ACTION

02:51:53.339 --> 02:51:57.243 line:78%
THAT JUDGE SIRICA HAS TAKEN.

02:51:56.342 --> 02:51:58.177 line:78%
THIS IS EMPHATICALLY THE

02:51:57.343 --> 02:52:03.449 line:78%
PROVIDENCE OF THIS COURT TO

02:51:58.277 --> 02:52:06.285 line:78%
DECIDE.

02:52:03.549 --> 02:52:10.322 line:78%
NOT TO BELABOR THE POINT, BUT

02:52:06.385 --> 02:52:13.292 line:78%
PERHAPS THE FINEST CHAPTER IN

02:52:10.423 --> 02:52:17.263 line:78%
THE COURT'S RECENT HISTORY HAS

02:52:13.392 --> 02:52:18.297 line:78%
COME UPON THESE CHAPTERS AND HAD

02:52:17.363 --> 02:52:21.300 line:78%
COME IN THE FIELDS OF

02:52:18.397 --> 02:52:23.302 line:78%
REAPPORTIONMENT, CIVIL RIGHTS,

02:52:21.400 --> 02:52:24.303 line:78%
AND THE PROCEDURAL RIGHTS OF THE

02:52:23.402 --> 02:52:26.305 line:78%
CRIMINALLY ACCUSED WOULD BE

02:52:24.403 --> 02:52:28.340 line:78%
NAÏVE TO SAY THAT THOSE WERE NOT

02:52:26.405 --> 02:52:30.376 line:78%
PROFOUNDLY POLITICALLY IMPORTANT

02:52:28.441 --> 02:52:31.410 line:78%
DECISIONS BUT THEY WERE MADE AS

02:52:30.476 --> 02:52:34.480 line:78%
DECISIONS OF CONSTITUTIONAL LAW

02:52:31.510 --> 02:52:39.485 line:78%
DESPITE THE CONSEQUENCES THAT

02:52:34.580 --> 02:52:40.453 line:78%
POLITICAL BRANCHES MIGHT FACE.

02:52:39.585 --> 02:52:41.454 line:78%
DESPITE THE PUBLIC REACTION, THE

02:52:40.553 --> 02:52:53.466 line:78%
COURT UNDERSTOOD ITS DUTY TO

02:52:41.554 --> 02:52:54.567 line:78%
INTERPRET THE CONSTITUTION.

02:52:53.566 --> 02:52:55.301 line:78%
THAT'S ALL WE ASK FOR TODAY.

02:52:54.667 --> 02:52:55.601 line:78%
THAT'S ALL JUDGE SIRICA HAS

02:52:55.401 --> 02:52:56.602 line:78%
DONE.

02:52:55.701 --> 02:52:56.969 line:78%
WE BELIEVE HE HAS DONE IT

02:52:56.702 --> 02:52:57.636 line:78%
CORRECTLY.

02:52:57.069 --> 02:52:58.037 line:78%
WE BELIEVE THE CASE IS FULLY

02:52:57.737 --> 02:52:58.738 line:78%
JUSTICIABLE.

02:52:58.137 --> 02:52:59.538 line:78%
WE BELIEVE THE PRINCIPLES THAT

02:52:58.838 --> 02:53:00.506 line:78%
HAVE BEEN BRIEFED BY THE PARTIES

02:52:59.638 --> 02:53:04.543 line:78%
SUPPORT THE CORRECTNESS OF THE

02:53:00.606 --> 02:53:06.579 line:78%
DECISION BELOW.

02:53:04.643 --> 02:53:08.614 line:78%
AND, WE SUBMIT THAT THIS COURT

02:53:06.679 --> 02:53:11.684 line:78%
SHOULD FULLY EXPLICITLY AND

02:53:08.714 --> 02:53:19.692 line:78%
DECISIVELY AND DEFINITIVELY

02:53:11.784 --> 02:53:20.826 line:78%
UPHOLD JUDGE SIRICA'S DECISION.

02:53:19.792 --> 02:53:21.460 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU, MR. LACOVAR.

02:53:20.926 --> 02:53:21.894 line:78%
MR. ST. CLAIR, YOU HAVE 15

02:53:21.560 --> 02:53:22.695 line:78%
MINUTES LEFT.

02:53:21.994 --> 02:53:26.932 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU, MR. CHIEF JUSTICE

02:53:22.795 --> 02:53:27.733 line:78%
AND MEMBERS OF THE COURT.

02:53:27.032 --> 02:53:28.801 line:78%
IN RESPONSE TO MY BROTHER'S MOST

02:53:27.833 --> 02:53:29.802 line:78%
RECENT ARGUMENT, OF COURSE

02:53:28.901 --> 02:53:32.805 line:78%
SAWYER WAS AN IMPORTANT CASE

02:53:29.902 --> 02:53:34.807 line:78%
WITH POLITICAL IMPLICATIONS.

02:53:32.905 --> 02:53:36.776 line:78%
OF COURSE, THE OTHER CASES WERE

02:53:34.907 --> 02:53:37.743 line:78%
IN IT OF THEMSELVES IMPORTANT

02:53:36.876 --> 02:53:40.780 line:78%
CASES WITH POLITICAL

02:53:37.843 --> 02:53:41.814 line:78%
IMPLICATIONS.

02:53:40.880 --> 02:53:43.849 line:78%
BUT, THIS CASE IS DIFFERENT IN

02:53:41.914 --> 02:53:44.884 line:78%
THAT THE DECISION IN THIS CASE

02:53:43.949 --> 02:53:48.954 line:78%
WILL HAVE AN UNDENIABLE IMPACT

02:53:44.984 --> 02:53:50.990 line:78%
ON ANOTHER PROCEEDING IN ANOTHER

02:53:49.054 --> 02:53:52.958 line:78%
PROCEEDING WHICH THE

02:53:51.090 --> 02:53:53.959 line:78%
CONSTITUTION SAYS IS ESSENTIALLY

02:53:53.058 --> 02:53:55.995 line:78%
A POLITICAL PROCEEDING FROM

02:53:54.059 --> 02:53:57.029 line:78%
WHICH THE COURT IS EXCLUDED.

02:53:56.095 --> 02:53:58.998 line:78%
AND FOR THIS COURT TO BE DRAWN

02:53:57.129 --> 02:53:59.999 line:78%
INTO THAT THICKET, IF I MAY CALL

02:53:59.098 --> 02:54:00.933 line:78%
IT THAT, SEEMS TO ME HIGHLY

02:54:00.099 --> 02:54:04.003 line:78%
INAPPROPRIATE AT LEAST AT THIS

02:54:01.033 --> 02:54:06.005 line:78%
TIME.

02:54:04.103 --> 02:54:07.039 line:78%
AS I INDICATED AT THE OUTSET,

02:54:06.105 --> 02:54:10.042 line:78%
THE HOUSE COMMITTEE HAS MADE

02:54:07.139 --> 02:54:11.010 line:78%
CERTAIN POLITICAL DECISIONS.

02:54:10.142 --> 02:54:15.047 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT HAS MADE CERTAIN

02:54:11.110 --> 02:54:16.015 line:78%
POLITICAL DECISIONS.

02:54:15.147 --> 02:54:17.049 line:78%
THEY WILL EACH HAVE TO BEAR THE

02:54:16.115 --> 02:54:17.950 line:78%
RESPONSIBILITY OF THOSE

02:54:17.149 --> 02:54:19.051 line:78%
DECISIONS WITH THE AMERICAN

02:54:18.050 --> 02:54:21.120 line:78%
PEOPLE.

02:54:19.151 --> 02:54:22.087 line:78%
THIS COURT SHOULD NOT IMPAIR,

02:54:21.220 --> 02:54:25.224 line:78%
INTERFERE WITH, OR OTHERWISE

02:54:22.188 --> 02:54:29.261 line:78%
PARTICIPATE DIRECTLY OR

02:54:25.324 --> 02:54:31.163 line:78%
INDIRECTLY IN THAT PROCEEDING.

02:54:29.361 --> 02:54:35.267 line:78%
AND, IT'S INEVITABLE IT WOULD

02:54:31.263 --> 02:54:36.268 line:78%
HAPPEN.

02:54:35.367 --> 02:54:38.237 line:78%
THIS COURTROOM WOULDN'T BE FULL

02:54:36.368 --> 02:54:39.271 line:78%
TODAY IF THIS WERE SIMPLY A SUIT

02:54:38.337 --> 02:54:40.272 line:78%
ON A SUBPOENA BROUGHT BY THE

02:54:39.371 --> 02:54:41.273 line:78%
SPECIAL PROSECUTOR AGAINST THE

02:54:40.372 --> 02:54:42.241 line:78%
PRESIDENT EVEN THOUGH THAT WOULD

02:54:41.373 --> 02:54:44.176 line:78%
BE AN IMPORTANT POLITICAL MATTER

02:54:42.341 --> 02:54:46.312 line:78%
BECAUSE THE PRESIDENT IS

02:54:44.276 --> 02:54:47.313 line:78%
INVOLVED.

02:54:46.412 --> 02:54:52.484 line:78%
BUT, THIS IS IMPORTANT FOR OTHER

02:54:47.413 --> 02:54:53.352 line:78%
REASONS QUITE APART FROM THAT.

02:54:52.585 --> 02:54:54.320 line:78%
OTHER REASONS WHICH I SUGGEST

02:54:53.452 --> 02:54:55.354 line:78%
INDICATE QUITE CLEARLY THAT THIS

02:54:54.420 --> 02:54:57.389 line:78%
COURT OUGHT TO, IN ITS

02:54:55.454 --> 02:54:59.391 line:78%
DISCRETION AND IN ITS JUDGMENT,

02:54:57.489 --> 02:55:00.392 line:78%
STAY ITS HAND AT LEAST UNTIL

02:54:59.491 --> 02:55:02.428 line:78%
SUCH TIME AS THOSE PROCEEDINGS

02:55:00.492 --> 02:55:05.464 line:78%
HAVE RUN THEIR COURSE BECAUSE

02:55:02.528 --> 02:55:06.532 line:78%
THOSE ARE POLITICAL DECISIONS

02:55:05.564 --> 02:55:08.534 line:78%
BEING MADE.

02:55:06.632 --> 02:55:10.469 line:78%
THEY SHOULD NOT BEAR THE BURDEN

02:55:08.634 --> 02:55:12.538 line:78%
EITHER WAY OF A JUDICIAL

02:55:10.569 --> 02:55:13.539 line:78%
DECISION.

02:55:12.638 --> 02:55:14.540 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, UNDER THAT THEORY, ALL

02:55:13.639 --> 02:55:16.542 line:78%
THE CRIMINAL TRIALS THAT ARE

02:55:14.640 --> 02:55:19.545 line:78%
GOING ON SHOULD STOP TODAY.

02:55:16.642 --> 02:55:22.615 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT WOULD NOT BE THE FIRST

02:55:19.645 --> 02:55:23.616 line:78%
TIME, MR. JUSTICE DOUGLAS, THAT

02:55:22.715 --> 02:55:24.617 line:78%
A CRIMINAL TRIAL WAS DELAYED.

02:55:23.716 --> 02:55:25.651 line:78%
AND IN BALANCING THE IMPORTANCE

02:55:24.717 --> 02:55:26.619 line:78%
TO THIS NATION, I WOULD SUGGEST

02:55:25.751 --> 02:55:27.620 line:78%
THAT THAT IS CLEARLY INDICATED

02:55:26.719 --> 02:55:28.621 line:78%
AND I DON'T BELIEVE THE

02:55:27.720 --> 02:55:30.689 line:78%
DEFENDANTS WOULD BE CRYING VERY

02:55:28.721 --> 02:55:33.759 line:78%
BITTER TEARS.

02:55:30.789 --> 02:55:35.728 line:78%
BUT IN ANY EVENT, THE

02:55:33.859 --> 02:55:37.763 line:78%
JUSTICIABILITY OF THIS CASE,

02:55:35.828 --> 02:55:38.764 line:78%
SEEMS TO BE, THE SINGLE

02:55:37.863 --> 02:55:39.765 line:78%
IMPORTANT OBVIOUS MATTER THAT MY

02:55:38.864 --> 02:55:40.699 line:78%
BROTHER WOULD PREFER NOT MUCH TO

02:55:39.865 --> 02:55:42.801 line:78%
TALK ABOUT, BUT THERE CAN BE NO

02:55:40.799 --> 02:55:44.803 line:78%
DOUBT ABOUT IT.

02:55:42.902 --> 02:55:46.872 line:78%
IF YOU READ PAGE 59 IN HIS

02:55:44.904 --> 02:55:47.907 line:78%
BRIEF, HE SAYS "HE, THE

02:55:46.972 --> 02:55:49.909 line:78%
PRESIDENT, IS NOW THE SUBJECT OF

02:55:48.007 --> 02:55:50.943 line:78%
AN IMPEACHMENT INQUIRY BY THE

02:55:50.009 --> 02:55:53.012 line:78%
COMMITTEE ON THE JUDICIARY OF

02:55:51.043 --> 02:55:55.014 line:78%
THE HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES AND

02:55:53.112 --> 02:55:56.015 line:78%
THE SUBPOENAED EVIDENCE MAY HAVE

02:55:55.114 --> 02:55:57.983 line:78%
A MATERIAL BEARING ON WHETHER HE

02:55:56.115 --> 02:56:00.019 line:78%
IS IMPEACHED AND, IF IMPEACHED,

02:55:58.083 --> 02:56:02.054 line:78%
WHETHER HE IS CONVICTED AND

02:56:00.119 --> 02:56:05.090 line:78%
REMOVED FROM OFFICE."

02:56:02.154 --> 02:56:08.160 line:78%
AND, I SUGGEST THE CONSTITUTION

02:56:05.190 --> 02:56:12.164 line:78%
IN ALL OF THE HISTORY, THE

02:56:08.260 --> 02:56:14.199 line:78%
FRAMERS MAKES IT QUITE CLEAR

02:56:12.264 --> 02:56:15.134 line:78%
THAT THE FRAMERS CONCEIVED

02:56:14.300 --> 02:56:16.201 line:78%
IMPEACHMENT AS A LEGISLATIVE

02:56:15.234 --> 02:56:20.272 line:78%
PROCESS.

02:56:16.302 --> 02:56:21.307 line:78%
THE COURT WAS EXCLUDED

02:56:20.372 --> 02:56:23.309 line:78%
SPECIFICALLY FROM THAT FUNCTION.

02:56:21.407 --> 02:56:27.379 line:78%
MARBURY AGAINST MADISON, ITSELF,

02:56:23.409 --> 02:56:28.347 line:78%
I AGREE WITH THE CHIEF JUSTICE

02:56:27.479 --> 02:56:29.381 line:78%
THAT IT DECIDED THE CASE IN

02:56:28.447 --> 02:56:30.349 line:78%
FAVOR OF THE PRESIDENT.

02:56:29.481 --> 02:56:31.383 line:78%
THE RULE WAS DISCHARGED AND THE

02:56:30.449 --> 02:56:33.385 line:78%
COMMISSION WAS NOT ISSUED.

02:56:31.483 --> 02:56:35.421 line:78%
BUT IT ALSO HELPS, AND IT'S BEEN

02:56:33.485 --> 02:56:36.422 line:78%
THE LAW SINCE THAT CASE, THAT

02:56:35.521 --> 02:56:38.490 line:78%
THE COURTS WILL NOT INTERFERE

02:56:36.522 --> 02:56:40.459 line:78%
WITH OR DIRECT A DISCRETIONARY

02:56:38.590 --> 02:56:43.562 line:78%
ACT ON THE PART OF THE PRESIDENT

02:56:40.559 --> 02:56:46.598 line:78%
OR ANY OTHER BRANCH OF

02:56:43.662 --> 02:56:47.599 line:78%
GOVERNMENT, AND THAT'S BEEN

02:56:46.699 --> 02:56:49.501 line:78%
CONFIRMED IN MISSISSIPPI AGAINST

02:56:47.700 --> 02:56:53.572 line:78%
JOHNSON AND ANY CASE SINCE THAT

02:56:49.601 --> 02:56:55.607 line:78%
TIME.

02:56:53.672 --> 02:56:56.575 line:78%
AND, THE DISCRETION THAT THE

02:56:55.708 --> 02:56:58.577 line:78%
CONSTITUTION BY IMPLICATION AND

02:56:56.675 --> 02:57:02.648 line:78%
BY NECESSITY THAT HAS BEEN

02:56:58.677 --> 02:57:03.682 line:78%
VESTED IN THE PRESIDENT IN

02:57:02.748 --> 02:57:04.717 line:78%
DETERMINING WHICH OF HIS

02:57:03.782 --> 02:57:05.751 line:78%
CONFIDENTIAL COMMUNICATIONS

02:57:04.817 --> 02:57:06.719 line:78%
SHALL BE MADE PUBLIC OR RELEASED

02:57:05.851 --> 02:57:07.720 line:78%
IS A DISCRETIONARY ACT THAT THIS

02:57:06.819 --> 02:57:09.722 line:78%
COURT OUGHT NOT BY ITS DECISION

02:57:07.820 --> 02:57:11.724 line:78%
TO UNDERTAKE TO DO FOR HIM

02:57:09.822 --> 02:57:12.758 line:78%
BECAUSE THIS COURT IS NOT

02:57:11.824 --> 02:57:13.759 line:78%
EQUIPPED IN KNOWLEDGE,

02:57:12.858 --> 02:57:15.761 line:78%
BACKGROUND, OR IN ANY OTHER WAY

02:57:13.859 --> 02:57:16.662 line:78%
TO EXERCISE THAT DISCRETION FOR

02:57:15.861 --> 02:57:18.797 line:78%
THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED

02:57:16.762 --> 02:57:19.798 line:78%
STATES.

02:57:18.897 --> 02:57:21.800 line:78%
THIS IS NOT A MINISTERIAL ACT.

02:57:19.898 --> 02:57:24.903 line:78%
FINALLY, I OBSERVE A SLIGHT BUT

02:57:21.900 --> 02:57:26.905 line:78%
SIGNIFICANT SHIFT IN MY

02:57:25.004 --> 02:57:29.975 line:78%
BROTHER'S POSITION WITH RESPECT

02:57:27.006 --> 02:57:31.910 line:78%
TO THE PRIMA FACIE NATURE OF

02:57:30.075 --> 02:57:35.981 line:78%
NAMING OF THE PRESIDENT AS A

02:57:32.011 --> 02:57:38.984 line:78%
CO-CONSPIRATOR.

02:57:36.081 --> 02:57:39.985 line:78%
I SAY IT CAN BE MADE NOW THAT IT

02:57:39.084 --> 02:57:42.087 line:78%
CAN BE MADE PRIMA FACIE, I TAKE

02:57:40.085 --> 02:57:44.089 line:78%
IT, THAT IS BY EXAMINING THE

02:57:42.187 --> 02:57:46.125 line:78%
EVIDENCE BEFORE THE GRAND JURY

02:57:44.189 --> 02:57:47.126 line:78%
IN ORDER TO DETERMINE WHETHER OR

02:57:46.225 --> 02:57:50.129 line:78%
NOT THAT EVIDENCE IN FACT

02:57:47.226 --> 02:57:52.131 line:78%
SUPPORTS THAT DETERMINATION.

02:57:50.229 --> 02:57:54.099 line:78%
WE HAVE INVITED THIS COURT AND

02:57:52.231 --> 02:57:56.135 line:78%
JUDGE SIRICA TO DO JUST THAT.

02:57:54.199 --> 02:57:58.137 line:78%
THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR HAS

02:57:56.235 --> 02:58:00.139 line:78%
OPPOSED IN EACH INSTANCE THIS OR

02:57:58.237 --> 02:58:02.107 line:78%
ANY OTHER COURT LOOKING BEHIND

02:58:00.239 --> 02:58:05.177 line:78%
THAT TO SEE WHETHER, IN FACT,

02:58:02.207 --> 02:58:06.211 line:78%
THE EVIDENCE CAN BE MADE AS HE

02:58:05.277 --> 02:58:11.383 line:78%
NOW STATES A POSITION TO SUPPORT

02:58:06.311 --> 02:58:13.218 line:78%
A CHARGE OF CRIMINALITY.

02:58:11.483 --> 02:58:15.220 line:78%
BEFORE THE ARGUMENT, THE

02:58:13.318 --> 02:58:16.188 line:78%
ARGUMENT WAS THAT BECAUSE IT WAS

02:58:15.320 --> 02:58:18.257 line:78%
A FINDING OR A VOTE, IT WAS

02:58:16.288 --> 02:58:20.225 line:78%
PRIMA FACIE.

02:58:18.357 --> 02:58:22.361 line:78%
NOW IT IS, I TAKE IT, SOMEWHAT

02:58:20.325 --> 02:58:25.364 line:78%
DIFFERENT.

02:58:22.461 --> 02:58:28.367 line:78%
BUT IN ANY EVENT, AN ACTION BY A

02:58:25.464 --> 02:58:30.436 line:78%
GRAND JURY PURPORTING TO ASSESS

02:58:28.467 --> 02:58:33.472 line:78%
CRIMINALITY TO A PRESIDENT OF

02:58:30.536 --> 02:58:34.506 line:78%
THE UNITED STATES IS A CLEAR

02:58:33.572 --> 02:58:36.508 line:78%
INTRUSION UPON THE LEGISLATIVE

02:58:34.606 --> 02:58:37.576 line:78%
FUNCTION AND POWER WITH RESPECT

02:58:36.608 --> 02:58:38.610 line:78%
TO IMPEACHMENT.

02:58:37.676 --> 02:58:40.579 line:78%
AS I SAID EARLIER, THE PRESIDENT

02:58:38.710 --> 02:58:43.615 line:78%
IS NOT ABOVE THE LAW NOR DOES HE

02:58:40.679 --> 02:58:44.616 line:78%
CONTEND THAT HE IS, BUT HE DOES

02:58:43.715 --> 02:58:46.652 line:78%
CONTEND THAT, AS PRESIDENT, THE

02:58:44.716 --> 02:58:49.721 line:78%
LAW CAN BE APPLIED TO HIM IN

02:58:46.752 --> 02:58:52.925 line:78%
ONLY ONE WAY AND THAT'S BY

02:58:49.822 --> 02:58:53.625 line:78%
IMPEACHMENT, NOT BY NAMING AS A

02:58:53.025 --> 02:58:54.326 line:78%
CO-CONSPIRATOR IN A GRAND JURY

02:58:53.725 --> 02:58:55.794 line:78%
INDICTMENT, NOT BY INDICTMENT,

02:58:54.426 --> 02:58:59.798 line:78%
OR ANY OTHER WAY.

02:58:55.894 --> 02:59:02.801 line:78%
THEREFORE, IN THIS CASE, I URGE

02:58:59.898 --> 02:59:05.838 line:78%
THAT THIS COURT TAKE SUCH ACTION

02:59:02.901 --> 02:59:06.839 line:78%
AS IS APPROPRIATE AND OVERRULE

02:59:05.938 --> 02:59:09.808 line:78%
JUDGE SIRICA'S DECISION AND

02:59:06.939 --> 02:59:10.909 line:78%
ORDER THAT THIS CASE BE

02:59:09.908 --> 02:59:14.012 line:78%
DISMISSED.

02:59:11.009 --> 02:59:14.746 line:78%
THANK YOU, MR. ST. CLAIR.

02:59:14.113 --> 02:59:14.980 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU, MR. JAWORSKI, MR.

02:59:14.847 --> 02:59:14.980 line:78%
LACOVARA.

